{"level":30,"time":1777030600986,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpnHrzi6DUzMMmawEakjR2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n     4→\n     5→[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    10→\n    11→A detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n    14→\n    15→**Utility Notes**\n    16→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    17→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    18→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n    19→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n    20→\n    21→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    22→\n    23→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    24→\n    25→## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n    26→\n    27→See Sht. 19\n    28→for Profile\n    29→\n    30→## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n    31→\n    32→**Tree List**\n    33→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    34→\n    35→**Note**\n    36→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n    37→\n    38→## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n    39→\n    40→**Benchmarks**\n    41→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    42→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    43→\n    44→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    45→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    46→\n    47→## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n    48→\n    49→**Legal Description**\n    50→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    51→\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"6feefca5-d9e7-4639-86a1-a74a590574b9","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n\n[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\nA detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\n## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n\nSee Sht. 19\nfor Profile\n\n## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n\n**Tree List**\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n**Note**\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777030600987,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UgXsU1pZQ2AgmzKkbc8Ezj","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 7: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n     4→\n     5→Americans with Disabilities Act\n     6→The City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n     7→\n     8→## Block 11: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n     9→\n    10→Legal Description\n    11→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 12: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n    14→\n    15→Site Plan Release Notes\n    16→1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n    17→2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n    18→3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n    19→4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n    20→5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n    21→6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n    22→8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n    23→9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n    24→10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n    25→\n    26→## Block 15: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n    27→\n    28→Fire Department\n    29→1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n    30→2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n    31→3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n    32→4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n    33→5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n    34→6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n    35→7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n    36→\n    37→## Block 18: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n    38→\n    39→Benchmarks\n    40→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    41→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    42→\n    43→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    44→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    45→\n    46→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"dd3b3a6a-757b-4c38-a7eb-0ad5ae498fba","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 7: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n\nAmericans with Disabilities Act\nThe City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 12: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n\nSite Plan Release Notes\n1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n\n## Block 15: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n\nFire Department\n1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n\n## Block 18: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777030600990,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfdJWL1xykGxA2LRBNALhx","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"c737dd96-69e5-4e6f-94b1-b6f1e9064642","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
