**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n    22→- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n    23→- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n    28→\n    29→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    30→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d291c25-51de-4c78-8a82-6fde89edc795","uuid":"86bd8739-f441-4add-b793-8d2e467c9e35","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-32/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 32 — Tree List\n\nThis page provides a detailed list of surveyed trees.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the comprehensive Tree List for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to inventory all surveyed trees on the site, detail their current condition, specify whether they will remain or be removed, and calculate the total required tree protection and tree mitigation in inches based on local codes.\n\n**Key values**:\n- Total Required Tree Protection: 672.00 inches\n- Total Removed Trees: 306.00 inches\n- Total Required Tree Mitigation: 217.00 inches\n- Total Surveyed Heritage Trees (24\" & UP): 212 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (19\" - 23.9\"): 99 inches\n- Total Surveyed ECM Appendix F Trees (8\" - 18.9\"): 295 inches\n- Tree Survey Date: 03/28/2025\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n- **Block 3: table — Tree Survey and Mitigation Table**: This is the primary data source on the sheet. READ the block content for the line-item details of every tree, including its tag number, diameter in inches, species, arborist-assessed condition, and mitigation status. Read the far-right and bottom rows for the exact calculations of required tree protection inches, removal inches, and mitigation inches categorized by tree type (Heritage, Non-Heritage, Appendix F, etc.).\n- **Block 10: text_block — Survey Note**: READ the block content to confirm the source of the foundational tree data (Sinclair Land Surveying, Inc.) and the date the survey was completed (03/28/2025).\n- **Blocks 4, 9, 11: text_blocks — Project Information**: READ for project identity, confirming the name (\"Valley View Townhomes\"), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704), and the owner entity (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC).\n- **Blocks 1, 7: various — Landscape Architect Information**: READ for the contact information and branding for the landscape architecture firm responsible for the mitigation plan, BLU FISH Collaborative. \n- **Blocks 2, 5, 6, 8, 12, 13: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**: READ for sheet metadata, including the drawing title (\"TREE LIST\"), project number (010-25-01), sheet sequence (29 of 35), and the professional seal with the issue date of 02/13/2026.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — table: Table detailing surveyed trees, required protection, removed trees, and required tree mitigation.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777030654157,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This is the Landscape Plan for Valley View Townhomes. I need to understand:\n\n1. WHERE are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? Identify all locations and describe the lines' paths across the site.\n\n2. WHERE are proposed trees shown? Identify all tree symbols and their locations relative to buildings, parking areas, and utility lines. Use the key notes from the plan (SY = Street Yard Tree, PL = Parking Lot Tree, P = Parking Buffer Point, M = Mitigation Tree).\n\n3. WHICH proposed trees (if any) are located near or potentially within restricted clearance zones from the overhead electric lines? Look for any trees that appear to be:\n   - Less than 15 feet from OHE lines\n   - Less than 25 feet from OHE lines  \n   - Within 10 feet of any utility poles\n\n4. Are the tree locations clearly shown relative to the overhead electric utility lines shown on the plan, or is the relationship unclear?\n\n5. Can you identify any specific tree symbols (circle with dot, circle with cross, circle with hash, circle with wavy edge, circle with jagged edge, etc.) and their approximate locations?\n\nPlease be very specific about locations using building references and cardinal directions (e.g., \"north side of Building 1\", \"parking lot island adjacent to Building 5\").","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35) for Valley View Townhomes, here is the specific information requested:\n\n**1. WHERE are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan?**\n*   An overhead electric line is shown running roughly east-west along the entire southern boundary of the site plan area shown.\n*   It is depicted as a solid line with periodic text reading \"-OHE-\" breaking the line.\n*   The path roughly follows the southern property line/limits of construction, running parallel to a line labeled \"SD\" (Storm Drain).\n\n**2. WHERE are proposed trees shown? (Using key notes SY, PL, P, M)**\nProposed trees are located around the perimeter and within the interior courtyards/parking areas of the development. Specific locations by designation:\n*   **SY (Street Yard Tree):** Found primarily along the western edge of the site, adjacent to the main roadway (Valley View Road). These are depicted with a wavy, cloud-like circular symbol.\n*   **M (Mitigation Tree):** Found in several locations:\n    *   A row along the northern edge of the site (plain circle symbols).\n    *   Interspersed along the western edge mixed with the SY trees (circle with a center dot symbol).\n    *   Within the interior parking/courtyard areas (circle with a center dot).\n    *   At least one located near the southeast corner along the southern boundary (jagged/spiky circle symbol).\n*   **PL (Parking Lot Tree):** Found within the interior parking area islands. One clear example is labeled \"PL\" in the north-central parking island (plain circle symbol).\n*   **P (Parking Buffer Point Tree):** No trees with this specific \"P\" label are clearly legible on this specific sheet, though many unlabeled trees exist along the eastern buffering edge.\n\n**3. WHICH proposed trees (if any) are located near or potentially within restricted clearance zones from the overhead electric lines?**\n*   There is a row of approximately 6 to 8 tree symbols planted along the southern boundary, directly adjacent to and running parallel with the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Less than 15 feet / Less than 25 feet:** Based on the provided graphic scale (1\" = 20'-0\"), the centers of these tree symbols along the southern boundary appear to be situated within 5 to 10 feet of the \"-OHE-\" line. Therefore, they all appear to be less than 15 feet (and less than 25 feet) from the overhead electric lines.\n*   **Specific tagg