 tree canopy.\n5.  **Bollards/Protection:** No bollards or other physical protective measures are visible or called out around this pad.\n6.  **Notes/Callouts:** Identified solely by a blue box containing the text **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** with a leader line pointing to the rectangular symbol.\n\n**Transformer Pad 2 (West-Central area, near Bldg. 2)**\n1.  **Location:** Located on the west side of Bldg. 2.\n2.  **Mounting:** Appears to be pad-mounted (rectangular symbol, labeled \"Pad\").\n3.  **Dimensions/Clearances:** No dimensions or clearances are shown.\n4.  **Proximity:** Situated in a narrow strip between the western exterior wall of Bldg. 2 (near Unit 201) and the property line/Sidewalk Easement. It is very close to the building facade and is underneath a drawn tree canopy.\n5.  **Bollards/Protection:** No bollards or protective measures are visible.\n6.  **Notes/Callouts:** Identified by the text **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** with a leader line pointing to the symbol.\n\n**Transformer Pad 3 (Southwest area, near Bldg. 8)**\n1.  **Location:** Located on the west side of Bldg. 8.\n2.  **Mounting:** Appears to be pad-mounted (rectangular symbol, labeled \"Pad\").\n3.  **Dimensions/Clearances:** No dimensions or clearances are shown.\n4.  **Proximity:** Located between the western exterior wall of Bldg. 8 (near Unit 801) and the property line/Sidewalk Easement. It is positioned very close to the building and sits underneath a drawn tree canopy.\n5.  **Bollards/Protection:** No bollards or protective measures are visible.\n6.  **Notes/Callouts:** Identified by the text **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** with a leader line pointing to the symbol.\n\n**Transformer Pad 4 (East-Central area, near Bldg. 4 and 5)**\n1.  **Location:** Located in the central portion of the site, on the east side of Bldg. 4 and south side of Bldg. 5.\n2.  **Mounting:** Appears to be pad-mounted (rectangular symbol, labeled \"Pad\").\n3.  **Dimensions/Clearances:** No dimensions or clearances are shown.\n4.  **Proximity:** This pad is located immediately adjacent to the curb of the central parking/drive aisle. It is situated near the corners of Bldg. 4 (Unit 404) and Bldg. 5 (Unit 504) and sits underneath a drawn tree canopy.\n5.  **Bollards/Protection:** Despite its proximity to a vehicular drive aisle, no bollards or physical barriers are drawn around it.\n6.  **Notes/Callouts:** Identified by the text **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** with a leader line pointing to the symbol.\n\n**Transformer Pad 5 (Southeast area, near Bldg. 6 and 7)**\n1.  **Location:** Located in the central-eastern portion of the site, positioned between the east side of Bldg. 7 and the north side of Bldg. 6.\n2.  **Mounting:** Appears to be pad-mounted (rectangular symbol, labeled \"Pad\").\n3.  **Dimensions/Clearances:** No dimensions or clearances are shown.\n4.  **Proximity:** Located adjacent to the curb of the central drive aisle, nestled in the open space between Bldg. 7 (near Unit 704) and Bldg. 6 (near Unit 602). It is underneath a drawn tree canopy.\n5.  **Bollards/Protection:** Despite its proximity to a vehicular drive aisle, no bollards or physical barriers are drawn around it.\n6.  **Notes/Callouts:** Identified by the text **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** with a leader line pointing to the symbol.\n\n---\n\n### Other Electrical Infrastructure Identified\n\nThe plan details an extensive electrical network connecting to these transformers. All electrical routing and callouts are marked in blue ink.\n\n**Underground Routing:**\n*   A thick blue line traverses the site, identified by a callout box pointing to it that reads **\"Underground Electric Line\"** (located on the middle-left side of the plan, entering from the street).\n*   This underground line creates a primary loop through the center of the development (running between the rows of buildings) and branches off to service the perimeter features. It directly connects all transformer pads and pull boxes.\n\n**Electrical Pull Boxes:**\nThere are eight locations explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**. These appear to serve as junction or routing points along the underground line:\n1.  Northwest property corner, north of Bldg. 1.\n2.  North side, between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 3.\n3.  North side, between Bldg. 3 and Bldg. 5.\n4.  Center of site, between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 4.\n5.  Southwest area, just south of Bldg. 8.\n6.  South side, between Bldg. 8 and Bldg. 7.\n7.  Southeast area, south of Bldg. 7 near the drive aisle.\n8.  East property edge, east of Bldg. 6.\n\n**Electrical Meters:**\nBanks of meters are shown attached to the exterior walls of the buildings, connected to the underground system. They are identified by callouts reading **\"Electrical Meters\"**:\n*   North face of Bldg. 1.\n*   North face of Bldg. 3.\n*   East face of Bldg. 5.\n*   West face of Bldg. 2 (between Units 201/202).\n*   West face of Bldg. 8 (between Units 801/802). *Note: There is also a callout pointing to a dashed rectangular area near these meters on Bldg 8 labeled **\"Vault Easement\"**.*\n*   South face of Bldg. 7.\n*   East face of Bldg. 6.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1445,"outputTokens":1539,"totalTokens":4958,"reasoningTokens":1974},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requiremen