{"level":30,"time":1777030849170,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Qe5tnHkC3eumktaB5YEHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The measurements show:\n- West transformer to Building 1: 13.7 feet (PASS - exceeds 5 feet)\n- West transformer to Building 2: 21 feet (PASS)\n- East transformer to Building 4: 22.2 feet (PASS)\n- South transformer to Building 7: 5.9 feet (PASS - exceeds 5 feet by just 0.9 feet)\n- South transformer to Building 6: 67.6 feet (PASS)\n\nSo all transformer pads meet the minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings (EL-13.1).\n\nHowever, the confidence levels are MEDIUM on all these measurements. Given the 1\" = 20' scale and the relatively tight tolerance (5.9 feet vs 5 feet required), I should note this in my findings.\n\nNow I need to verify other critical clearances:\n1. Whether transformer pads have any dimension/specification labels (EL-13.37)\n2. Fire lane clearance (EL-13.19)\n3. Underground utilities (EL-13.21-26)\n4. Property location (EL-13.33)\n5. Easement placement (EL-13.34)\n6. Transformer easements (EL-13.35)\n7. Electrical routing to meters (EL-13.36)\n8. Any trees within clearance zones\n\nLet me look at more details to see if transformer pad specifications are shown on detail sheets. Let me check the construction details to see if there's an AE-approved transformer pad detail.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3228,"cache_read_input_tokens":55231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3228,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d291c25-51de-4c78-8a82-6fde89edc795","uuid":"1ff51fa3-8692-4756-af6e-59981476