{"level":30,"time":1777030849174,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Identify and describe the locations of all overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L. as defined in the legend) and utility poles visible on this existing conditions survey. Note which edges of the property they are on, whether they are on the subject site or on adjacent properties, and approximately where they cross or run along the property. Also note if any poles appear to be positioned near existing or proposed building areas that might need clearance verification.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey, here are the locations and descriptions of the overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) and utility poles visible on the document.\n\n*Note: In accordance with the drawing's legend, overhead utility lines are identified by dashed lines interspersed with \"--- OH ---\", and utility poles are identified by a symbol consisting of a circle with an 'X' or cross inside it.*\n\n### 1. Western Boundary (Valley View Road)\n*   **Overhead Lines:** An overhead utility line (marked \"--- OH ---\") runs parallel to the western property boundary along \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". This line appears to be located entirely **off-site** within the public right-of-way.\n*   **Utility Poles:** A utility pole symbol is visible in the right-of-way, **off-site**, located just north of the existing driveway entrance near the property boundary segment labeled \"N28°04'28\"E 93.20'\".\n*   **Crossings:** There are no overhead lines depicted crossing over the western property boundary onto the subject site.\n\n### 2. Northern Boundary (Adjacent to \"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\")\n*   **Overhead Lines:** An overhead utility line runs roughly parallel to the northern property boundary (labeled \"S63°02'28\"E 419.86'\"). Unlike the wes