{"level":30,"time":1777030849175,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing and identify: 1) Are there any overhead electric poles or lines shown? 2) Are there any electric easements depicted? 3) What utility lines are shown and their locations? 4) Are there any clearance dimensions shown related to electric facilities? 5) Where is the proposed electrical infrastructure (underground lines, transformers, meters)?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan image, here are the findings regarding your specific questions about electrical and utility infrastructure:\n\n**1) Are there any overhead electric poles or lines shown?**\nYes. Overhead electric lines are depicted on the plan using a dashed line type with the label **\"- OHE -\"**. These lines run along the perimeters of the site:\n*   Along the Southern property boundary.\n*   Along the Northern property boundary.\n*   Along the Eastern property boundary (where it is also specifically labeled nearby as \"Existing Overhead Electric Line\").\nThere are also circular symbols indicating utility poles along these lines, particularly visible at the property corners.\n\n**2) Are there any electric easements depicted?**\nYes, there are explicit electric easements shown:\n*   On the central-eastern boundary, there is a dashed boundary line indicating an easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"**.\n*   In the bottom right (Southeast) corner of the property line, there is an easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5068, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**.\n*   Additionally, near the top right (Northeast), there is a **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) which typically includes electric infrastructure.\n\n**3) What utility lines are shown and their locations?**\nThe following utility lines are depicted on the site plan:\n*   **Water (\"- W -\"):** A solid line labeled \"W\" enters the site from the main road on the West, branches, and loops through the central driveways of the development to service the buildings.\n*   **Wastewater / Sanitary Sewer (\"- S -\"):** A line labeled \"S\" runs generally East-to-West through the center of the site (between the northern and southern rows of buildings). It exits the site at the Northwest corner, where it is labeled **\"Wastewater Service Connection\"**.\n*   **Storm Drainage (\"- SD -\"):** Lines labeled \"SD\" are visible primarily on the Eastern half of the site, capturing runoff and directing it toward the **\"Detention Pond\"** located in the Northeast corner.\n*   **Overhead Electric (\"- OHE -\"):** As noted above, running along the North, East, and South perimeters.\n*   **Gas (\"- G -\"):** A line labeled \"G\" is visible running North-South within the right-of-way of the main road on the far West side, outside the main property boundary.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance dimensions shown related to electric facilities?**\nNo. Based on the visual evidence on this specific sheet, there are no dimension lines or textual callouts indicating required clearance distances (e.g., building setback from OHE lines, or clear workspace zones around the transformer).\n\n**5) Where is the proposed electrical infrastructure (underground lines, transformers, meters)?**\n*   **Transformers:** There is one proposed transformer location shown. It is located on the Western side of the site, situated between the northernmost entrance driveway and Building 1. It is indicated by a square box and labeled exactly as **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"**.\n*   **Meters:** There are no distinct electrical meter banks or individual electric meters explicitly drawn or labeled on the building footprints on this sheet.\n*   **Underground Lines:** The specific routing of proposed underground electrical lines (such as the primary feed from the OHE to the transformer, or the secondary feeds from the transformer to the buildings) is not depicted with explicit line types on this drawing.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1387,"outputTokens":800,"totalTokens":4667,"reasoningTokens":2480},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan drawing and identify: 1) Are there any overhead electric poles or lines shown? 2) Are there any electric easements depicted? 3) What utility lines are shown and their locations? 4) Are there any cleara