{"level":30,"time":1777030849175,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Analyze the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC FACILITIES: Identify and describe any overhead electric distribution or transmission lines, conductors, poles, and their locations on the site. Note voltage levels if shown.\n\n2. UNDERGROUND ELECTRIC EQUIPMENT: Identify locations of transformers, pull boxes, pad-mounted equipment, vaults, or other underground electrical infrastructure. Note any labels or designations.\n\n3. UTILITY ROUTING: Describe how electrical lines are routed through the site (above or below ground). Note any easement locations.\n\n4. MEASUREMENTS/DIMENSIONS: Are there any dimension lines showing distances from electrical infrastructure to other site features?\n\n5. TREE REFERENCES: Does the electrical plan show or reference the location of trees in relation to electrical facilities?\n\n6. OVERALL LAYOUT: Describe the general positioning of electrical infrastructure relative to the 8 buildings shown on the plan.\n\nPlease focus on spatial relationships and locations that would be relevant to assessing tree clearances from electrical facilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21), here is detailed information regarding the electrical infrastructure and its spatial relationships on the site:\n\n**1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC FACILITIES**\n\n*   **Locations:** Overhead electric lines are indicated by dashed lines accompanied by the label \"**OHE**\". These are located along the perimeter of the site:\n    *   Running vertically along the western property line boundary/street frontage.\n    *   Running horizontally along the southern property line boundary/street frontage.\n*   **Poles:** Small circular symbols appear at intervals along the \"OHE\" lines, which typically represent utility poles, though they are not explicitly labeled with text as \"poles\".\n*   **Conductors & Voltage:** There are no text labels indicating the number of conductors, type of wire, or voltage levels for these overhead lines on this specific sheet.\n\n**2. UNDERGROUND ELECTRIC EQUIPMENT**\n\nUnderground infrastructure is denoted by solid blue lines marked with an \"E\" and specific equipment boxes.\n*   **Labels & Designations:** The main blue routing line is explicitly labeled as \"**Underground Electric Line**\" near the western edge.\n*   **Equipment Locations:**\n    *   **Transformers:** Labeled exactly as \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\". Four are visible:\n        1.  West of Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 2.\n        2.  East of Bldg. 4.\n        3.  Southwest of Bldg. 8.\n        4.  Southeast of Bldg. 6.\n    *   **Pull Boxes:** Labeled exactly as \"**Electrical Pull Box**\". These are frequently located adjacent to transformer pads and at junction points along the main line. Locations include: Next to all four transformer pads, in the northeast drive aisle near Bldg. 3, east of Bldg. 7, and near the southern property line connecting to the overhead system.\n    *   **Meters:** Labeled exactly as \"**Electrical Meters**\". These are shown pointing to locations on the exterior walls of the buildings.\n\n**3. UTILITY ROUTING**\n\n*   **Above Ground:** Routed around the west and south perimeters (labeled \"OHE\").\n*   **Below Ground:** The internal distribution is entirely underground (blue lines). The underground system appears to tap into the perimeter overhead lines at three primary locations: on the west side (near the Bldg. 1 transformer), on the south side (middle, via a pull box), and near the southeast corner (near the Bldg. 6 transformer).\n*   **Easements:** Dashed lines parallel to the western and southern property lines are labeled \"**10' P.U.E.**\" (Public Utility Easement), where the overhead lines and initial underground connections are located.\n\n**4. MEASUREMENTS/DIMENSIONS**\n\n*   **No Explicit Dimensions:** While the drawing includes a scale bar (\"Scale 1\" = 20'\"), there are **no written dimension lines** explicitly showing the distance (e.g., \"15 ft\") between electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, or underground lines) and other site features like buildings, curbs, or trees.\n\n**5. TREE REFERENCES**\n\n*   **Visual Representation:** Trees are prominently shown as large circular graphics with scalloped edges indicating canopy spread. Extensive existing tree coverage is shown along the north, west, and south property boundaries, as well as a large cluster in the north-central area of the site.\n*   **Text Reference:** A box in the lower middle of the plan states: \"**Tree List: Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.**\"\n*   **Spatial Relationship to Electrical:**\n    *   *Underground:* The blue \"Underground Electric Line\" routing appears designed to weave through the site, generally staying within paved drive aisles and specifically appearing to route *around* the root zones of the central tree cluster.\n    *   *Overhead:* The \"OHE\" lines on the western and southern boundaries appear to intersect directly with the drawn canopies of numerous existing perimeter trees.\n\n**6. OVERALL LAYOUT**\n\nThe electrical design utilizes a perimeter overhead supply that feeds into an internal underground distribution network. Instead of a single central hub, the site uses a distributed node system. There are four main \"Electrical Transformer Pads\" placed strategically around the exterior of the central building blocks (serving roughly two buildings per pad). The main underground line loops through the central drive aisles to connect these four transformer nodes, from which secondary lines run to the individual \"Electrical Meters\" on the buildings. The internal underground routing largely avoids the footprints of the indicated central existing trees.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1522,"outputTokens":969,"totalTokens":4642,"reasoningTokens":2151},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Analyze the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC FACILITIES: Identify and describe any overhead electric distribution or transmission lines, conductors, poles, and their locations on the site. Note voltage levels if shown.\n\n2. UNDERGROUND ELECTRIC EQUIPMENT: Identify locations of tra