as \"**Electrical Meters**\". These are shown pointing to locations on the exterior walls of the buildings.\n\n**3. UTILITY ROUTING**\n\n*   **Above Ground:** Routed around the west and south perimeters (labeled \"OHE\").\n*   **Below Ground:** The internal distribution is entirely underground (blue lines). The underground system appears to tap into the perimeter overhead lines at three primary locations: on the west side (near the Bldg. 1 transformer), on the south side (middle, via a pull box), and near the southeast corner (near the Bldg. 6 transformer).\n*   **Easements:** Dashed lines parallel to the western and southern property lines are labeled \"**10' P.U.E.**\" (Public Utility Easement), where the overhead lines and initial underground connections are located.\n\n**4. MEASUREMENTS/DIMENSIONS**\n\n*   **No Explicit Dimensions:** While the drawing includes a scale bar (\"Scale 1\" = 20'\"), there are **no written dimension lines** explicitly showing the distance (e.g., \"15 ft\") between electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes, or underground lines) and other site features like buildings, curbs, or trees.\n\n**5. TREE REFERENCES**\n\n*   **Visual Representation:** Trees are prominently shown as large circular graphics with scalloped edges indicating canopy spread. Extensive existing tree coverage is shown along the north, west, and south property boundaries, as well as a large cluster in the north-central area of the site.\n*   **Text Reference:** A box in the lower middle of the plan states: \"**Tree List: Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.**\"\n*   **Spatial Relationship to Electrical:**\n    *   *Underground:* The blue \"Underground Electric Line\" routing appears designed to weave through the site, generally staying within paved drive aisles and specifically appearing to route *around* the root zones of the central tree cluster.\n    *   *Overhead:* The \"OHE\" lines on the western and southern boundaries appear to intersect directly with the drawn canopies of numerous existing perimeter trees.\n\n**6. OVERALL LAYOUT**\n\nThe electrical design utilizes a perimeter overhead supply that feeds into an internal underground distribution network. Instead of a single central hub, the site uses a distributed node system. There are four main \"Electrical Transformer Pads\" placed strategically around the exterior of the central building blocks (serving roughly two buildings per pad). The main underground line loops through the central drive aisles to connect these four transformer nodes, from which secondary lines run to the individual \"Electrical Meters\" on the buildings. The internal underground routing largely avoids the footprints of the indicated central existing trees.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":3425809.42809,"endTime":3481532.016524,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"41XraZTbMKKLl7oP8o3REQ"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.040484","marketCost":"0.040484","inferenceCost":"0.040484","inputInferenceCost":"0.003044","outputInferenceCost":"0.03744","generationId":"gen_01KPZMF081B4Y5TCTKZVDTAF6W"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1777030849183,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"This is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes. I need to understand the electrical infrastructure:\n\n1. WHERE are transformers/transformer pads shown on this plan? Describe their locations by building reference and identify how many there are.\n\n2. WHERE are utility poles shown? Are they explicitly marked, or can they be inferred from the overhead electric line routing?\n\n3. WHERE are underground electrical equipment locations shown (pull boxes, vaults, or equipment)? Describe their locations.\n\n4. Are there any pad-mounted transformers shown, and if so, where are they located relative to buildings and the site perimeter?\n\n5. Can you identify the overall routing/path of the electrical distribution system on the site?\n\n6. Are there dimensions or clearance notes shown for any electrical equipment relative to buildings or proposed structures?\n\nPlease be specific about locations using building references (Bldg 1-8) and cardinal directions (e.g., \"northeast corner\", \"south side\").","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here is the information regarding the electrical infrastructure:\n\n**1. WHERE are transformers/transformer pads shown on this plan?**\nThere are four (4) locations explicitly labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**:\n*   **Northwest Area:** Located west of **Bldg. 1**, between the building and the western property boundary.\n*   **Southwest Area:** Located west of **Bldg. 8**, near the southwest corner of the site.\n*   **Central-East Area:** Located between the east side of **Bldg. 4** and the west side of **Bldg. 5**.\n*   **South-Central Area:** Located between **Bldg. 6** and **Bldg. 7**.\n\n**2. WHERE are utility poles shown?**\nUtility poles are not explicitly labeled with text (e.g., \"Utility Pole\"). However, their locations can be inferred from the overhead electric line routing, marked by dashed lines with **\"OHE\"** labels. These lines run along the outside of the western property boundary (parallel to the road) and along the southern property boundary. Small circular symbols on these lines, particularly where the underground electrical lines tap off (e.g., west of Bldg. 2 and southwest of Bldg. 8), likely indicate pole locations.\n\n**3. WHERE are underground electrical equipment locations shown (pull boxes, vaults, or equipment)?**\n*   **Pull Boxes:** There are several locations explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**, generally found along the solid blue underground electrical routing lines:\n    *   West of **Bldg. 1** (near the northwest transformer pad).\n    *   West of **Bldg. 2**.\n    *   West of **Bldg. 8** (near the southwest transformer pad).\n    *   Between the north ends of **Bldg. 3** and **Bldg. 5**.\n    *   East of **Bldg. 4**.\n    *   Between **Bldg. 6** and **Bldg. 7** (near the south-central transformer pad).\n    *   South of **Bldg. 6**.\n*   **Vaults:** There is a specific label for a **\"Vault Easement\"** located west of **Bldg. 8**, pointing to a dashed rectangular area that encloses an Electrical Transformer Pad and an Electrical Pull Box.\n*   **Underground Lines:** The routing itself is marked by a solid blue line with the letter 'E' at intervals, and is explicitly labeled **\"Underground Electric Line\"** west of Bldg. 2 and centrally between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 7.\n\n**4. Are there any pad-mounted transformers shown?**\nYes. Because the explicit labels read **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**, it can be inferred that these are pad-mounted transformers. Their locations relative to buildings and perimeters are the same as listed in Question 1:\n*   Two are located near the western site perimeter (west of Bldg. 1 and west of Bldg. 8).\n*   Two are located internally between buildings (between Bldg. 4/5 and Bldg. 6/7).\n\n**5. Can you identify the overall routing/path of the electrical distribution system on the site?**\nThe distribution system originates from the overhead lines (**\"OHE\"**) on the western and southern boundaries. The underground system (represented by the solid blue line with 'E') taps into the overhead lines on the west side. It then creates a looped routing network throughout the site to connect the various equipment. It runs longitudinally down the western side (serving Bldgs 1, 2, 8), traverses eastward across the north (serving Bldgs 1, 3, 4), loops through the central and eastern portions (serving Bldgs 4, 5), and traverses the southern portion (serving Bldgs 6, 7). This blue routing line directly connects to every \"Electrical Transformer Pad\", \"Electrical Pull Box\", and the **\"Electrical Meters\"** banks shown on the sides of every building (Bldg 1-8).\n\n**6. Are there dimensions or clearance notes shown for any electrical equipment?**\nNo. While there are standard property line and building footprint dimensions shown on the plan, there are no explicit dimension lines, callouts, or text notes detailing specific clearance requirements or setback distances for the electrical equipment relative to the buildings or proposed structures on this specific sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1511,"outputTokens":959,"totalTokens":4651,"reasoningTokens":2181},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-b