{"level":30,"time":1777030849186,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) and identify: 1) All electrical infrastructure shown including transformers, pad-mounted equipment, poles, underground conduits, and pull boxes with their approximate locations on the site plan; 2) Whether overhead or underground electric lines are shown and if so where; 3) Any notation about the type of electrical service (distribution vs transmission); 4) The scale of the drawing (should be 1\" = 20'); 5) Any reference to conductors or overhead lines. Please be specific about locations (e.g., \"northeast corner near Building 1\").","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Sheet 21, \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the detailed analysis of the electrical infrastructure and related elements as requested:\n\n**1) Electrical Infrastructure Shown and Approximate Locations:**\nThe site plan details an extensive electrical network using solid blue lines to represent routing, connecting various labeled components.\n*   **Transformers:** Labeled as `\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"`. There are four identified on the site:\n    *   West of Building 2 (near the western boundary).\n    *   West of Building 8 (near the western boundary).\n    *   East of Building 4 (in the central-eastern area).\n    *   East of Building 7 (between Building 7 and Building 6).\n*   **Pull Boxes:** Labeled as `\"Electrical Pull Box\"`. These are denoted by small blue circles with an \"E\" inside. Locations include:\n    *   Northwest of Building 1.\n    *   West of Building 2 (adjacent to the transformer pad).\n    *   West of Building 8 (adjacent to the transformer pad).\n    *   East of Building 3.\n    *   East of Building 4 (adjacent to the transformer pad).\n    *   East of Building 7 (adjacent to the transformer pad).\n    *   South of Building 7 (near the southern boundary).\n    *   East of Building 6 (near the eastern boundary).\n*   **Meters:** Labeled as `\"Electrical Meters\"`. Locations include:\n    *   North side of Building 1.\n    *   North side of Building 3.\n    *   West side of Building 2.\n    *   West side of Building 8.\n    *   East side of Building 4.\n    *   East side of Building 7.\n    *   East side of Building 6.\n*   **Underground Conduits:** The solid blue lines routing through the interior of the development connecting the pull boxes, transformers, and meters represent the underground conduit network. A specific callout box on the western boundary points to a line entering the site labeled explicitly as `\"Underground Electric Line\"`.\n*   **Poles:** There are no explicit labels or callouts for electrical poles on this sheet. \n\n**2) Overhead vs. Underground Electric Lines:**\n*   **Underground Lines:** Yes, they are shown. The entire interior network servicing the buildings is underground, explicitly indicated by a callout box reading `\"Underground Electric Line\"` on the western edge of the property where the service enters the site.\n*   **Overhead Lines:** Yes, they are shown along the exterior perimeter. Line types designated with ` - OHE - ` run outside the property line along the western (left) and southern (bottom) boundaries of the plan.\n\n**3) Notation About the Type of Electrical Service:**\nThere is no text or notation explicitly stating the type of electrical service (e.g., \"distribution\" or \"transmission\") on this sheet.\n\n**4) Scale of the Drawing:**\nIn the top right corner, there is a graphic scale with the exact text: `\"Scale 1\" = 20'\"`. \n\n**5) Reference to Conductors or Overhead Lines:**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** The drawing references overhead lines primarily through the line type labels ` - OHE - ` located along the western and southern boundaries. There is also a small label pointing to a line on the far west edge that reads `\"Existing Overhead Electric Line\"` (though slightly cut off, the intent is visible).\n*   **Conductors:** There is no explicit text or reference using the word \"conductors\" anywhere on this sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1439,"outputTokens":768,"totalTokens":5303,"reasoningTokens":3096},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design Plan) and identify: 1) All electrical infrastructure shown including transformers, pad-mounted equipment, poles, underground conduits, and pull boxes