{"level":30,"time":1777030849190,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKwy1qp4vLXaP28EmKcU4V","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey, here are the locations and descriptions of the overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) and utility poles visible on the document.\n\n*Note: In accordance with the drawing's legend, overhead utility lines are identified by dashed lines interspersed with \"--- OH ---\", and utility poles are identified by a symbol consisting of a circle with an 'X' or cross inside it.*\n\n### 1. Western Boundary (Valley View Road)\n*   **Overhead Lines:** An overhead utility line (marked \"--- OH ---\") runs parallel to the western property boundary along \"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\". This line appears to be located entirely **off-site** within the public right-of-way.\n*   **Utility Poles:** A utility pole symbol is visible in the right-of-way, **off-site**, located just north of the existing driveway entrance near the property boundary segment labeled \"N28°04'28\"E 93.20'\".\n*   **Crossings:** There are no overhead lines depicted crossing over the western property boundary onto the subject site.\n\n### 2. Northern Boundary (Adjacent to \"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\")\n*   **Overhead Lines:** An overhead utility line runs roughly parallel to the northern property boundary (labeled \"S63°02'28\"E 419.86'\"). Unlike the western side, this line appears to be located **on-site**, running just inside the subject property line for most of its length.\n*   **Utility Poles:** There is one clearly visible utility pole located **on-site** along this northern boundary. It is positioned near the midpoint of the boundary line, adjacent to a tree symbol with the tag \"+4028\".\n\n### 3. Eastern Boundary (Adjacent to \"CLAWSON RIDGE CONDOMINIUMS\")\n*   **Overhead Lines:** The overhead line from the northern boundary appears to turn south and run along or very close to the eastern property boundary (labeled \"S27°19'28\"W 146.15'\").\n*   **Utility Poles:** Near the southeast corner of the property, there is a utility pole symbol located **off-site** on the adjacent property (near the boundary segment labeled \"S26°15'01\"W 80.67'\"). Overhead lines connect to this pole from the north and from the west.\n\n### 4. Southern Boundary (Adjacent to \"WILLIAM LANCE CORSBIE, JR.\")\n*   **Overhead Lines:** An overhead utility line runs parallel to the southern property boundary (labeled \"N63°50'57\"W 414.24'\"). This line appears to be located entirely **off-site** on the adjacent property to the south, connecting to the off-site pole mentioned at the southeast corner and running westward towards Valley View Road.\n*   **Utility Poles:** No distinct utility poles are drawn along this southern run other than the one at the southeast corner.\n\n### Clearance Verification Notes\n*   **Northern Area:** The most critical area requiring clearance verification is along the **northern property boundary**. The overhead line and the specific utility pole located **on-site** in this area are positioned in relatively close proximity to the northern edge of the existing building structure (labeled \"SLAB F.F.E.=686.8'\"). Any proposed modifications, expansions, or vertical construction near the northern edge of this existing slab will need to verify clearance from these active on-site overhead utilities.\n*   There are no overhead lines depicted crossing directly over the main footprint of the existing central \"SLAB\"."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef672522-d4e7-4b95-adea-0f34cf5c6c5b","uuid":"23efa282-d50e-4fc3-b92d-d91983d91d44","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided existing conditions survey, here are the locations and descriptions of the overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) and uti