{"level":30,"time":1777030852569,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Cmvt9rMMRMGRaqJozuLqja","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! This is very helpful. Key findings from the electrical plan:\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure (OHE):**\n- Located along western and southern property line boundaries (street frontages)\n- Poles shown as small circles at intervals\n- 10' Public Utility Easement (P.U.E.) along west and south boundaries\n\n**Underground Electric Equipment:**\n- 4 Electrical Transformer Pads\n- Multiple Electrical Pull Boxes\n- Electrical Meters on building exteriors\n- Blue lines showing underground electric lines routing through the site\n\n**Trees and Electrical Relationship:**\n- Existing trees shown along north, west, and south boundaries\n- Overhead lines at the west and south perimeters appear to intersect with canopies of perimeter trees\n- Underground routing appears to avoid central tree clusters but... I need to check if the PROPOSED trees are located near any electrical infrastructure\n\nNow let me check the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) to see where PROPOSED trees are being planted in relation to electrical infrastructure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1975,"cache_read_input_tokens":56041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1975,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88e5e1a0-af42-4247-99ef-1088ed9cc7e1","uuid":"6f58f9a2-0a9a-4d38-9890-e7c0ce6b1867"}
{"level":30,"time":1777030852669,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JgZ7M7DP49iJMAQzcg7L23","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The vision analysis of Sheet 4 confirms:\n\n1. **Western boundary (Valley View Road):** Overhead utility line in ROW off-site, plus a utility pole off-site\n2. **Northern boundary:** An overhead utility line appears to be on-site along the northern property boundary, plus a utility pole on-site near the midpoint\n3. **Eastern boundary:** Overhead line along or near eastern boundary\n4. **Southern boundary:** Overhead line off-site on adjacent property\n\nSo there ARE overhead facilities both on and adjacent to the site, particularly along the northern boundary which appears to be on-site. This means the EL-MD-EXP grouping IS APPLICABLE to this project.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check if the Site Plan (Sheet 9) shows these overhead utilities and whether proposed improvements maintain clearances\n2. Check the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) for tree plantings near overhead utilities\n3. Check for any building elevations that might show vertical clearances\n4. Look for any clearance dimensions or notes\n\nLet me examine the site plan (Sheet 9) blocks to see if overhead utilities are shown there.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":49017,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef672522-d4e7-4b95-adea-0f34cf5c6c5b","uuid":"9bd4bf74-2240-414f-b9ee-714aa7d0d7d6"}
