begins, there are large, faint circular lines indicating tree canopies that visually overlap the area where the OHE line is drawn.\n\n**4) Are there any clearance annotations for trees relative to overhead lines?**\n*   **No**, there are no clearance annotations present on this document.\n*   A review of the drawn elements near the OHE line reveals no dimensional lines or callouts specifying required distances from the wires.\n*   A complete review of the text blocks provided on the page—including **\"IRRIGATION NOTES:\"**, the general **\"NOTE:\"** section, and **\"KEY NOTES:\"**—shows no mention of overhead electric lines, power line clearances, or planting restrictions related to utilities.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1390,"outputTokens":453,"totalTokens":3768,"reasoningTokens":1925},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for a