ents near the OHE line reveals no dimensional lines or callouts specifying required distances from the wires.\n*   A complete review of the text blocks provided on the page—including **\"IRRIGATION NOTES:\"**, the general **\"NOTE:\"** section, and **\"KEY NOTES:\"**—shows no mention of overhead electric lines, power line clearances, or planting restrictions related to utilities."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"2452db45-52af-4cdd-94ad-19eee192e1d0","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan, here are the findings corresponding to your specific questions:\n\n**1) Are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown? If yes, where and in what form?**\n*   **Yes**, overhead electric lines are shown on the plan.\n*   **Location:** They run horizontally along the bottom (Southern) boundary line of the site plan drawing.\n*   **Form:** The utility is represented by a solid black line that is periodically broken by the text notation **\"-OHE-\"**.\n\n**2) Are any trees planted near or under overhead electric lines?**\n*   **Yes**, there are proposed tree plantings located in close proximity to the line marked \"-OHE-\".\n\n**3) What is the location of proposed trees relative to any utilities marked as \"OHE\"?**\n*   **Bottom Right Area:** Near the bottom right corner of the property boundary, there is a cluster of proposed trees located immediately adjacent to (just North/above) the \"-OHE-\" line. While the root ball symbols (the smaller circles with internal markings like a '+' or 'x', one of which has a leader pointing to the letter **\"M\"**) are planted just inside the property line above the OHE line, the larger outer circles representing the expected tree canopy spread visually intersect and overlap the \"-OHE-\" line on the drawing.\n*   **Bottom Left Area:** Near the bottom left corner where the \"-OHE-\" line begins, there are large, faint circular lines indic