{"level":30,"time":1777030888966,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine this site plan and identify:\n1. The locations of the 8 proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) relative to property lines\n2. Any overhead utility lines shown on this proposed site plan (marked as O.H.U.L. or utility poles)\n3. The locations of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks\n4. Any clearance dimensions or annotations showing distances from proposed structures to overhead utilities\n5. Whether overhead utility poles and lines are depicted, and if so, where they are positioned relative to buildings, driveways, and other site features\n6. Any utility notes or easement boundaries shown\nNote: Compare this to the existing conditions survey to understand what existing overhead infrastructure the site must accommodate.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the requested information regarding the site features, buildings, and utilities:\n\n**1. Locations of the 8 proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) relative to property lines**\nThe 8 buildings are generally clustered within the center of the parcel, constrained by access drives and setback lines:\n*   **Bldg. 1 (3,290 sf):** Located in the northwest quadrant, near the western property line (fronting the street). It is oriented horizontally.\n*   **Bldg. 2 (4,830 sf):** Located south of Bldg. 1 along the western side of the site, situated between the internal drive aisle loop. Oriented horizontally.\n*   **Bldg. 3 (4,144 sf):** Located in the north-central area, positioned parallel to the northern property line but set back behind a \"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\" and a retaining wall.\n*   **Bldg. 4 (4,144 sf):** Located centrally within the site, directly south of Bldg. 3 and east of Bldg. 2. Oriented horizontally.\n*   **Bldg. 5 (3,290 sf):** Located in the northeast quadrant. Unlike buildings 1-4, it is oriented vertically, running parallel to the eastern property line.\n*   **Bldg. 6 (3,290 sf):** Located directly south of Bldg. 5, oriented vertically and parallel to the eastern property line.\n*   **Bldg. 7 (4,144 sf):** Located in the south-central area, oriented horizontally. It is situated north of the southern property line, separated from it by a drive aisle and a 25' setback area.\n*   **Bldg. 8 (4,997 sf):** Located in the southwest quadrant, directly west of Bldg. 7. It is oriented horizontally, north of the southern property line and drive aisle.\n*   *Note on Setbacks:* A \"25' Building Setback Line\" (represented by a dashed line) runs along the perimeter of the property lines, and all buildings appear to be positioned completely within this boundary.\n\n**2. Any overhead utility lines shown on this proposed site plan (marked as O.H.U.L. or utility poles)**\n*   **Overhead Lines:** A continuous overhead utility line is explicitly drawn along the southern (bottom) property line. It is marked with the repeating line type **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric).\n*   **Utility Poles:** Utility pole symbols (circles with a cross inside) are visible at several locations along the perimeter. Notable pole locations include:\n    *   Near the northwest corner by the northernmost driveway entrance.\n    *   Along the \"- OHE -\" line on the southern property line (one near the southwest corner, one near the center-south boundary, and one near the southeast corner).\n    *   A guy wire symbol is also visible near the southwest pole.\n\n**3. Locations of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks**\n*   **Driveways:** The site is accessed via two driveway cuts on the western property line bordering the street. Both are labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 4/835-2\"**. These entrances connect to a continuous internal \"24'-0\" access drive that loops around the central buildings (Bldgs 2 and 4).\n*   **Parking Areas:** \n    *   The \"Parking Data\" table explicitly states: **\"10 Surface/ 76 Garage\"**.\n    *   Garage parking is contained within the townhome units.\n    *   The 10 surface parking spaces are distributed in small bays along the internal drive aisle: parallel spaces are located in front of Bldg. 2, and perpendicular spaces are situated near Bldg. 1, Bldg. 8, between Bldgs. 3 & 5, and in front of Bldg. 7.\n*   **Sidewalks:**\n    *   A public sidewalk runs along the street frontage on the west, labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dt. 4/335-1\"**.\n    *   Internal pathways include a **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"** running along the northern edge of Bldgs. 1 and 3.\n    *   Internal concrete sidewalks connecting buildings to drive aisles are labeled **\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ)\"**.\n\n**4. Clearance dimensions or annotations showing distances from proposed structures to overhead utilities**\n*   There are **no explicit vertical clearance dimensions** or safety buffer zones specifically labeled for the overhead utilities on this 2D plan view.\n*   There are *horizontal* dimension lines showing distances from the buildings to the property lines/easements where the OHE lines run. For example, a dimension of **\"26.8'\"** is shown between the southwest corner of Bldg. 8 and the southern property line/OHE area. Another dimension of **\"21.3'\"** is shown from the southeast corner of Bldg. 7 to the southern property line.\n\n**5. Position of utility poles and lines relative to buildings, driveways, and other site features**\n*   The primary **\"- OHE -\"** line runs strictly along the southern perimeter boundary. It is separated from Buildings 7 and 8 by the proposed internal 24'-0\" concrete drive aisle and a 25' building setback zone.\n*   The OHE line does not cross over any proposed buildings or internal drive aisles; it remains entirely on the periphery of the southern edge.\n*   The utility poles on the western street frontage are positioned between the public street and the proposed 5' concrete sidewalk, outside the main building envelope.\n\n**6. Any utility notes or easement boundaries shown**\n*   **Easement Boundaries:** Several easements are recorded and shown with dashed lines around the property edges:\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Northern boundary edge).\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Northeast corner / Eastern boundary).\n    *   **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Mid-Eastern boundary).\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5168, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Southern/Southeastern boundary).\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"** [Document number is unclear/cut off] (Western boundary near the street).\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement Doc#\"** [Document number is unclear] (Northwestern corner).\n*   **Utility Notes:**\n    *   A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is noted on the west side of Bldg. 2.\n    *   A warning graphic at the bottom right center reads: **\"Texas 811 Call Before You Dig!!\"**\n    *   The \"Site Plan Release Notes\" contain a specific utility note: **\"e. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\"**\n    *   Existing utility infrastructure is labeled near the street, including an **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**, **\"Water Meter\"**, and a **\"Wastewater Service Connection\"**.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1462,"outputTokens":1651,"totalTokens":5728,"reasoningTokens":2615},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine this site plan and identify:\n1. The locations of the 8 proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) relative to property lines\n2. Any overhead utility lines shown on this proposed site plan (marked as O.H.U.L. or utility poles)\n3. The locations of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks\n4. Any clearance dimensions or annotations showing distances from proposed structures to overhead utilities\n5. Whether overhead utility poles and lines are depicted, and if so, where they are positioned relative to buildings, driveways, and other site features\n6. Any utility notes or easement boundaries shown\nNote: Compare this to the existing conditions survey to understand what existing overhead infrastructure the site must accommodate."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-Ryu12dKraYPejjWdP85ltuId","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/