at loops around the central buildings (Bldgs 2 and 4).\n*   **Parking Areas:** \n    *   The \"Parking Data\" table explicitly states: **\"10 Surface/ 76 Garage\"**.\n    *   Garage parking is contained within the townhome units.\n    *   The 10 surface parking spaces are distributed in small bays along the internal drive aisle: parallel spaces are located in front of Bldg. 2, and perpendicular spaces are situated near Bldg. 1, Bldg. 8, between Bldgs. 3 & 5, and in front of Bldg. 7.\n*   **Sidewalks:**\n    *   A public sidewalk runs along the street frontage on the west, labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dt. 4/335-1\"**.\n    *   Internal pathways include a **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"** running along the northern edge of Bldgs. 1 and 3.\n    *   Internal concrete sidewalks connecting buildings to drive aisles are labeled **\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ)\"**.\n\n**4. Clearance dimensions or annotations showing distances from proposed structures to overhead utilities**\n*   There are **no explicit vertical clearance dimensions** or safety buffer zones specifically labeled for the overhead utilities on this 2D plan view.\n*   There are *horizontal* dimension lines showing distances from the buildings to the property lines/easements where the OHE lines run. For example, a dimension of **\"26.8'\"** is shown between the southwest corner of Bldg. 8 and the southern property line/OHE area. Another dimension of **\"21.3'\"** is shown from the southeast corner of Bldg. 7 to the southern property line.\n\n**5. Position of utility poles and lines relative to buildings, driveways, and other site features**\n*   The primary **\"- OHE -\"** line runs strictly along the southern perimeter boundary. It is separated from Buildings 7 and 8 by the proposed internal 24'-0\" concrete drive aisle and a 25' building setback zone.\n*   The OHE line does not cross over any proposed buildings or internal drive aisles; it remains entirely on the periphery of the southern edge.\n*   The utility poles on the western street frontage are positioned between the public street and the proposed 5' concrete sidewalk, outside the main building envelope.\n\n**6. Any utility notes or easement boundaries shown**\n*   **Easement Boundaries:** Several easements are recorded and shown with dashed lines around the property edges:\n    *   **\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Northern boundary edge).\n    *   **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Northeast corner / Eastern boundary).\n    *   **\"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Mid-Eastern boundary).\n    *   **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5168, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx\"** (Southern/Southeastern boundary).\n    *   **\"Sidewalk Easement Doc#\"** [Document number is unclear/cut off] (Western boundary near the street).\n    *   **\"Wastewater Easement Doc#\"** [Document number is unclear] (Northwestern corner).\n*   **Utility Notes:**\n    *   A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is noted on the west side of Bldg. 2.\n    *   A warning graphic at the bottom right center reads: **\"Texas 811 Call Before You Dig!!\"**\n    *   The \"Site Plan Release Notes\" contain a specific utility note: **\"e. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\"**\n    *   Existing utility infrastructure is labeled near the street, including an **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**, **\"Water Meter\"**, and a **\"Wastewater Service Connection\"**."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1777030889625,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Analyze the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. PROPOSED TREES: Identify all proposed trees shown on the plan. Note their locations (by building, parking area, or site zone), their symbols (if any), and whether they are shade trees, ornamental trees, or mitigation trees. Describe their spatial distribution around the site.\n\n2. ELECTRICAL INFRASTRUCTURE SHOWN: Identify all electrical utility facilities shown on the landscape plan (overhead lines, poles, transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground lines). Note how they are depicted (symbols, labels, line styles).\n\n3. TREE-TO-ELECTRICAL PROXIMITY: For each proposed tree, assess its spatial relationship to nearby electrical infrastructure. Are trees shown near or adjacent to:\n   - Overhead electric distribution lines (OHE)?\n   - Electrical transformer pads?\n   - Electrical pull boxes?\n   - Overhead utility poles?\n   - Underground electric lines?\n\n4. BUILDING PROXIMITY: Describe the locations of proposed trees relative to the 8 buildings and parking areas.\n\n5. SCALE AND DIMENSIONS: Note the scale used (1\" = 20') and identify any dimension lines or clearance dimensions between trees and electrical infrastructure.\n\n6. LEGEND/SYMBOLS: Identify the symbols used for trees and other site elements, and explain what each symbol represents (e.g., SY = street yard tree, PL = parking lot tree, M = mitigation tree).\n\n7. UTILITY ZONES: Describe any utility easement areas shown on the plan and whether trees are proposed within these easements.\n\nFocus on spatial relationships between proposed trees and electrical facilities to assess compliance with clearance requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (labeled Sheet 28 of 35), here is the detailed information requested:\n\n**1. PROPOSED TREES**\n*   **Depiction:** Proposed trees are depicted as solid circular outlines with a central crosshair. They are distinguished from existing trees, which are shown with dashed circular outlines.\n*   **Symbols/Labels:** Many proposed trees contain text labels identifying their role based on the legend:\n    *   **\"SY\"**: Street Yard Tree\n    *   **\"PL\"**: Parking Lot Tree\n    *   **\"M\"**: Mitigation Tree\n    *   *(Note: Several proposed tree symbols are blank inside and lack a specific letter designation).*\n*   **Spatial Distribution:**\n    *   **West Zone (Street Yard):** A heavy concentration of trees labeled \"SY\" and \"M\" are located in the shaded area designated as \"STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\" (Key Note H-3) along Valley View Road.\n    *   **North Perimeter:** A row of proposed trees (several labeled \"M\" and some unlabeled) runs parallel to the northern property/LOC boundary.\n    *   **East Perimeter:** A row of proposed trees (labeled \"M\", plus one \"SY\" near the northeast corner) runs parallel to the eastern property/LOC boundary behind the buildings.\n    *   **South Perimeter:** A row of proposed trees (several labeled \"M\" and some unlabeled) runs parallel to the southern property boundary.\n    *   **Interior Parking Area:** Proposed trees (labeled \"PL\" and \"M\") are located within designated landscape islands (Key Note H-4) scattered throughout the central parking areas between the buildings.\n\n**2. ELECTRICAL INFRASTRUCTURE SHOWN**\n*   **Overhead Lines (OHE):** A distinct line labeled **\"--- OHE ---\"** runs parallel to the entire southern property boundary.\n*   **Poles:** Asterisk/star symbols (**\\***) are located at intervals along the \"--- OHE ---\" line on the southern boundary, as well as along the eastern and northern boundaries (along the \"- LOC -\" lines). These typically represent utility poles.\n*   **Transformers/Pads:** There is a small square box containing the letter **\"E\"** located in the central parking area, immediately west of an interior landscape island. This commonly denotes an electrical transformer or pedestal.\n*   **Underground Lines / Pull Boxes / Meters:** There are no explicit labels for underground electric lines (e.g., UE), electric pull boxes, or electric meters on this specific landscape plan sheet.\n\n**3. TREE-TO-ELECTRICAL PROXIMITY**\n*   **Overhead electric distribution lines (OHE):** **Yes.** There is a direct spatial conflict shown on the plan. Multiple proposed trees (including those labeled \"M\" and unlabeled solid circles) are placed directly over, under, or immediately adjacent to the **\"--- OHE ---\"** line along the southern property boundary. The drawn tree canopies intersect the OHE line.\n*   **Overhead utility poles:** **Yes.** Proposed trees along the southern boundary are located in close proximity to the asterisk (*) symbols representing poles.\n*   **Electrical transformer pads:** **Yes.** A proposed tree (unlabeled solid circle) is located in the landscape island immediately east of the square labeled **\"E\"**. The tree canopy circle does not appear to overlap the \"E\" box, but it is planted in the adjacent island.\n*   **Electrical pull boxes & Underground electric lines:** Cannot be assessed as they are not explicitly identified on this sheet.\n\n**4. BUILDING PROXIMITY**\nThe site features a series of connected building footprints surrounding a central parking area, with a separate building mass to the west.\n*   Trees act as a perimeter buffer, planted between the outer building facades and the North, East, and South property lines.\n*   Trees are heavily clustered between the westernmost building facade and Valley View Road to create the Street Yard.\n*   Interior trees are confined strictly to curbed parking islands scattered amidst the parking bays, surrounded by the interior-facing building facades.\n\n**5. SCALE AND DIMENSIONS**\n*   **Scale:** The graphic scale in the bottom right corner indicates **SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")**.\n*   **Dimensions:** There are **no specific dimension lines** or numerical clearance distances drawn between any proposed trees and the electrical infrastructure (OHE line, poles, or the \"E\" box) on this plan.\n\n**6. LEGEND/SYMBOLS**\nThe plan utilizes Key Notes and a text legend to define symbols:\n*   **H-1 (Stippled dot pattern):** PROPOSED PAVING\n*   **H-2 (Vertical line pattern):** STREET YARD\n*   **H-3 (Diagonal crosshatch pattern):** STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-4 (Horizontal/vertical crosshatch pattern):** PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-5 (Diagonal line pattern):** PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n*   **H-6 (Line with 'X'):** WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\n*   **H-7 (Blank box):** SOD\n*   **SY:** \"STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **PL:** \"PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **P:** \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   **M:** \"MITIGATION TREE\"\n*   **--- LOC ---:** Limit of Construction\n*   **--- SD ---:** Storm Drain\n\n**7. UTILITY ZONES**\n*   **Easements:** There are **no explicitly labeled Utility Easement (UE) or Public Utility Easement (PUE)** boundaries (typically shown as dashed lines with labels) depicted on this specific landscape plan. While trees are proposed directly adjacent to the OHE line, it is not possible to confirm from this sheet alone if they fall within a legally recorded easement, only that they are in direct physical proximity to the line itself.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1661,"outputTokens":1303,"totalTokens":5247,"reasoningTokens":2283},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Analyze the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. PROPOSED TREES: Identify all proposed trees shown on the plan. Note their locations (by building, parking area, or site zone), their symbols (if any), and whether they are shade trees, ornamental trees, or mitigation trees. Describe their spatial distribution around the site.\n\n2. ELECTRICAL INFRASTRUCTURE SHOWN: Identify all electrical utility facilities shown on the landscape plan (overhead lines, poles, transformers, pull boxes, meters, underground lines). Note how they are depicted (symbols, labels, line styles).\n\n3. TREE-TO-ELECTRICAL PROXIMITY: For each proposed tree, assess its spatial relationship to nearby electrical infrastructure. Are trees shown near or adjacent to:\n   - Overhead electric distribution lines (OHE)?\n   - Electrical transformer pads?\n   - Electrical pull boxes?\n   - Overhead utility poles?\n   - Underground electric lines?\n\n4. BUILDING PROXIMITY: Describe the locations of proposed trees relative to the 8 buildings and parking areas.\n\n5. SCALE AND DIMENSIONS: Note the scale used (1\" = 20') and identify any dimension lines or clearance dimensions between trees and electrical infrastructure.\n\n6. LEGEND/SYMBOLS: Identify the symbols used for trees and other site elements, and explain what each symbol represents (e.g., SY = street yard tree, PL = parking lot tree, M = mitigation tree).\n\n7. UTILITY ZONES: Describe any utility easement areas shown on the plan and whether trees are proposed within these easements.\n\nFocus on spatial relationships between proposed trees and electrical facilities to assess compliance with clearance requirements."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-hun4JoU1rNSHmMoKyrU0Gohb","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 24 Apr 2026 11:41:29 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::8vfm4-1777030857697-edebc2bd0021"},"body":{"co