{"level":30,"time":1777030895374,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":10,"prompt":"Show the location of the private fire hydrant on this fire protection plan. Provide:\n1. Its precise location on the site (which area, relative to which buildings)\n2. The distance in estimated feet (using the scale shown) from the fire hydrant to the nearest transformer pad shown on Sheet 21\n3. Whether the transformer pads are clearly visible on this sheet, or if they need to be cross-referenced with another sheet\n4. Any labels or callouts related to the hydrant location and specifications\n\nUse the 1\" = 20' scale shown on the sheet for distance estimates.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided fire protection plan, here are the details regarding the private fire hydrants:\n\n**1. Precise Location on the Site**\nThere are two \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" locations explicitly labeled within the property boundaries (which, according to the notes on the sheet, designate them as private hydrants):\n\n*   **Hydrant Location A (Internal):** Located on the eastern side of the site's internal drive loop (labeled \"Fire Lane\"). It is situated directly between **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 6**, specifically across the drive from units 704/705 and adjacent to unit 604.\n*   **Hydrant Location B (Entrance):** Located in the southwest corner of the site near the main entrance drive. It is situated south of the \"Fire Lane\" entering the site, directly south of **Bldg. 8**.\n\n*(Note: There is also an \"Existing Fire Hydrant\" labeled in the far northwest corner outside the main property area, near the public right-of-way).*\n\n**2. Distance to Nearest Transformer Pad**\nIt is **not possible** to estimate the distance from either fire hydrant to the nearest transformer pad using the provided 1\" = 20' scale on this specific document.\n\n**3. Visibility of Transformer Pads**\nElectrical transformer pads are **not clearly visible or labeled** anywhere on this sheet. While there are labels for \"Gas Meter,\" \"Water Meter,\" and an \"Elec. Easement\" on the eastern boundary, there are no symbols or callouts specifically identifying transformer pads. Therefore, identifying their locations would absolutely require cross-referencing with another sheet (such as the Sheet 21 mentioned in your prompt).\n\n**4. Labels or Callouts Related to Hydrant Location and Specifications**\n*   **Direct Callouts:** Both hydrant locations identified above have a rectangular callout box pointing to the symbol with the exact text: **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**. The internal hydrant (Location A) also has the letters **\"FH\"** next to the symbol. Both are shown connected to water lines (labeled \"8\" W\" and \"8\" WL DI\").\n*   **Utility Notes:** In the bottom left quadrant, under the heading \"City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\", the text states: *\"This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code.\"*\n*   **Fire Zone Notes:** Note #4 in this section states: *\"Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time. Unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\"*\n*   **General Notes:** Note #2 in this section repeats the exact specification from Fire Zone Note #4 regarding the installation and testing of *\"Underground mains feeding private hydrants\"*.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1435,"outputTokens":645,"totalTokens":3682,"reasoningTokens":1602},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"typ