ecifications**\n*   **Direct Callouts:** Both hydrant locations identified above have a rectangular callout box pointing to the symbol with the exact text: **\"Proposed Fire Hydrant\"**. The internal hydrant (Location A) also has the letters **\"FH\"** next to the symbol. Both are shown connected to water lines (labeled \"8\" W\" and \"8\" WL DI\").\n*   **Utility Notes:** In the bottom left quadrant, under the heading \"City of Austin Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\", the text states: *\"This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code.\"*\n*   **Fire Zone Notes:** Note #4 in this section states: *\"Underground mains feeding private hydrants must be installed and tested in accordance with NFPA-24, and the Fire Code, by a licensed contractor with a plumbing permit. The entire main must be hydrostatically tested at one time. Unless isolation valves are provided between tested sections.\"*\n*   **General Notes:** Note #2 in this section repeats the exact specification from Fire Zone Note #4 regarding the installation and testing of *\"Underground mains feeding private hydrants\"*."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd542ab3-a24e-4d13-af12-e84b414b992a","uuid":"06aab256-18f3-496c-96a2-c2e59d7044ac","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided fire protection plan, here are the details regarding the private fire hydrants:\n\n**1. Precise Location on the Site**\nThere are two \"Proposed Fire Hydrant\" locations explicitly labeled within the property boundaries (which, according to the notes on the sheet, designate them as private hydrants):\n\n*   **Hydrant Location A (Internal):** Located on the eastern side of the site's internal drive loop (labeled \"Fire Lane\"). It is situated directly between **Bldg. 7** and **Bldg. 6**, specifically across the drive from units 704/705 and adjacent to unit 604.\n*  