{"level":30,"time":1777030897199,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify: 1) All trees shown on the plan with their approximate locations and type (shade trees, ornamental, etc.); 2) Utility lines shown including any overhead electric (OHE) lines marked on the plan; 3) The location of any overhead conductors or utility poles relative to proposed trees; 4) Any trees that appear to be positioned near utility infrastructure; 5) The scale (should be 1\" = 20'); 6) Any key notes or symbols used to identify tree types. Please be specific about locations and distances where possible.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (which is labeled as Sheet 28 of 35, despite the prompt's reference to Sheet 31), here is the visual analysis addressing your specific requirements:\n\n**1) All trees shown on the plan with their approximate locations and type:**\nThe plan differentiates between what appear to be existing large trees (indicated by large, dashed circular canopies extending off-site or on the perimeter) and proposed trees (indicated by smaller, solid circles with crosshairs or dots inside). Proposed tree types are indicated by letter labels next to or inside the symbols:\n*   **West Side (along Valley View Road):** There are several proposed trees labeled **\"SY\"** and **\"M\"** (e.g., one labeled \"SY/M\"). These are planted within the shaded area labeled \"H-2\" (STREET YARD).\n*   **North Side (top edge):** A row of proposed trees labeled **\"M\"** is located just inside the northern \"LOC\" (Limits of Construction) line.\n*   **East Side (right edge):** Trees labeled **\"PL\"** are located near the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\". Further south along this edge, there are additional trees labeled **\"M\"**.\n*   **South Side (bottom edge):** A row of approximately six proposed trees labeled **\"M\"** is spaced along the southern property line.\n*   **Internal Areas:** Trees labeled **\"PL\"** are located in the central islands/peninsulas between the parking areas and townhome structures.\n\n**2) Utility lines shown including any overhead electric (OHE) lines marked on the plan:**\n*   **Overhead Electric:** A line clearly marked **\"---OHE---\"** runs horizontally along the entire southern (bottom) boundary of the site plan.\n*   **Storm Drain:** A line marked **\"---SD---\"** runs horizontally through the central drive aisle of the site.\n*   **Water:** A line marked **\"---W---\"** runs parallel and just below the storm drain line through the central drive aisle.\n*   **Limits of Construction:** Marked as **\"---LOC---\"** around the perimeter of the work area.\n\n**3) The location of any overhead conductors or utility poles relative to proposed trees:**\n*   The **\"---OHE---\"** line runs directly along the southern property line.\n*   There is a row of approximately six proposed trees (mostly marked with the **\"M\"** label or standard crosshair symbol) positioned immediately adjacent to, and potentially directly underneath, this **\"---OHE---\"** line along the south boundary.\n\n**4) Any trees that appear to be positioned near utility infrastructure:**\n*   **Near OHE:** As noted above, the entire row of proposed trees along the southern edge is positioned very close to the \"---OHE---\" line.\n*   **Near Underground Utilities:** The trees planted in the central parking islands (labeled \"PL\") are located in close proximity to the underground \"---SD---\" (Storm Drain) and \"---W---\" (Water) lines running through the center of the site.\n*   **Near Basements/Basins:** Trees in the northeast corner are located immediately adjacent to the structural walls of the \"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\" and \"FILTRATION BASIN\".\n\n**5) The scale:**\n*   The scale is explicitly stated in the bottom right corner above the graphic scale bar as: **\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"**.\n\n**6) Any key notes or symbols used to identify tree types:**\nThe plan uses an unnumbered legend located on the right side of the page, beneath the \"KEY NOTES\" table, to identify tree abbreviations. It reads exactly as follows:\n\n*   **SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)**\n*   **PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)**\n*   **P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE**\n*   **M - MITIGATION TREE**\n\nAdditionally, the \"KEY NOTES\" table identifies landscaped areas where these trees are planted:\n*   **H-2**: STREET YARD\n*   **H-3**: STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-4**: PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1438,"outputTokens":938,"totalTokens":4388,"reasoningTokens":2012},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify: 1) All trees shown on the plan with their approximate locations and type (shade trees, ornamental, etc.); 2) Utility lines shown including any overhead electric (OHE) lines marked on the plan; 3) The location of any overhead conductors or utility poles relative to proposed trees; 4) Any trees that appear to be positioned near utility infrastructure; 5) The scale (should be 1\" = 20'); 6) Any key notes or symbols used to identify tree types. Please be specific about locations and distances where possible."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-UzZtaEcnLWWDxteO3LyIGNPG","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 24 Apr 2026 11:41:37 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::b7nq7-1777030849782-21