{"level":30,"time":1777030984915,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012qmcVLfVNLmuvPtz7yENTc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eaadeb1-5dc7-43fe-b5e0-df226e0d41af","uuid":"12580197-06c0-4045-a9f7-67f73e247b2c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777030984915,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Fr7qUcAWBft3r5Y2oPA2PN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The Electric Review section lists:\n- UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n- UCM § 1.10.10.4 is the exact section I'm reviewing in my grouping\n\nSo Austin Energy is aware of this project and has specific requirements. The Bluebeam link suggests there are redline comments, but I don't have access to that link. However, the fact that these requirements are listed suggests that Austin Energy will be reviewing the tree placement against these standards.\n\nNow let me synthesize what I've found so far:\n\n**KEY FINDINGS FROM RESEARCH:**\n\n1. **Applicability**: YES - The project has:\n   - Overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on Sheet 31 running along the southern boundary\n   - Underground electric infrastructure with transformers shown on Sheet 21\n   - Proposed trees shown on the landscape plan (Sheets 31, 32, 35)\n\n2. **Trees Proposed**: According to Sheet 35 plant schedule:\n   - Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 2 trees @ 100 GAL, 16' HT minimum\n   - Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 10 trees @ 100 GAL, 16' HT minimum\n   - Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 2 trees @ 45 GAL, 8' HT minimum\n   - Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 6 trees @ 45 GAL, 10' HT minimum\n\n3. **Locations**: Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows:\n   - Trees along southern boundary running parallel to OHE line (within 5-10 feet based on visual scale)\n   - Trees along western boundary (street yard area near Valley View Road)\n   - Trees scattered throughout interior parking areas and islands, though species designations aren't marked on the plan itself\n\n4. **Issues Identified**:\n   - **EL-2.10 FAIL**: Sheet 31 displays tree symbols without species labels, even though the plant schedule exists separately on Sheet 35. This creates a disconnect and violates the requirement to identify species near electric facilities.\n   - **EL-2.14 NOT-VERIFIABLE / FAIL**: Without dimension lines or clearance measurements shown on the landscape plan, I cannot verify that trees meet the required setbacks from overhead lines.\n   - **EL-2.1 and EL-2.3 potentially FAIL**: The southern boundary trees appear to fall within less than 15 feet of the OHE line based on the 1\"=20' scale, but without species information, I can't confirm whether they're utility-compatible or if they exceed height restrictions. I need to measure the actual distances to verify the clearances.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":62327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eaadeb1-5dc7-43fe-b5e0-df226e0d41af","uuid":"9c32c1a5-d85d-4565-b8f6-7283fc1c14ac"}
{"level":30,"time":1777030984915,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Fr7qUcAWBft3r5Y2oPA2PN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research, let me now compile my findings. I have identified several key issues:\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**APPLICABILITY:** This grouping IS APPLICABLE. The project has:\n- Overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the landscape plan running east-west along the southern property boundary\n- Four pad-mounted electrical transformers shown on the electrical design plan\n- Underground electrical infrastructure with pull boxes\n- Proposed new trees shown on the landscape plan\n\n**PROPOSED TREES (from Plant Schedule on Sheet 35):**\n- Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 2 trees @ 16' HT minimum\n- Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 10 trees @ 16' HT minimum  \n- Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 2 trees @ 8' HT minimum\n- Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 6 trees @ 10' HT minimum\n\n**CRITICAL FINDING - NOT FOUND/NOT VERIFIABLE:**\nThe landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols at various locations but **DOES NOT IDENTIFY THE SPECIES** at each location. The plan shows:\n- Trees along the southern boundary very close to the OHE line (approximately 5-10 feet based on graphic scale of 1\"=20')\n- Trees marked with generic symbols (circles with crosses, dots, etc.) and category labels (M, SY, PL, P)\n- **NO** species identification labels or callouts on the plan itself\n\nWhile Sheet 35 provides a complete plant schedule with species, quantities, and specifications, this schedule is NOT cross-referenced to specific locations on the landscape plan. This prevents verification of:\n- Whether trees near overhead lines are utility-compatible\n- The mature heights of specific trees near electric facilities\n- Whether large trees (40+ feet) are within restricted zones\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":62327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eaadeb1-5dc7-43fe-b5e0-df226e0d41af","uuid":"b9306a66-ede7-4897-9ffb-2e8440884a5b"}
{"level":30,"time":1777030984915,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Fr7qUcAWBft3r5Y2oPA2PN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DKNLDQEPTtE4quS7ZNFHkM","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary of site, running parallel to overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan"}],"comment":"Trees are shown planted along the southern site boundary within approximately 5-10 feet of the overhead electric line (based on graphic scale 1\"=20'). However, the landscape plan does not identify the species of these trees, so utility-compatible status per ECM Appendix F cannot be verified. Plant species schedule exists on Sheet 35 but is not cross-referenced to specific locations on the landscape plan. Provide species identification labels on the landscape plan for all trees proposed within 25 feet of overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern boundary of site, running parallel to overhead electric line; western street yard area near Valley View Road"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Calculations"}],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet) cannot be verified as meeting the 25-foot clearance requirement from distribution conductors because the landscape plan does not identify which species are planted at which locations. While Live Oak and Cedar Elm are shown in the plant schedule with 16-foot minimum heights, their mature heights per ECM Appendix F cannot be verified against specific planting locations on the site plan. Provide species identification and mature height notation on landscape plan for all proposed trees."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site, all proposed trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan"}],"comment":"The landscape plan does not identify species of trees proposed near overhead electric facilities. Trees are shown with category symbols (M=Mitigation, SY=Street Yard, PL=Parking Lot) and geometric symbols but no botanical or common names are labeled on the plan. While a complete plant schedule exists on Sheet 35 listing Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, and Texas Mountain Laurel with quantities, this schedule is not cross-referenced to specific tree locations on the landscape plan. Add species common names or abbreviations (e.g., 'CE' for Cedar Elm, 'LO' for Live Oak) to tree symbols on the landscape plan for all trees within 50 feet of overhead electric facilities."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.14","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site, particularly southern boundary and western boundary where trees and overhead electric lines overlap"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Landscape Plan"},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan"}],"comment":"The overhead electric line is shown on the landscape plan, but trees are not clearly related to it with dimensions. While both overhead electric lines and tree symbols are visible on Sheet 31, there are no dimension lines, call-outs, or notes indicating clearance distances between the trees and conductors. Sheet 21 shows electrical infrastructure separately from the landscape. Cross-reference the two plans with dimension lines or notes showing clearance distances between trees and overhead conductors, demonstrating compliance with 15-foot (distribution) and 50-foot (transmission) requirements."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":62327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6eaadeb1-5dc7-43fe-b5e0-df226e0d41af","uuid":"d8ec10df-b5d6-4810-8cdf-dc1d56f61e0e"}
