ED WITHIN PAVED AREAS SUCH AS\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-15.md:90:21. THE DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION OF RETAINING WALLS, BRIDGES, CULVERTS, HEADWALLS,\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-15.md:91:JUNCTION STRUCTURES, SCREENING WALLS, AND STORMWATER DRAINAGE PIPE WITHIN THE\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-15.md:100:* ON CITY SPONSORED PROJECTS, WHERE CONFLICTS ARE IDENTIFIED BETWEEN THESE CONSTRUCTION NOTES AND\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-26/blocks.md:381:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-24/blocks.md:6:(UCM Section 5.8.0)\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-24/blocks.md:7:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-3.md:16:USE UNTREATED WOOD CHIPS PRODUCED FROM A CHIPPER WITH COMPOST (SECTION 1.0.2.B WOOD CHIP MULCH COMPONENTS).\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-3.md:17:MULCH SOCKS IS PRIMARILY OF ORGANIC MATERIAL SEPARATED AT THE ROOT OF VEGETATION, AND MAY INCLUDE MATERIALS SUCH AS LEAVES, BRANCHES, AND BARK FROM TREES.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-3.md:23:3. MULCH MATERIAL MUST BE FREE OF REFUSE, PHYSICAL CONTAMINANTS, AND MATERIAL TOXIC TO PLANT GROWTH. IT IS NOT ACCEPTABLE FOR THE MULCH MATERIAL TO CONTAIN ANY NON-COMPOSTABLE ITEMS SUCH AS PLASTIC, GLASS, ETC.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-3.md:24:4. SOCK MATERIAL WILL BE 100% BIODEGRADABLE, PHOTODEGRADABLE, OR RECYCLABLE SUCH AS BURLAP, TWINE, UV PHOTODEGRADABLE PLASTIC, POLYESTER, OR ANY OTHER ACCEPTABLE MATERIAL.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-3.md:26:6. ACCUMULATED SILT SHALL BE REMOVED WHEN IT REACHES A DEPTH OF 150 mm (6 INCHES). THE SILT SHALL BE DISPOSED OF ON AN APPROVED SITE AND IN SUCH A MANNER THAT WILL NOT CONTRIBUTE TO ADDITIONAL SILTATION.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-24/block-16.md:33:PLACED INDUCTIVE TRACER TAPE IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE MANUFACTURER'S RE-\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/blocks.md:28:LINEAR CONSTRUCTION THROUGH TREES\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/blocks.md:33:[Illustration showing a tree in a natural area. Callouts indicate 'LIMIT OF CONSTRUCTION LINE', 'AS SHOWN ON PLAN', 'CRITICAL ROOT ZONE (C.R.Z.) RADIUS = 12 mm PER mm (1 FT PER INCH) OF TRUNK DIAMETER'.]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/blocks.md:38:CONSTRUCTION ACTIVITY\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-1.md:5:[Illustration showing a profile of a stabilized construction entrance. Callouts indicate '15 m (50') MIN.', 'GRADIENT TO PREVENT RUNOFF FROM LEAVING SITE', '> 200 mm (8\") MIN.', 'ROADWAY', 'EXISTING GRADE', 'PROVIDE APPROPRIATE TRANSITION BETWEEN STABILIZED CONSTRUCTION ENTRANCE AND PUBLIC RIGHT-OF-WAY'.]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-1.md:18:7. DRAINAGE: ENTRANCE MUST BE PROPERLY GRADED OR INCORPORATE A DRAINAGE SWALE TO PREVENT RUNOFF FROM LEAVING THE CONSTRUCTION SITE.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-1.md:22:STABILIZED CONSTRUCTION ENTRANCE\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/blocks.md:19:ALL PIPE FROM CITY MAIN TO CUSTOMER VALVE SHALL BE RESTRAINED DUCTILE IRON\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/blocks.md:32:7. THE TOP OF THE VAULT SHALL BE AT AN ELEVATION SUCH THAT THE SURROUNDING GROUND SLOPES AWAY FROM THE VAULT. ADDITIONAL DRAINAGE CONSIDERATIONS SUCH AS CONNECTION OF VAULT DRAINAGE TO STORM SEWER, LATERAL DRAIN LINES FROM GRAVEL FLOOR, OR OTHER MEANS SHALL BE REQUIRED IF CONDITIONS CAUSE WATER TO COLLECT IN VAULT.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/blocks.md:56:| 6 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x FLG |\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-25/blocks.md:57:| 7 | DUCTILE IRON CLASS 53 PIPE PER COA SPL WW-27E | 6\", 8\" OR 10\" | FLG x PE |\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-8.md:13:(6\" x 6\") WIRE MESH STRUCTURE\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-8.md:27:3. THE SKIRT SHALL BE WEIGHTED WITH A CONTINUOUS LAYER OF 75-125 mm (3\"-5\") OPEN GRADED ROCK OR TOED-IN 150 mm (6\") WITH MECHANICALLY COMPACTED MATERIAL COVERING THE ENTIRE STRUCTURE SHALL BE TRENCHED IN 100 mm (4\").\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-8.md:30:6. THE DIKE STRUCTURE SHALL BE W4x4-150 mmX150 mm (6 GA 6\"x6\") WIRE MESH, 450 mm (18\") ON A SIDE.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-07/block-4.md:20:7. ACCUMULATED SILT SHALL BE REMOVED WHEN IT REACHES A DEPTH OF 150 mm (6 INCHES). THE SILT SHALL BE DISPOSED OF ON AN APPROVED SITE AND IN SUCH A MANNER THAT WILL NOT CONTRIBUTE TO ADDITIONAL SILTATION.","numLines":148}}
