 answers below apply to all four locations.*\n\n1. **Dimension lines or size labels:** There are no dimension lines or size labels (e.g., \"5'x5'\") on or immediately adjacent to any of the transformer pads.\n2. **Reference callouts:** There are no reference callouts to detail sheets (e.g., \"See Detail X-X\") attached to or pointing to the transformer pads. The only text provided is the label \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" or \"Electrical / Transformer Pad\".\n3. **Phase specifications:** There are no notes or specifications near the transformer pads indicating whether the service is single-phase or three-phase. \n4. **Access door orientation:** There are no symbols, clearance boxes, or annotations showing the access door orientation on any of the transformers. The symbol used is a simple rectangle with diagonal cross lines inside.\n5. **Bollards/Barriers:** There are no bollard symbols (typically small circles) or protective barrier details shown around any of the pads.\n6. **Property lines:** All four transformer pads are clearly shown as being entirely on private property. They are all situated well inside the heavy dashed and dotted line that marks the site's property boundary. \n7. **Easement boundaries:** While there are public utility easements (P.U.E.) and other easements noted on the site plan (e.g., a \"10' P.U.E.\" label on the property line near the middle-left pad), there are no specific dimension lines or notations tying the exact location of the transformer pads to these easement boundaries.\n8. **Shape and size:** All four transformer pads are represented by an exact **rectangular** shape with diagonal crosshatching (an 'X' spanning corner to corner). Based strictly on a visual estimation using the provided \"Scale 1\" = 20'\" bar in the top right, the drawn rectangular symbols appear to represent an approximate footprint of roughly 5 to 7 feet wide by 6 to 8 feet long.\n9. **Drainage/slope indicators:** There are no drainage direction arrows, spot elevations, or slope indicators shown immediately around the transformer pads.\n10. **Utility lines and clearances:** There are various utility lines running near the transformer pads. For instance:\n    * The top-left pad is in the vicinity of a water line (labeled \"-W-\"), a wastewater line (labeled \"-WW-\"), and a \"Gas Meter\" callout. \n    * The middle-left, middle-right, and bottom-middle pads all have water lines (\"-W-\") routed nearby. \n    However, there are **no callouts or labels** stating that clearance verification is required between these utilities and the transformer pads.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1583,"outputTokens":668,"totalTokens":5311,"reasoningTokens":3060},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to lo