r lines shown on the plan**\n*   **Lines:** An existing overhead electric line is shown running north-south along the far western edge of the property boundary (along Valley View Road). It is denoted by a dashed line with the recurring text label \"- OHE -\".\n*   **Poles:** There are no specific individual utility poles clearly marked or labeled along that overhead line within the immediate viewable area of the property boundary on this sheet.\n\n**3. The locations of proposed electrical meters and transformers relative to buildings**\n*   **Transformers:** (See locations listed in Point 1).\n*   **Electrical Meters:** Proposed meter banks are marked with callout boxes reading EXACTLY: \"Electrical Meters\". They are located adjacent to the buildings as follows:\n    *   **Bldg. 1:** Located on the exterior north wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 2:** Located on the exterior east wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 3:** Located on the exterior north wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 4:** Located on the exterior north wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 5:** Located on the exterior west wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 6:** Located on the exterior west wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 7:** Located on the exterior south wall.\n    *   **Bldg. 8:** Located on the exterior south wall, near the southwest corner.\n\n**4. Any dimensions or clearance annotations from overhead utilities to structures**\n*   Reviewing the area between the existing overhead line (\"- OHE -\") on the western boundary and the nearest proposed structures (Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8), there are **no** dimension lines or clearance annotations provided on this specific plan sheet indicating the distance between the overhead utilities and the buildings.\n\n**5. Whether any electric easements are marked**\n*   Yes, several electric and public utility easements (P.U.E.) are marked around the perimeter of the site. Notable labels include:\n    *   Western boundary: \"10' P.U.E.\"\n    *   Northern boundary: \"5' P.U.E.\"\n    *   Eastern boundary: \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14, Vol. 75, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n    *   Southern boundary: \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14, Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" and \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 385 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n\n**6. Any notes about coordination with existing Austin Energy utilities**\n*   While there are notes regarding utility coordination, the specific entity \"Austin Energy\" is **not explicitly named** in the notes on this sheet.\n*   The \"Utility Notes\" box states:\n    *   \"1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\"\n    *   \"2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\"\n*   A note box at the bottom right states: \"The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\"\n\n**7. The overall electrical infrastructure routing and how it relates to the proposed buildings**\n*   The primary electrical infrastructure (shown in solid blue lines) enters the property from the west (Valley View Road), routing underground to an initial \"Electrical Pull Box\" and then to the first \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" near Bldg 2.\n*   From this western point, a main underground trunk line routes eastward, running underneath the central paved driveway/parking areas.\n*   Along this central spine, there are multiple \"Electrical Pull Box\" locations.\n*   The routing branches off from this central spine to feed the two other transformer pads (near Bldg. 5 and Bldg. 7).\n*   From the three respective transformer pads, secondary underground lines route directly to the \"Electrical Meters\" 