{"level":30,"time":1777031854485,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"This is the main site plan (Sheet 9). Please examine it and provide information about:\n1. The location and extent of all parking areas (surface lots, drive aisles, garage entrances)\n2. Fire lanes or fire lane access routes\n3. Sidewalk locations and widths\n4. Any designated open spaces or pedestrian areas\n5. Retaining walls and their locations\n6. Detention/drainage pond location\n7. Overall site layout that would help understand clearance requirements\nAlso note any utility infrastructure shown, such as transformer pads if visible, or other electrical/utility features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (the main site plan), here is the information requested regarding the site layout, infrastructure, and specific features. \n\n### 1. Parking Areas (Surface lots, drive aisles, garage entrances)\n*   **Overall Layout:** The site utilizes a looped drive aisle system that enters from the west (street side) and circles a central block of buildings (Buildings 2, 5, and 8).\n*   **Garages:** The site primarily relies on garage parking. While individual garage doors are not explicitly drawn, unit layouts and the \"Parking Data\" table confirm this. The drive aisles provide direct access to the front of the units in Buildings 1 through 8. \n*   **Surface Parking:** There are three small surface parking areas located off the main drive aisle:\n    *   **Southwest (near entrance):** 2 standard spaces.\n    *   **Southeast (south of Bldg 7):** 3 spaces, including one ADA-accessible space with a striped access aisle.\n    *   **Northeast (east of Bldg 6):** 5 standard spaces.\n*   **Parking Data Table:** (Transcribed exactly as it appears)\n    ```text\n    Parking Data\n    Land Use                                Residential\n    Parking Spaces Provided                 10 Surface/ 76 Garage\n    Compact Spaces Provided                 0\n    ADA Spaces Required                     2\n    ADA Spaces Provided                     2\n    Total Bicycle Spaces Required           5\n    Long Term Bicycle Spaces Required       5\n    Long Term Bicycle Spaces Provided       39 (1 per Garage)\n    Short Term Bicycle Spaces Required      2\n    Short Term Bicycle Spaces Provided      2\n    ```\n\n### 2. Fire Lanes or Fire Lane Access Routes\n*   The primary drive aisle surrounding the central buildings serves as the fire access route. \n*   **Northern Aisle:** Labeled exactly as **\"24' Fire Access / Maintenance Drive\"** running between the detention pond and Buildings 3 and 4.\n*   **Clearances/Radii:** The site plan notes specific turning radii to accommodate emergency vehicles. For example, the outer curve near the detention pond is marked with an **\"R42\"** radius, and inner curves near the central buildings feature bollards, labeled **\"Bollard (Typ)\"**, to protect structures from vehicle encroachment.\n\n### 3. Sidewalk Locations and Widths\n*   **Street Frontage:** A perimeter sidewalk is shown along the western edge of the property boundary, labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 4/33S-2\"**.\n*   **Internal Pathways:** The buildings are connected by a network of walkways labeled **\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ) See Dtl 4/33S-1\"**. These run between the buildings (e.g., between Bldg 1 and 2, and Bldg 4 and 5) to provide pedestrian access to the central open space and units.\n*   **Pond Perimeter:** A distinct path runs along the northern edge of the property next to the detention pond, labeled **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"**.\n\n### 4. Designated Open Spaces or Pedestrian Areas\n*   **Central Courtyard:** A large central gathering area is located between Buildings 2, 4, 5, and 8. It is explicitly labeled **\"Common Open Space 4,960 sf\"**.\n*   **Amenities:** An area labeled **\"BBQ Pit\"** is located on the eastern edge of the property, adjacent to the 5-space surface parking lot.\n*   **Private Spaces:** Rectangular areas labeled **\"Patio\"** are depicted at the rear of the individual townhome units.\n*   **Data Table Confirmation:** The \"Site Data Table\" lists:\n    *   `Common Open Space Required 4709.62`\n    *   `Common Open Space provided 4710`\n\n### 5. Retaining Walls and Their Locations\nRetaining walls are heavily utilized around the perimeter of the site, denoted by thick black lines with structural tick marks:\n*   **North Edge:** A **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** forms the boundary of the detention pond.\n*   **East Edge:** Multiple segments along the eastern property line are labeled **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n*   **South Edge:** Labels read **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** and **\"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall. Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\"**.\n*   **Entrance (West):** Short **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** segments flank the main entrance driveway.\n\n### 6. Detention/Drainage Pond Location\n*   **Location:** The pond is located in the northeast corner of the site plan.\n*   **Features:** It is labeled **\"Filtration/ Detention Pond\"**. It is enclosed by a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and features **\"2 - 6' Pond Access Gates\"** opening toward the fire access/maintenance drive.\n\n### 7. Overall Site Layout (Clearances & Separation)\n*   The site consists of 8 multi-family buildings (ranging from 4-Plex to 6-Plex configurations, totaling 39 units).\n*   Buildings are arranged in a perimeter ring (Bldgs 1, 3, 4, 6, 7) surrounding a central core (Bldgs 2, 5, 8). \n*   **Building Clearances:** Precise building separation dimensions are noted on the plan. For example:\n    *   Between Bldg 1 and Bldg 3: **\"19.3'\"**\n    *   Between Bldg 3 and Bldg 4: **\"18.3'\"**\n    *   Between Bldg 2 and Bldg 8: **\"19.3'\"**\n\n### Utility Infrastructure & Other Features\n*   **Transformers:** A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is prominently located on the western edge of the site, just south of the main entrance driveway, set back from the street. \n*   **Water/Wastewater:** The main utility connection point is at the street (west side), featuring a **\"Wastewater Service Connection\"** and an **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**. Water (\"W\") and Sanitary Sewer (\"SS\") lines are shown routed underneath the internal drive aisles.\n*   **Fire Hydrants:** Several fire hydrants (marked \"FH\") are visible along the drive aisles, including one near the street entrance and others strategically placed near Buildings 4, 5, and 7.\n*   **Easements:** A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** and an **\"Electric & Tele. Easement\"** are demarcated along the eastern and southeastern boundaries of the property.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1431,"outputTokens":1451,"totalTokens":5889,"reasoningTokens":3007},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is the main site plan (Sheet 9). Please examine it and provide information about:\n1. The location and extent of all parking areas (surface lots, drive aisles, garage entrances)\n2. Fire lanes or fire lane access routes\n3. Sidewalk locations and widths\n4. Any designated open spaces or pedestrian areas\n5. Retaining walls and their locations\n6. Detention/drainage pond location\n7. Overall site layout that would help understand clearance requirements\nAlso note any utility infrastructure shown, such as transformer pads if visible, or other electrical/utility features."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-2XAh6iwsgPAtL7Eb8g5LlsnR","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 24 Apr 2026 11:42:02 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-p