n*   **Northern Aisle:** Labeled exactly as **\"24' Fire Access / Maintenance Drive\"** running between the detention pond and Buildings 3 and 4.\n*   **Clearances/Radii:** The site plan notes specific turning radii to accommodate emergency vehicles. For example, the outer curve near the detention pond is marked with an **\"R42\"** radius, and inner curves near the central buildings feature bollards, labeled **\"Bollard (Typ)\"**, to protect structures from vehicle encroachment.\n\n### 3. Sidewalk Locations and Widths\n*   **Street Frontage:** A perimeter sidewalk is shown along the western edge of the property boundary, labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 4/33S-2\"**.\n*   **Internal Pathways:** The buildings are connected by a network of walkways labeled **\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ) See Dtl 4/33S-1\"**. These run between the buildings (e.g., between Bldg 1 and 2, and Bldg 4 and 5) to provide pedestrian access to the central open space and units.\n*   **Pond Perimeter:** A distinct path runs along the northern edge of the property next to the detention pond, labeled **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"**.\n\n### 4. Designated Open Spaces or Pedestrian Areas\n*   **Central Courtyard:** A large central gathering area is located between Buildings 2, 4, 5, and 8. It is explicitly labeled **\"Common Open Space 4,960 sf\"**.\n*   **Amenities:** An area labeled **\"BBQ Pit\"** is located on the eastern edge of the property, adjacent to the 5-space surface parking lot.\n*   **Private Spaces:** Rectangular areas labeled **\"Patio\"** are depicted at the rear of the individual townhome units.\n*   **Data Table Confirmation:** The \"Site Data Table\" lists:\n    *   `Common Open Space Required 4709.62`\n    *   `Common Open Space provided 4710`\n\n### 5. Retaining Walls and Their Locations\nRetaining walls are heavily utilized around the perimeter of the site, denoted by thick black lines with structural tick marks:\n*   **North Edge:** A **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** forms the boundary of the detention pond.\n*   **East Edge:** Multiple segments along the eastern property line are labeled **\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"**.\n*   **South Edge:** Labels read **\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"** and **\"End Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall. Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\"**.\n*   **Entrance (West):** Short **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** segments flank the main entrance driveway.\n\n### 6. Detention/Drainage Pond Location\n*   **Location:** The pond is located in the northeast corner of the site plan.\n*   **Features:** It is labeled **\"Filtration/ Detention Pond\"**. It is enclosed by a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and features **\"2 - 6' Pond Access Gates\"** opening toward the fire access/maintenance drive.\n\n### 7. Overall Site Layout (Clearances & Separation)\n*   The site consists of 8 multi-family buildings (ranging from 4-Plex to 6-Plex configurations, totaling 39 units).\n*   Buildings are arranged in a perimeter ring (Bldgs 1, 3, 4, 6, 7) surrounding a central core (Bldgs 2, 5, 8). \n*   **Building Clearances:** Precise building separation dimensions are noted on the plan. For example:\n    *   Between Bldg 1 and Bldg 3: **\"19.3'\"**\n    *   Between Bldg 3 and Bldg 4: **\"18.3'\"**\n    *   Between Bldg 2 and Bldg 8: **\"19.3'\"**\n\n### Utility Infrastructure & Other Features\n*   **Transformers:** A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is prominently located on the western edge of the site, just south of the main entrance driveway, set back from the street. \n*   **Water/Wastewater:** The main utility connection point is at the street (west side), featuring a **\"Wastewater Service Connection\"** and an **\"Existing Water Manhole\"**. Water (\"W\") and Sanitary Sewer (\"SS\") lines are shown routed underneath the internal drive aisles.\n*   **Fire Hydrants:** Several fire hydrants (marked \"FH\") are visible along the drive aisles, including one near the street entrance and others strategically placed near Buildings 4, 5, and 7.\n*   **Easements:** A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** and an **\"Electric & Tele. Easement\"** are demarcated along the eastern and southeastern boundaries of the property.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1431,"outputTokens":1451,"totalTokens":5889,"reasoningTokens":3007},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":215896.794247,"endTime":288815.835238,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"wlbrab-JCLz-sbwP4uKJsA8"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.056358","marketCost":"0.056358","inferenceCost":"0.056358","inputInferenceCost":"0.002862","outputInferenceCost":"0.053496","generationId":"gen_01KPZMNSCE9FHYCJ3TSBK0K1VQ"}}},"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (the main site plan), here is the information requested regarding the site layout, infrastructure, and specific features. \n\n### 1. Parking Areas (Surface lots, drive aisles, garage entrances)\n*   **Overall Layout:** The site utilizes a