blic utility easements (P.U.E.) and other easements noted on the site plan (e.g., a \"10' P.U.E.\" label on the property line near the middle-left pad), there are no specific dimension lines or notations tying the exact location of the transformer pads to these easement boundaries.\n8. **Shape and size:** All four transformer pads are represented by an exact **rectangular** shape with diagonal crosshatching (an 'X' spanning corner to corner). Based strictly on a visual estimation using the provided \"Scale 1\" = 20'\" bar in the top right, the drawn rectangular symbols appear to represent an approximate footprint of roughly 5 to 7 feet wide by 6 to 8 feet long.\n9. **Drainage/slope indicators:** There are no drainage direction arrows, spot elevations, or slope indicators shown immediately around the transformer pads.\n10. **Utility lines and clearances:** There are various utility lines running near the transformer pads. For instance:\n    * The top-left pad is in the vicinity of a water line (labeled \"-W-\"), a wastewater line (labeled \"-WW-\"), and a \"Gas Meter\" callout. \n    * The middle-left, middle-right, and bottom-middle pads all have water lines (\"-W-\") routed nearby. \n    However, there are **no callouts or labels** stating that clearance verification is required between these utilities and the transformer pads."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d291c25-51de-4c78-8a82-6fde89edc795","uuid":"d65a1b9f-2cd2-4404-890f-c712f8c873a0","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the answers to your questions regarding the transformer pads. \n\n*Note: While the prompt mentions \"the three transformer pads\", a close review of the document reveals **four** distinct locations with callouts pointing to an \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" (top-left near entry, middle-left near Bldg 2, bottom-middle near Bldg 7, and middle-right near Bldg 6). The answers below