{"level":30,"time":1777031854497,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify: (1) Are overhead utility lines (marked O.H.U.L. or with pole symbols) depicted on this plan? (2) If shown, where are they located and which buildings or site features are near them? (3) Are there any clearance dimensions, notes, or annotations related to overhead electric lines? (4) Identify the locations of Buildings 1-8, driveways, any fences, retaining walls, or other site features that might need clearance from overhead utilities. (5) Check the northern property boundary area in particular, as the existing conditions survey showed overhead utilities along that boundary.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan sheet (Sheet 9 of 39 for Valley View Townhomes), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**(1) Depiction of overhead utilities:**\nYes, overhead utility lines are depicted on this plan. They are identified by a dashed line type interspersed with the label `---OHE---` (indicating Overhead Electric) and connect to circular utility pole symbols.\n\n**(2) Location of overhead utilities:**\nThe `---OHE---` line is located exclusively along the **southern property boundary** (the bottom edge of the site plan drawing), running generally parallel to the adjacent roadway. \n*   It runs continuously across the bottom frontage of the site.\n*   It directly crosses over both proposed driveway entrances (labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\").\n*   It crosses over the proposed \"Construct 6' Concrete Sidewalk\" near the bottom left and bottom right.\n*   It is located directly south of Building 8, Building 7, and Building 6.\n\n**(3) Clearance dimensions, notes, or annotations:**\nA thorough review of the plan's annotations, line work, and all provided text blocks (including \"Site Plan Release Notes,\" \"Accessibility Notes,\" \"Lighting Note,\" etc.) reveals **no clearance dimensions, notes, or annotations** related to required distances or safety buffers from the overhead electric lines on this specific sheet.\n\n**(4) Locations of Buildings and relevant site features:**\n*   **Building 1 (3 Units, FFE=687.50):** Located in the northwest quadrant.\n*   **Building 2 (4 Units, FFE=686.50):** Located in the center-west area.\n*   **Building 3 (5 Units, FFE=685.50):** Located in the north-central area.\n*   **Building 4 (5 Units, FFE=686.50):** Located in the center of the site.\n*   **Building 5 (4 Units, FFE=688.0):** Located along the eastern boundary.\n*   **Building 6 (4 Units, FFE=683.0):** Located in the southeast corner.\n*   **Building 7 (5 Units, FFE=685.0):** Located in the south-central area.\n*   **Building 8 (6 Units, FFE=685.50):** Located in the southwest corner.\n*   **Driveways:** Two primary driveways (labeled \"Construct Type II Driveway\") enter from the south boundary (underneath the `---OHE---` line) to provide internal circulation.\n*   **Fences:** A \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" is shown around the detention pond in the northeast. A \"Wood Fence\" runs along the eastern property line.\n*   **Retaining Walls:** A \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" bounds the northeast pond. An \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" runs along the eastern boundary (near Buildings 5 and 6). Several segments labeled \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall\" are located along the southern frontage near the street and sidewalks.\n\n**(5) Northern property boundary check:**\nA precise inspection of the northern property boundary (the top edge of the drawing) shows features such as a \"Wastewater Service Connection,\" \"Existing Water Manhole,\" \"AT&T Ped.,\" \"Concrete Curb,\" and a \"Biofiltration/Detention Pond.\" **There are no overhead utility lines (`---OHE---`) or utility pole symbols depicted along the northern boundary on this specific proposed site plan sheet.** Only underground utility lines, such as wastewater (`---WW---`) and water (`---W---`), are visible in that specific area.\n\n***\n\n### Transcribed Tables\nPer your instructions to reproduce tables exactly as they appear for validation requirements, the primary data tables from the document are transcribed below:\n\n**Building Data Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | Gross Floor Area (sf) | Building Coverage (sf) | Bedroom Type | Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Two Bedroom | 16 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Three Bedroom | 23 |\n| 3 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | Total Units | 39 |\n| 4 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | | |\n| 5 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Maximum Number of Building Stories = 3 | |\n| 6 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | | |\n| 7 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | | |\n| 8 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Foundation = Slab on grade | |\n\n**Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n| Unit Type | Efficiency | 1 Bedroom | 2+ Bedroom |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| Number of Units | 0 | 0 | 39 |\n| Required Site Area Per Unit (sf) | 1,600 | 2,000 | 2,400 |\n| Site Area Required (sf) | 0 | 0 | 93,600 |\n| Total Site Area Required (sf) | | 93,600 | |\n| Total Site Area Provided (sf) | | 94,192 | |","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1443,"outputTokens":1275,"totalTokens":7451,"reasoningTokens":4733},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase,