{"level":30,"time":1777031861188,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019YWME62JrM1Mt8ATXYSj5R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the vision tool now identifies FOUR transformer pads, not three as previously stated. The tool mentions:\n1. Top-left near entry\n2. Middle-left near Building 2\n3. Bottom-middle near Building 7\n4. Middle-right near Building 6\n\nKey findings from this detailed vision analysis:\n- NO dimension labels on any pads\n- NO reference callouts to detail sheets\n- NO phase specifications shown\n- NO access door orientation marked\n- NO bollards/barriers shown\n- ALL pads are on private property (good)\n- NO specific easement boundary callouts\n- Estimated size: 5-7 feet wide by 6-8 feet long (roughly)\n- NO drainage indicators\n- Various utilities nearby (W, WW, gas) but NO clearance verification callouts\n\nThis is significant - the transformer pad design lacks critical details that should be shown per the code requirements. Specifically:\n\n1. EL-13.37 - \"Transformer pad dimensions do not match Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets\" - No AE-approved details are referenced on the plan\n2. EL-13.4, 5, 6 - Various clearance reductions and special conditions cannot be verified without proper documentation\n3. EL-13.38 - Bollard details not shown (if within 4 feet of parking)\n4. EL-13.39 - Overhead distribution facilities need to be confirmed\n\nSince there are no AE-approved transformer pad details referenced, I should mark this as not meeting the requirement. Also, I need to verify if any transformer pads are within 4 feet of parking areas (EL-13.38).\n\nLet me measure the distances from transformer pads to parking areas.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"ca