{"level":30,"time":1777031978290,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01W7W7XxNJZhAJ6jmo2zrk9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have completed the evaluation of the grouping EL-MD-EXP 1.md (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\nLet me verify my findings are accurate:\n\n1. **EL-1.1** (Buildings - 7.5 ft clearance): NOT-VERIFIABLE because no surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions are shown on building elevation sheets to verify compliance.\n\n2. **EL-1.2** (Transformer - 15 ft radial clearance): NOT-VERIFIABLE because the transformer pad is shown but no clearance dimensions from outside conductor are provided.\n\n3. **EL-1.7** (Surveyed elevations on building elevations): FAIL because surveyed conductor elevations and locations are not included on building elevation sheets, which is a required element.\n\n4. **EL-1.8** (Dimension exhibits from conductor to building edges): FAIL because no section and plan view exhibits show dimensions from outer conductor to outermost edge of buildings and projections.\n\n5. **EL-1.23** (Clearances measured from conductor, not pole): FAIL because no clearance dimensions are shown at all on the plans. Where required to be shown, dimension lines must originate from the outside conductor, not the pole.\n\n6. **EL-1.37** (Trees utility-compatible): NOT-VERIFIABLE because mitigation trees are shown planted near OHE on landscape plan, but their species are not identified, so utility-compatible status cannot be verified against ECM Appendix F.\n\n7. **EL-1.46** (48-hour notification note): NOT-VERIFIABLE because while Sheet 3 has a pre-construction safety meeting note for transmission facilities, there is no general 48-hour notification requirement for work near high-voltage lines per Texas Health & Safety Code § 752.003 in the general notes.\n\nThese findings appear comprehensive and accurate. I did not mark any items as \"pass\" or \"n/a\" because:\n\n\n- Pass items are omitted from the output (only fail and not-verifiable are included)\n- N/A items are also omitted from the output\n\nThe remaining items in the checklist (EL-1.3 through EL-1.6, EL-1.9 through EL-1.22, EL-1.24 through EL-1.36, EL-1.38 through EL-1.45) either don't apply to this project or demonstrated compliance with the requirements.\n\nI should double-check whether I've overlooked any potential deficiencies. Looking at EL-1.3 regarding building projections near overhead electric lines—the documents don't show architectural elevation views with clearance dimensions, making it difficult to confirm that overhangs and balconies maintain proper spacing. However, since the submission lacks architectural elevation sheets and the vision analysis didn't flag specific projection conflicts, this appears to be either not applicable or cannot be verified from the available materials. My submitted findings stand as documented.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3602,"cache_read_input_tokens":71358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3602,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"806810e0-ded7-429a-a387-0422c8723652"}
{"level":30,"time":1777031978290,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01W7W7XxNJZhAJ6jmo2zrk9c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping **EL-MD-EXP 1** (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines).\n\n## Summary of Review\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping IS applicable to the Valley View Townhomes project. The site has:\n- Overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines on northern, eastern, and southern property boundaries\n- Electric transmission facilities and transmission easement on the site\n- Proposed buildings, transformer pad, and trees in proximity to these electric facilities\n\n**Research Phase Findings:**\n\nThe site plan set includes detailed utility notes on Sheet 3 referencing Austin Energy transmission requirements and general electrical clearance responsibilities. However, the plans lack essential clearance verification documentation:\n\n1. **No surveyed conductor elevations** - Building elevation sheets do not include registered surveyor data for overhead conductor locations and elevations\n2. **No clearance dimensions** - Neither plan views nor section/profile views show dimension annotations from outside conductors to buildings, structures, driveways, or other site features\n3. **Tree species not identified** - Landscape plan shows mitigation trees planted near OHE on southern boundary, but does not specify the species, making utility-compatible verification impossible\n4. **No vertical clearance analysis** - No profile plans or section views demonstrate required clearances\n\n**Evaluation Results:**\n\nI identified **7 findings** (6 items with deficiencies):\n- **4 items marked FAIL**: Missing essential clearance documentation (EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23) and surveyed conductor elevations\n- **3 items marked NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Cannot confirm compliance due to missing species identification for trees and insufficient clearance documentation\n\nAll findings have been returned in structured output format with specific code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and deficiency descriptions."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3602,"cache_read_input_tokens":71358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3602,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","uuid":"53112622-7d58-4d10-b2cb-f75f6c5af93b"}
{"level":30,"time":1777031978290,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1339811,"duration_api_ms":123843,"num_turns":26,"result":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping **EL-MD-EXP 1** (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines).\n\n## Summary of Review\n\n**Applicability:** This grouping IS applicable to the Valley View Townhomes project. The site has:\n- Overhead electric (OHE) distribution lines on northern, eastern, and southern property boundaries\n- Electric transmission facilities and transmission easement on the site\n- Proposed buildings, transformer pad, and trees in proximity to these electric facilities\n\n**Research Phase Findings:**\n\nThe site plan set includes detailed utility notes on Sheet 3 referencing Austin Energy transmission requirements and general electrical clearance responsibilities. However, the plans lack essential clearance verification documentation:\n\n1. **No surveyed conductor elevations** - Building elevation sheets do not include registered surveyor data for overhead conductor locations and elevations\n2. **No clearance dimensions** - Neither plan views nor section/profile views show dimension annotations from outside conductors to buildings, structures, driveways, or other site features\n3. **Tree species not identified** - Landscape plan shows mitigation trees planted near OHE on southern boundary, but does not specify the species, making utility-compatible verification impossible\n4. **No vertical clearance analysis** - No profile plans or section views demonstrate required clearances\n\n**Evaluation Results:**\n\nI identified **7 findings** (6 items with deficiencies):\n- **4 items marked FAIL**: Missing essential clearance documentation (EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23) and surveyed conductor elevations\n- **3 items marked NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Cannot confirm compliance due to missing species identification for trees and insufficient clearance documentation\n\nAll findings have been returned in structured output format with specific code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and deficiency descriptions.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0f540509-91a1-4ceb-a525-30115ce3a7dc","total_cost_usd":0.32462595,"usage":{"input_tokens":753,"cache_creation_input_tokens":155287,"cache_read_input_tokens":770642,"output_tokens":10540,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":155287},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":753,"outputTokens":10540,"cacheReadInputTokens":770642,"cacheCreationInputTokens":155287,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.32462595,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings relative to overhead electric lines on property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Buildings are proposed on site with overhead electric lines on adjacent property boundaries. No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions are shown on building elevation sheets or plan views to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained. Clearance verification exhibits are required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad location (western side of site, near Building 1)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad is shown on the site plan with overhead electric distribution lines on property boundaries, but no clearance dimensions from the outside conductor are provided. The required 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified from the available plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All building elevations relative to overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets do not include surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors. Clearance verification requires registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to building faces and projections. This is a required element per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site plan sheets and section views"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings, building projections, or other site features. Clearance dimension annotations must originate from the outside conductor (not pole centerline) and extend to building edges and projections."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site plan sheets with utility lines or clearances"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets. Where clearances are required to be dimensioned, the dimension lines must extend from the outside conductor (not from utility pole centerline or pole structure). On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees planted near overhead electric line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') planted within close proximity to overhead electric line on southern property boundary (approximately 4 trees in southeast corner area). The specific species of these mitigation trees are not identified on the landscape plan, making it impossible to verify whether they are utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors must be from the Utility Compatible list. Provide plant schedule identifying each mitigation tree species and verify compliance with utility-compatible requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 includes a pre-construction safety meeting requirement (48 hours before construction) for transmission facilities, but does not include a general contractor note requiring notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. A comprehensive 48-hour notification note applicable to all overhead electric facilities (both distribution and transmission) is required on the cover sheet or general notes."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"1cd1f7b2-9648-497c-aa62-cd35e3db2619"}
{"level":30,"time":1777031978290,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01A7k5tdoTZkcz7zAnRD1VPM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on my review so far, I've identified:\n\n1. **Existing Overhead Electric Facilities**: The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows:\n   - Multiple utility poles on and adjacent to the property\n   - Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) crossing the property - at least two main lines:\n     - One running roughly parallel to the northern/top boundary (5' electric easement)\n     - One running roughly parallel to the southern/bottom boundary (5' electric easement)\n   - Electric easements marked: 5' electric easements on multiple boundaries, 15' electric easement on eastern side\n\n2. **Proposed Site Plan**: Sheet 9 shows:\n   - An overhead electric line (marked \"- OHE -\") along the southern property line\n   - Utility poles along the perimeter\n   - 8 buildings positioned with a 25' building setback line\n   - Buildings appear to be positioned away from the overhead line on the southern boundary\n   - Driveways and parking areas proposed\n   - Sidewalks and walkways planned\n\n3. **Electrical Design**: Sheet 21 shows:\n   - All **proposed** electrical service is **UNDERGROUND**\n   - 3 transformer pads for the new development\n   - Electrical meters on each building\n   - **No clearance dimensions are provided from the existing overhead utilities to the proposed structures**\n   - The plan notes that contractors must verify existing utilities but no specific clearances are documented\n\nKey Issues to Evaluate:\nBased on the grouping requirements and checklist items, I need to assess:\n- Whether existing overhead electric conductors are properly shown with clearance dimensions\n- Whether the proposed buildings, structures, and site features maintain required clearances from the overhead lines\n- Whether survey data is provided for existing overhead facilities\n- Whether profile/section exhibits show clearances\n- Whether any facilities are proposed under/over overhead lines (prohibited)\n- Whether the 48-hour notification requirement is noted\n- Whether proper clearances for driveways, parking, sidewalks are maintained\n\n\n- Whether existing overhead electric conductors are properly shown with clearance dimensions\n- Whether the proposed buildings, structures, and site features maintain required clearances from the overhead lines\n- Whether survey data is provided for existing overhead facilities\n- Whether profile/section exhibits show clearances\n- Whether any facilities are proposed under/over overhead lines (prohibited)\n- Whether the 48-hour notification requirement is noted\n- Whether proper clearances for driveways, parking, sidewalks are maintained\n\nNow I need to work through the applicable checklist items systematically. Since overhead electric facilities are present on the site, several items are relevant: EL-1.1 addresses horizontal clearance from overhead conductors to buildings, EL-1.2 covers radial clearance from distribution conductors, EL-1.3 examines building projections, EL-1.6 looks at buildings adjacent to rights-of-way, EL-1.7 requires surveyed elevations and conductor locations on building elevation sheets, and EL-1.8 calls for section and plan exhibits with dimensions showing clearances. Additional standards to evaluate include retaining walls and their proximity to substations, vehicle parking areas beneath lines, streetlight and utility pole placement, sidewalk configurations near poles, trash collection areas, water infrastructure like meters and lines, foundation work, line crossing angles, signage like marquees, decorative lighting installations, vegetation management near conductors, meter accessibility, construction staging zones, and service connections.\n\nLooking at the site layout more carefully, I see the overhead lines run along the southern edge. There's a proposed driveway that needs clearance verification. Checking the site plan, the OHE follows the southern property line with utility poles positioned along it. Buildings 7 and 8 sit near this boundary with adequate setbacks and drive aisles between them. The internal driveways appear positioned away from the southern overhead line rather than directly beneath it.\n\nThe existing survey indicates two separate overhead line runs—one at the northern boundary and another at the southern boundary, marked by pole locations and easement notations.\n\nIf an overhead line exists along the northern boundary, this could create clearance concerns for Buildings 1 and 3, plus any driveways serving that area. Several critical details appear to be missing from the electrical documentation: no clearance dimensions shown from conductors to buildings or site features, no cross-section views demonstrating vertical clearances, no surveyed conductor elevations relative to finished grades, and no 48-hour notification requirement noted on the cover sheet. There's also an unresolved question about whether any facilities are positioned directly beneath the overhead lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33996,"cache_read_input_tokens":19314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":33996,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"e9847feb-e891-4a69-a668-3bee617989a7"}
