{"level":30,"time":1777031991982,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: (1) Where are the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines located? Are they shown on the northern boundary, southern boundary, or elsewhere? (2) Are there any proposed trees (shown as symbols with SY, PL, P, or M designations) located within 10 feet horizontally from the overhead electric lines? (3) What tree species are proposed near overhead utilities, and are there any notes or callouts about clearances or utility-compatible trees? (4) Are there any proposed structures, fences, lighting poles, or other features near the overhead electric lines that might need clearance verification? (5) Compare the overhead electric line locations shown here to what was documented on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) - do they appear consistent?","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032016886,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: (1) Where are the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines located? Are they shown on the northern boundary, southern boundary, or elsewhere? (2) Are there any proposed trees (shown as symbols with SY, PL, P, or M designations) located within 10 feet horizontally from the overhead electric lines? (3) What tree species are proposed near overhead utilities, and are there any notes or callouts about clearances or utility-compatible trees? (4) Are there any proposed structures, fences, lighting poles, or other features near the overhead electric lines that might need clearance verification? (5) Compare the overhead electric line locations shown here to what was documented on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) - do they appear consistent?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided \"LANDSCAPE PLAN\" (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the findings corresponding to your questions:\n\n**(1) Where are the overhead electric (OHE) utility lines located?**\nThe overhead electric utility lines are located along the **southern boundary** of the site plan (the bottom edge of the drawing). They are clearly denoted by a line type with the text **\"-OHE-\"** running horizontally across the bottom section. \n\n**(2) Are there any proposed trees (shown as symbols with SY, PL, P, or M designations) located within 10 feet horizontally from the overhead electric lines?**\nYes, near the southeast corner (bottom right of the drawing), there are proposed trees designated with an **\"M\"** (which the legend identifies as **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**) situated very close to the southern property line and the \"-OHE-\" line. While an exact measurement cannot be confirmed without a physical scale ruler, at the stated scale of 1\"=20', these \"M\" designated trees appear to be planted within approximately 10 to 15 scale feet of the indicated overhead electric lines. \n\n**(3) What tree species are proposed near overhead utilities, and are there any notes or callouts about clearances or utility-compatible trees?**\n*   **Species:** Specific tree species cannot be identified from this sheet. The plan uses functional category labels (e.g., \"M\" for Mitigation Tree, \"SY\" for Street Yard Tree) rather than specific botanical callouts. A separate plant schedule (likely on another sheet) would be needed to determine the exact species.\n*   **Notes/Clearances:** There are **no notes, callouts, or warnings** on this sheet regarding utility clearances, planting restrictions under power lines, or the selection of utility-compatible tree species. The visible \"NOTE:\" and \"IRRIGATION NOTES:\" sections do not mention overhead utilities.\n\n**(4) Are there any proposed structures, fences, lighting poles, or other features near the overhead electric lines that might need clearance verification?**\nYes. There is a proposed fence line running directly adjacent to/underneath the \"-OHE-\" line along that southern boundary. This line is designated with an \"X\" pattern and is pointed to by Key Note circle **\"H.6\"**. \nAccording to the KEY NOTES legend, H.6 is a **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"**. Additionally, an underground utility line designated as **\"-SD-\"** (typically Storm Drain) runs parallel just north of the OHE line. No lighting poles are visibly designated in this immediate area.\n\n**(5) Compare the overhead electric line locations shown here to what was documented on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) - do they appear consistent?**\nThis comparison cannot be performed, as only Sheet 28 (Landscape Plan) has been provided for this analysis. Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey) is required to verify consistency.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature"