{"level":30,"time":1777032044460,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018bGRDo3b939AjzHDCoVoRA","type":"tool_result","content":"/vercel/sandbox/src/orchestrator/checklist-manager.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/src/tools/validate-checklist.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/tests/checklist-manager.test.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/austin-energy-design-criteria/contents/site-plan-review-checklist.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/downtown-density-bonus-program/meta/structured-output/requirements-checklist.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/fire-alarm-submittal-checklist\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/fire-alarm-submittal-checklist/contents/requirements-checklist.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/nbg/meta/structured-output/requirements-checklist.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/plaza-saltillo/meta/structured-output/requirements-checklist.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/codes/wildland-urban-interface/contents/wui-review-checklist\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/review/scripts/split-by-grouping.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/jurisdictions/austin/workflows/smoke-test/prompts/checklist-setup.md\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/workflows/train/scripts/build-dept-checklists.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/bureau/workflows/train/scripts/build-refinement-checklist.ts\n/vercel/sandbox/workspace/workflow/scripts/split-by-grouping.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013TYaEkp4jKyikLtXBbFZe5","session_id":"ef672522-d4e7-4b95-adea-0f34cf5c6c5b","uuid":"a270cfe6-92de-4963-ab63-9dc3396674c5"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032046459,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LhtdwAFCHd55XuhNETGdkc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough information to evaluate all checklist items. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## Research Summary\n\nBased on my review of the site plan documents, I found:\n\n**Electrical Infrastructure Present:**\n- Overhead electric (OHE) line shown along southern property boundary on landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n- Underground electrical distribution system serving the buildings shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21)\n- 4 transformer pads shown on electrical plan (west of Buildings 2 & 8, east of Buildings 4 & 7)\n- No transmission facilities identified on the site (voltage not specified but typical for townhome development is distribution-level)\n- No transmission easement identified (easements are 5-foot electric, not transmission-scale)\n\n**Proposed Trees:**\n- Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists: 10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak, 6 Mexican Redbud, 2 Texas Mountain Laurel\n- Cedar Elm: Mature height 90 feet, NOT utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n- Live Oak: Mature height 60 feet, NOT utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F  \n- Mexican Redbud: Mature height 20 feet, IS utility-compatible\n- Texas Mountain Laurel: Mature height 25 feet, IS utility-compatible\n- Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees as symbols (SY, PL, P, M) with no species identification\n\n**Critical Finding - Clearance Measurements:**\n- Measured distance from OHE line to proposed trees along southern boundary: 3.1 feet and 6 feet (MEDIUM confidence)\n- Required clearances per UCM § 1.10.10.4:\n  - Non-utility-compatible trees: minimum 15 lateral feet from distribution conductor\n  - Large trees (40+ ft mature height): minimum 25 lateral feet from distribution conductor\n- **Trees measured are 3-6 feet from conductor - well below required minimums**\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Specific species identification for individual trees on landscape plan\n- Large tree notation/distinction on landscape plan showing mature height\n- Utility pole locations clearly marked on plans\n- Dimensioned clearances between trees and utilities on landscape plan\n- Underground equipment locations detailed enough to verify 5-foot and 20-foot clearances\n- Root barrier specifications on landscape plan\n- Austin Energy written approval for trees in restricted clearance zones\n- Cross-sheet references linking specific tree symbols on landscape plan to species listed on plant schedule\n\nNow let me prepare the structured findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1068,"cache_read_input_tokens":67707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1068,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13d31a74-8d60-4982-8b24-9aff9d56548a","uuid":"32eac99f-5402-4f71-b6ce-6b44edc76d48"}
