{"level":30,"time":1777032047498,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01LL3zvyydGqhmKJb7ZrRHfZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key findings from this vision analysis:\n\n1. Overhead electric lines shown OFF-SITE on the western edge (OHE)\n2. On-site transformers are fed by UNDERGROUND lines only\n3. No future/proposed utility routes crossing transformers\n4. A \"Vault Easement\" is shown near one transformer\n5. A \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement\" is shown along the southern property boundary\n6. Clear routing paths shown from each transformer to pull boxes to meters\n7. All electrical routing is on private property (GOOD)\n8. NO niche/enclosed locations for transformers\n9. NO oil-filled vs. dry-type designation shown\n10. NO cross-sections showing vertical clearances\n11. NO window/door details for building clearance verification\n\nNow I need to check:\n1. Whether the Vault Easement transformer might actually be a niche configuration (EL-13.29-30)\n2. Whether underground utilities are at the required clearances (EL-13.21-26)\n3. Whether overhead lines need clearance verification (EL-13.27-28)\n4. Whether trees are near any transformers (EL-13.13-15)\n5. Whether fire lanes are properly distanced (EL-13.19)\n\nLet me examine the utility plans to understand underground utility locations relative to transformer pads.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":64595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1865,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0d291c25-51de-4c78-8a82-6fde89edc795","uuid":"850d5dc8-808a-45c7-b91f-96ad9334e10