t Side Structures:** Multiple references to **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"**, **\"Concrete Buttress\"**, and **\"Wood Fence\"** are located behind Buildings 5 and 6.\n\n### 7. Overall Layout and Fire Safety Clearance Requirements\nThe overall site layout is designed as a continuous loop. This design is highly beneficial for fire safety as it allows fire apparatus to enter the site, circulate completely around the primary building clusters, and exit without needing to perform a multi-point turnaround (there are no dead-end fire lanes shown). The 26-foot width in the main loop provides adequate space for apparatus staging and outrigger deployment.\n\n**Crucial Fire Safety Note:**\nIn the bottom center of the page, under the \"Fire Riser Room Note\" heading, it states:\n**\"All buildings are to have a NFPA 13D fire suppression system.\"**\n\n**Relationship of Fire Lanes and Hydrants to Overall Circulation:**\nThe fire lane is integrated directly into the primary site circulation drive aisles; they are one and the same. The placement of the two proposed hydrants at the southwest and southeast curves of the loop ensures that all building facades facing the inner loop, as well as the outer perimeter buildings, are within reach of a water supply. The continuous loop allows a fire engine to pull past a hydrant, lay a supply line, and position itself favorably in front of any building on the site while maintaining a clear path for other incoming emergency vehicles.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canon