ulatory category symbols (M, SY, PL, P) with no species names. Plant schedule exists on Sheet 35 listing species, but landscape plan lacks cross-reference linking specific tree symbols to the species identified on the plant schedule. Proposed trees near utilities must be clearly identified by species directly on the landscape plan or through explicit cross-sheet notation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not differentiate large trees (mature height 40+ feet) from smaller trees near overhead electric facilities. Trees shown as 'M' symbols provide no indication of which are Cedar Elm (90 ft), Live Oak (60 ft), or smaller species (Mexican Redbud 20 ft, Texas Mountain Laurel 25 ft). Large tree species and mature heights must be clearly noted or indicated on the landscape plan to allow verification of clearance compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not show dimensioned clearances between proposed trees and overhead electric conductors. While field measurement identifies distances of 3.1 to 6 feet, plan dimensions and notes must clearly show that all clearances are measured from the outside conductor (not pole centerline) to the tree trunk center (not canopy edge) per UCM § 1.10.10.4 measurement methodology. Provide dimensions on landscape plan showing tree-to-conductor distances measured from proper reference points."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees near overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan does not dimension clearances from tree trunks to overhead electric conductors. All clearance measurements must originate from tree trunk center (planting location symbol), not from projected canopy edge per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Provide dimension lines and notes on landscape plan confirming that clearances are measured from proper reference points."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan proposes trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) within prohibited clearance zones (less than 15 feet from distribution conductors and less than 25 feet for large trees) without documented written approval from Austin Energy. Variations to standard tree placement distances and non-compatible species designations require explicit Austin Energy approval per UCM § 1.10.10.4. Provide signed approval letter from Austin Energy or revise landscape plan to maintain required clearances."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9ae73df5-d3c0-469e-ab23-34fd2f5f4ac7"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032185897,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_014c1jAXm3Ex6MoX14MjyBMC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. Now I have a good understanding of the site layout. Let me now use the measure-distance tool to check clearances from the transformer pads to nearby buildings, parking areas, fire hydrants, and other features. From the vision analysis, I know:\n\n1. Five transformer pads are located on the site (Sheet 21)\n2. Transformer Pad 1: Near Building 1, west side\n3. Transformer Pad 2: Near Building 2, west side  \n4. Transformer Pad 3: Near Building 8, west side\n5. Transformer Pad 4: Between Buildings 4 and 5, central area\n6. Transformer Pad 5: Between Buildings 6 and 7, southeast area\n\nThe grouping requirements are:\n- 5-foot minimum clearance from buildings/structures\n- 5-foot clearance from various features (fire hydrants, dumpsters, bike racks, light poles)\n- 10-foot from access door side (hot-stick clearance) or 15 feet if facing confined space\n- 5-foot clearance from fences (operators/controls side) or 3 feet (non-operators side)\n- 20-foot from fire escapes (oil-filled equipment)\n- 2 feet from back of sidewalks\n- 15 feet from fire lanes (if marked)\n- Within 4 feet of parking areas = needs 4-inch bollards\n- Trees within 10 feet need to be utility-compatible\n- Trees within 20 feet need root barriers\n- 5-foot clearances from water, wastewater, and storm drain lines\n- 5-foot from fire hydrants\n\nLet me measure critical distances using the measure-distance tool. I need to check several key distances:\n\n1. From each transformer pad to nearest building wall\n2. From transformer pads near parking areas (to see if within 4 feet)\n\n\n3. From transformer pads to fire hydrants\n4. From transformer pads to adjacent trees (if visible on plan)\n5. From transformer pads to sidewalks\n\nThe scale is 1\" = 20', so scaleInchesPerFoot = 1/20 = 0.05. I'll start with the most critical measurements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2389,"cache_read_input_tokens":62062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2389,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6a22569-366b-4e39-9203-cc923425b52a","uuid":"809442fe-7464-4f26-b2c0-88cef793d225"}
