{"level":30,"time":1777032493910,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013TYaEkp4jKyikLtXBbFZe5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have the complete checklist with all 47 items. Let me analyze each item against the evidence you've provided about the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\nBased on the facts you've documented, here is my evaluation of all 47 checklist items for the EL-MD-EXP grouping:\n\n---\n\n## OVERHEAD ELECTRIC CLEARANCE CHECKLIST EVALUATION\n### Valley View Townhomes Project\n### EL-MD-EXP Grouping (47 Items)\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.1: Buildings - 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Building locations shown on site plan (Sheet 9) with overhead electric line on southern boundary. However, no surveyed conductor elevation or building elevation sheets provided to verify 7.5-foot clearance is maintained. Cannot measure without surveyed conductor heights and building roof/eave elevations.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.2: Customer facilities - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings relative to southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Southern overhead line documented on Sheets 9, 31. Building locations shown but no clearance dimensions provided. Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance without dimension callouts, conductor identification (primary vs. secondary), and voltage information. Proposed driveways may also trigger this requirement.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.3: Building projections - clearances from overhead conductors**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets provided showing projections (overhangs, eaves, balconies). Cannot verify required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from building projections without elevation views.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.4: Gas pump canopies - clearances from overhead lines**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No gas pump canopies shown on any sheets. Item not applicable to residential townhome development.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.5: Stairs, elevated walkways, platforms - 15-foot radial clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Potential at building entries if shown  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Site plan does not clearly show elevated walkways or stairs. Cannot verify without detailed site plan callouts and section views showing any elevated features relative to overhead line routing.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.6: Buildings in ROW - clearances from relocated facilities**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE / FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings potentially within right-of-way setback distance  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Overhead utilities exist on adjacent properties (northern and southern boundaries). No utility relocation notes or ROW clearance documentation provided. Cannot verify setbacks maintained; concerning that northern overhead line documented on Sheet 4 is omitted from Sheet 9 with no demolition/relocation explanation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.7: Building elevations - surveyed conductor elevations**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets included in document set showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimensions. This is a critical missing document type explicitly required by code to demonstrate clearances are met.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.8: Section/plan exhibits - dimensions from conductor to building**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings relative to overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No section or profile exhibits provided showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building edges, projections, or other site features. Plans show buildings and overhead lines in plan view only; no cross-section documentation of vertical relationships.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.9: Fences - 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if fences shown  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No fence layout details found on submitted sheets. Cannot verify clearances if present. If fences are proposed, clearance dimensions from outside conductor must be provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.10: Fence posts - 10-foot clearance from electric poles**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if fences proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No fence or pole proximity information visible on submitted sheets. If fences proposed, verify 10-foot clearance from pole locations.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.11: Fences near substation - 10-foot non-conductive isolation**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** No substation facilities identified on site or adjacent property. Item not applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.12: Fencing near transmission lines - non-conductive/grounded**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** Overhead facilities appear to be distribution lines (not transmission; no voltage ≥60kV indicated). Item applies only to transmission facilities.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.13: Vehicle barrier fencing - 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If driveways cross southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Proposed driveways cross under overhead lines on southern boundary per narrative. However, no barrier fencing details or clearance exhibits provided. Cannot verify if barriers present or if 7.5-foot clearance maintained.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.14: Retaining walls - 7.5-foot clearance from overhead line**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if retaining walls present  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No retaining wall details visible on submitted sheets. If retaining walls exist near overhead lines, clearance dimensions from conductor must be provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.15: Retaining walls near substation - 5-foot separation**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No substation identified on or adjacent to site. Item not applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.16: Emergency access structures - 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) identified. Item not applicable to residential townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.17: Retaining walls - section exhibits with clearance dimensions**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If retaining walls exist near overhead  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No retaining wall sections provided. Cannot verify clearances if walls present.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.18: Driveways - 16 or 18-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** FAIL / NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Proposed driveways crossing southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed driveways crossing under overhead electric line on southern boundary. No vertical clearance dimensions provided on grading plan or sections. No determination whether truck traffic applies (16-foot vs. 18-foot requirement). No mid-span survey data provided. CRITICAL VIOLATION: Cannot verify driveways maintain minimum clearance from lowest point of overhead facilities.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.19: Vehicles parked/displayed - vertical clearance from overhead**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If parking proposed beneath overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** No parking areas explicitly shown beneath southern overhead line. If parking proposed in this area, vertical clearance dimensions (12-18 feet depending on use) must be noted on site plan with clearance verification.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.20: Roads/driveways beneath transmission - 30-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** Overhead facilities appear to be distribution lines, not transmission (voltage <60kV). Item applies only to transmission facilities ≥60kV.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.21: Highway/freeway - 40-foot clearance with underbuilt distribution**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** No highway or freeway grades shown. Item not applicable to townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.22: Electric poles in conflict with driveways - 30-foot relocation**\n**Status:** UNCLEAR / POSSIBLE FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern property boundary overhead pole if it still exists  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows overhead utility pole on northern boundary. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) omits northern overhead utilities with no relocation or demolition notation. If pole remains and driveways are within 30 feet, it must be relocated. Need clarification on pole disposition.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.23: Clearance dimensions measured from conductor (not pole)**\n**Status:** FAIL (Cannot Verify Compliance)  \n**Applicable Areas:** All clearance dimensions on plans  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Plans show overhead lines but provide NO clearance dimension callouts at all. Cannot verify that any clearance dimensions shown are measured from outside conductor (not pole centerline). This is a universal requirement whenever clearances are dimensioned.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.24: Streetlight poles under overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If streetlights proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No photometric plan or streetlight detail provided in document set. Cannot verify if streetlights placed appropriately relative to overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.25: Sidewalks cleared from power poles at property ends**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** ROW frontages on northern/southern boundaries  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Sidewalk alignment and power pole locations not clearly detailed on submitted sheets. Cannot verify clearance at property limits along ROW.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.26: Trash enclosures under overhead - bin raised height**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If trash enclosures shown  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No trash enclosure or dumpster locations provided on site plan. If trash facilities proposed near overhead lines, verify 7.5-foot clearance includes raised bin height during service.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.27: Facilities under/over distribution lines (absolute prohibition)**\n**Status:** FAIL / NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Potentially all buildings and driveways crossing overhead  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** This is a critical absolute prohibition independent of clearance distances. Plans show driveways crossing under southern overhead line and buildings near overhead facilities. No explicit documentation that facilities are NOT located directly beneath/over conductors. The omission of northern overhead line from Sheet 9 creates uncertainty about what exists. VIOLATION: Cannot confirm buildings/driveways are not placed directly under/over distribution conductors.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.28: Water meters - 7.5-foot clearance from service drops**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If water service to buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** Water meter locations not shown on utility plan. Cannot verify clearance from overhead service-drop conductors if meters proposed near overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.29: Water lines - clearance from distribution facilities**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If water lines cross overhead pole routes  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Water line routing not detailed on utility plan. If water mains cross near or under overhead distribution poles, verify clearance dimensions provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.30: Foundations within 5 feet of property line**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings at property perimeter  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Foundation locations not dimensioned relative to property lines on site plan. If buildings within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities in adjacent ROW, clearance space must be preserved.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.31: Registered surveyor data for marginal vertical clearances**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All buildings and driveways near overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Building elevations range 686.25-685 ft MSL; overhead line elevations unknown. Without surveyed conductor heights and building elevations, vertical clearances appear marginal or unverifiable. CRITICAL: Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey NOT provided when required by code for marginal clearances.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.32: Overhead line crossings at 90-degree angle**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Southern overhead line if it crosses driveways  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Overhead line crossing angle relative to driveway centerline not indicated on plans. If new overhead lines proposed to cross roads, verify 90-degree orientation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.33: Secondary over primary overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Southern overhead line configuration  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Conductor types (primary, secondary, neutral) not labeled on plans. Utility plan does not show section view of line routing. Cannot verify secondary lines do not cross above primary lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.34: Marquee signs - clearance verification**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No marquee signs shown. Item not applicable to townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.35: New poles for underground service - 20-foot spacing**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If underground conversion proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No utility plan detail showing underground service conversion or new pole locations. Cannot verify spacing if applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.36: Decorative lighting under overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Landscape areas if decorative lights proposed  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Landscape plan (Sheet 31) provided but no decorative lighting fixture locations detailed. If outdoor lighting proposed under overhead lines, verify clearances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) or relocation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.37: Trees within clearance zones - utility-compatible species required**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Trees planted 10-15 feet from southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4  \n**Comment:** Proposed mitigation trees shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) approximately 10-15 feet from southern overhead line. VIOLATION: Trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors MUST be Utility Compatible species (ECM Appendix F \"UC\" designation, generally ≤20 feet mature height). Narrative states \"mitigation trees\" but does not confirm species. Plan must identify specific species by botanical name and verify against UC list. If trees are NOT utility-compatible species, they will grow into overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.38: Meter locations obstructed by features**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If electric meters shown on plan  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.9.3.1  \n**Comment:** Electric meter locations not detailed on site plan. If meters proposed, verify 30-inch-wide front access, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom maintained without obstruction.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.39: Development maintaining clearances from streetlights**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings if streetlights present  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Streetlight pole locations not shown on site plan. If existing streetlights present, verify buildings/structures maintain clearances.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.40: Down guy wires - conflicts with paths/driveways**\n**Status:** FAIL / MISSING DATA  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern and southern boundaries where poles exist  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.17.0  \n**Comment:** Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole on northern boundary; southern boundary has overhead line. Down guy anchor locations typically omitted from plans per review guide. CRITICAL: Site plan does not show guy wire or anchor locations. If poles have down guys and driveways pass near poles, guy anchors could conflict with accessible routes. Requires verification from utility company and additional survey data.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.41: Guy easements for angled anchors (transmission)**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No transmission structures identified. Item applies only to transmission facilities. Distribution poles use down guys (addressed in EL-1.40/1.42), not angled guy anchors.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.42: Down guy anchor easements (10-foot width)**\n**Status:** FAIL / MISSING DATA  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern and southern poles if down guys present  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Easement exhibit and plat do not show down guy anchor easements. If poles have down guys (highly likely, not shown on plans), dedicated 10-foot-wide easement extending minimum 5 feet past anchor ground entry point REQUIRED per Austin Energy standards. No easement shown on exhibits.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.43: Transformers - 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If pad-mounted transformers exist  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Utility plan does not show transformer locations or details. If transformers present or proposed near overhead lines, verify 7.5-foot vertical clearance documented in section views.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.44: Transformers in niche - 35-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.4  \n**Comment:** No niche service configurations shown. Item applies only if transformers/switchgears are in covered/recessed installations. Not applicable to this project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.45: Construction staging - 10-foot radial clearance from energized lines**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Entire site during construction  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.2  \n**Comment:** No construction logistics or staging plan provided. VIOLATION: Plans must include note or logistics exhibit showing construction staging areas, equipment zones, and work platforms maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance (all directions) from energized overhead lines per OSHA 1910.333 and Texas Health & Safety Code § 752. This is separate from permanent clearance requirements and is mandatory when overhead lines exist.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.46: 48-hour notification note for high-voltage work**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Cover sheet  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.2  \n**Comment:** No 48-hour notification note found on cover sheet per your research. VIOLATION: Plans must include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. This note is MANDATORY when overhead lines exist on or adjacent to site.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.47: Service-mast roof clearance (3 feet or 18 inches)**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If service masts shown on building elevations  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets provided showing service-mast through-roof installations. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch if within 4 feet of roof edge) for ≤300V service. Building elevation sheets required to verify.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY OF FINDINGS\n\n**CLEAR FAILURES (Non-Compliant):**\n1. **EL-1.7** - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n2. **EL-1.8** - No section/profile exhibits showing clearance dimensions\n3. **EL-1.18** - Driveways under overhead line with no vertical clearance verification\n4. **EL-1.23** - No clearance dimensions shown on plans; cannot verify measured from conductor\n5. **EL-1.27** - Cannot confirm facilities not placed directly under/over distribution conductors\n6. **EL-1.37** - Proposed trees within 10-15 feet of overhead line; species not verified as utility-compatible\n7. **EL-1.40** - Down guy conflicts not addressed; guy locations omitted from plans\n8. **EL-1.42** - Down guy anchor easements not shown on plat/easement exhibit\n9. **EL-1.45** - No construction staging clearance plan provided\n10. **EL-1.46** - No 48-hour notification note on cover sheet\n\n**CRITICAL NOT-VERIFIABLE (Missing Essential Documentation):**\n1. **EL-1.1, 1.2, 1.3** - No building elevations or clearance dimensions to verify any clearances\n2. **EL-1.6** - Northern overhead utilities omitted from proposed plan with no explanation (demolition/relocation unknown)\n3. **EL-1.22** - Unclear if northern utility pole removed or remaining; if remaining and driveway nearby, relocation required\n4. **EL-1.31** - No surveyor mid-span clearance data when vertical clearances appear marginal\n\n**N/A ITEMS (Not Applicable):**\nEL-1.4, 1.11, 1.12, 1.15, 1.16, 1.20, 1.21, 1.34, 1.41, 1.44\n\n---\n\n**KEY ARCHITECTURAL/DOCUMENTATION GAPS:**\n- Building elevation sheets completely missing\n- Section/profile exhibits with clearance dimensions completely missing\n- Utility plan lacks conductor type labels, voltage, surveyed elevations\n- Grading plan lacks vertical clearance annotations for driveway crossings\n- Easement exhibit lacks down guy anchor easement boundaries\n- Cover sheet lacks required safety notification notes\n- Landscape plan tree species not confirmed as utility-compatible\n\nThis grouping requires substantial additional documentation and design changes to achieve compliance."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9756397ccdf4fe82 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 35502\ntool_uses: 5\nduration_ms: 62301</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef672522-d4e7-4b95-adea-0f34cf5c6c5b","uuid":"11af4380-f592-4cfb-b54f-17315a76958e","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm conducting a site plan review for overhead electric clearance requirements (EL-MD-EXP grouping, 47 checklist items total). I have completed research on the Valley View Townhomes project and found the following key facts:\n\n**EXISTING FACILITIES:**\n- Overhead utility line documented on-site along northern property boundary with a utility pole (Sheet 4)\n- Overhead electric line on southern property boundary (Sheets 9, 31)\n- Proposed 8 buildings with various elevations (686.25-685 ft MSL range)\n- Proposed driveways crossing under overhead lines on southern boundary\n- Proposed trees (mitigation trees) near southern overhead line, approximately 10-15 feet away\n- NO building elevations provided to verify vertical clearances\n- NO clearance dimension callouts on any sheets\n- NO surveyed conductor elevations shown\n- NO 48-hour notification note found on cover sheet\n- Discrepancy: Northern overhead utilities on existing survey (Sheet 4) are omitted from proposed site plan (Sheet 9) with no demolition/relocation notes\n\n**DOCUMENTS AVAILABLE:**\n- Sheet 4: Existing Conditions Survey (overhead utilities shown)\n- Sheet 9: Site Plan (overhead utilities shown on south only, north omitted)\n- Sheet 31: Landscape Plan (overhead utilities shown, trees planted 10-15 feet away)\n- Sheet 21: Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (underground only, not relevant)\n- Sheet 30: Existing Tree Plan\n- Sheets 1-39: Complete site plan set\n\n**GROUPING REQUIREMENTS:**\nThe grouping (EL-MD-EXP) requires:\n- Site Plan Sheets with existing/proposed facilities\n- Building Elevation Sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions\n- Section/Profile Exhibits with clearance dimensions\n- Utility Plans with clearance annotations\n- Landscape Plans with tree species verification\n- Cover Sheet notes including 48-hour notification requirement\n\n**YOUR TASK:**\nEvaluate each of the 47 checklist items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47) based on this evidence. For each item, determine:\n- **Status**: pass (compliant), fail (non-compliant), not-verifiable (cannot determine), or n/a (not applicable)\n- **Applicable Areas**: Where on the site the item applies (e.g., \"southern property boundary\", \"proposed buildings 1-3\", etc.)\n- **Code Citation**: The UCM or ECM section from the checklist\n- **Comment**: What was found, what's missing, or why it cannot be verified\n\nFocus on items where:\n1. Evidence shows a clear violation (fail)\n2. Critical evidence is missing preventing verification (not-verifiable)\n3. The item genuinely doesn't apply to this project (n/a)\n\nOutput your evaluation in a structured format for each item. Be thorough - this is the complete set of checklist items for this grouping.","agentId":"a9756397ccdf4fe82","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have the complete checklist with all 47 items. Let me analyze each item against the evidence you've provided about the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\nBased on the facts you've documented, here is my evaluation of all 47 checklist items for the EL-MD-EXP grouping:\n\n---\n\n## OVERHEAD ELECTRIC CLEARANCE CHECKLIST EVALUATION\n### Valley View Townhomes Project\n### EL-MD-EXP Grouping (47 Items)\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.1: Buildings - 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Building locations shown on site plan (Sheet 9) with overhead electric line on southern boundary. However, no surveyed conductor elevation or building elevation sheets provided to verify 7.5-foot clearance is maintained. Cannot measure without surveyed conductor heights and building roof/eave elevations.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.2: Customer facilities - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary/neutral**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings relative to southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Southern overhead line documented on Sheets 9, 31. Building locations shown but no clearance dimensions provided. Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance without dimension callouts, conductor identification (primary vs. secondary), and voltage information. Proposed driveways may also trigger this requirement.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.3: Building projections - clearances from overhead conductors**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets provided showing projections (overhangs, eaves, balconies). Cannot verify required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from building projections without elevation views.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.4: Gas pump canopies - clearances from overhead lines**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No gas pump canopies shown on any sheets. Item not applicable to residential townhome development.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.5: Stairs, elevated walkways, platforms - 15-foot radial clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Potential at building entries if shown  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Site plan does not clearly show elevated walkways or stairs. Cannot verify without detailed site plan callouts and section views showing any elevated features relative to overhead line routing.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.6: Buildings in ROW - clearances from relocated facilities**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE / FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings potentially within right-of-way setback distance  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Overhead utilities exist on adjacent properties (northern and southern boundaries). No utility relocation notes or ROW clearance documentation provided. Cannot verify setbacks maintained; concerning that northern overhead line documented on Sheet 4 is omitted from Sheet 9 with no demolition/relocation explanation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.7: Building elevations - surveyed conductor elevations**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets included in document set showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimensions. This is a critical missing document type explicitly required by code to demonstrate clearances are met.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.8: Section/plan exhibits - dimensions from conductor to building**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All 8 proposed buildings relative to overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No section or profile exhibits provided showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building edges, projections, or other site features. Plans show buildings and overhead lines in plan view only; no cross-section documentation of vertical relationships.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.9: Fences - 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if fences shown  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No fence layout details found on submitted sheets. Cannot verify clearances if present. If fences are proposed, clearance dimensions from outside conductor must be provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.10: Fence posts - 10-foot clearance from electric poles**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if fences proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No fence or pole proximity information visible on submitted sheets. If fences proposed, verify 10-foot clearance from pole locations.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.11: Fences near substation - 10-foot non-conductive isolation**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** No substation facilities identified on site or adjacent property. Item not applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.12: Fencing near transmission lines - non-conductive/grounded**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** Overhead facilities appear to be distribution lines (not transmission; no voltage ≥60kV indicated). Item applies only to transmission facilities.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.13: Vehicle barrier fencing - 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If driveways cross southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Proposed driveways cross under overhead lines on southern boundary per narrative. However, no barrier fencing details or clearance exhibits provided. Cannot verify if barriers present or if 7.5-foot clearance maintained.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.14: Retaining walls - 7.5-foot clearance from overhead line**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Site perimeter if retaining walls present  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No retaining wall details visible on submitted sheets. If retaining walls exist near overhead lines, clearance dimensions from conductor must be provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.15: Retaining walls near substation - 5-foot separation**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No substation identified on or adjacent to site. Item not applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.16: Emergency access structures - 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No emergency access structures (bridges, elevated platforms) identified. Item not applicable to residential townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.17: Retaining walls - section exhibits with clearance dimensions**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If retaining walls exist near overhead  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No retaining wall sections provided. Cannot verify clearances if walls present.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.18: Driveways - 16 or 18-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** FAIL / NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Proposed driveways crossing southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** Site plan (Sheet 9) shows proposed driveways crossing under overhead electric line on southern boundary. No vertical clearance dimensions provided on grading plan or sections. No determination whether truck traffic applies (16-foot vs. 18-foot requirement). No mid-span survey data provided. CRITICAL VIOLATION: Cannot verify driveways maintain minimum clearance from lowest point of overhead facilities.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.19: Vehicles parked/displayed - vertical clearance from overhead**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If parking proposed beneath overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** No parking areas explicitly shown beneath southern overhead line. If parking proposed in this area, vertical clearance dimensions (12-18 feet depending on use) must be noted on site plan with clearance verification.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.20: Roads/driveways beneath transmission - 30-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** Overhead facilities appear to be distribution lines, not transmission (voltage <60kV). Item applies only to transmission facilities ≥60kV.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.21: Highway/freeway - 40-foot clearance with underbuilt distribution**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.14.0  \n**Comment:** No highway or freeway grades shown. Item not applicable to townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.22: Electric poles in conflict with driveways - 30-foot relocation**\n**Status:** UNCLEAR / POSSIBLE FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern property boundary overhead pole if it still exists  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows overhead utility pole on northern boundary. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) omits northern overhead utilities with no relocation or demolition notation. If pole remains and driveways are within 30 feet, it must be relocated. Need clarification on pole disposition.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.23: Clearance dimensions measured from conductor (not pole)**\n**Status:** FAIL (Cannot Verify Compliance)  \n**Applicable Areas:** All clearance dimensions on plans  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Plans show overhead lines but provide NO clearance dimension callouts at all. Cannot verify that any clearance dimensions shown are measured from outside conductor (not pole centerline). This is a universal requirement whenever clearances are dimensioned.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.24: Streetlight poles under overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If streetlights proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No photometric plan or streetlight detail provided in document set. Cannot verify if streetlights placed appropriately relative to overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.25: Sidewalks cleared from power poles at property ends**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** ROW frontages on northern/southern boundaries  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Sidewalk alignment and power pole locations not clearly detailed on submitted sheets. Cannot verify clearance at property limits along ROW.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.26: Trash enclosures under overhead - bin raised height**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If trash enclosures shown  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No trash enclosure or dumpster locations provided on site plan. If trash facilities proposed near overhead lines, verify 7.5-foot clearance includes raised bin height during service.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.27: Facilities under/over distribution lines (absolute prohibition)**\n**Status:** FAIL / NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Potentially all buildings and driveways crossing overhead  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** This is a critical absolute prohibition independent of clearance distances. Plans show driveways crossing under southern overhead line and buildings near overhead facilities. No explicit documentation that facilities are NOT located directly beneath/over conductors. The omission of northern overhead line from Sheet 9 creates uncertainty about what exists. VIOLATION: Cannot confirm buildings/driveways are not placed directly under/over distribution conductors.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.28: Water meters - 7.5-foot clearance from service drops**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If water service to buildings  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3, UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** Water meter locations not shown on utility plan. Cannot verify clearance from overhead service-drop conductors if meters proposed near overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.29: Water lines - clearance from distribution facilities**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If water lines cross overhead pole routes  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Water line routing not detailed on utility plan. If water mains cross near or under overhead distribution poles, verify clearance dimensions provided.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.30: Foundations within 5 feet of property line**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings at property perimeter  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Foundation locations not dimensioned relative to property lines on site plan. If buildings within 5 feet of property line and electric facilities in adjacent ROW, clearance space must be preserved.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.31: Registered surveyor data for marginal vertical clearances**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** All buildings and driveways near overhead lines  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Building elevations range 686.25-685 ft MSL; overhead line elevations unknown. Without surveyed conductor heights and building elevations, vertical clearances appear marginal or unverifiable. CRITICAL: Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey NOT provided when required by code for marginal clearances.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.32: Overhead line crossings at 90-degree angle**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Southern overhead line if it crosses driveways  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Overhead line crossing angle relative to driveway centerline not indicated on plans. If new overhead lines proposed to cross roads, verify 90-degree orientation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.33: Secondary over primary overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Southern overhead line configuration  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Conductor types (primary, secondary, neutral) not labeled on plans. Utility plan does not show section view of line routing. Cannot verify secondary lines do not cross above primary lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.34: Marquee signs - clearance verification**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** No marquee signs shown. Item not applicable to townhome project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.35: New poles for underground service - 20-foot spacing**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If underground conversion proposed  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No utility plan detail showing underground service conversion or new pole locations. Cannot verify spacing if applicable.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.36: Decorative lighting under overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Landscape areas if decorative lights proposed  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Landscape plan (Sheet 31) provided but no decorative lighting fixture locations detailed. If outdoor lighting proposed under overhead lines, verify clearances (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) or relocation.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.37: Trees within clearance zones - utility-compatible species required**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Trees planted 10-15 feet from southern overhead line  \n**Code Citation:** ECM § 2.4.1.D, ECM § 2.4.2.C, UCM § 1.10.10.4  \n**Comment:** Proposed mitigation trees shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) approximately 10-15 feet from southern overhead line. VIOLATION: Trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors MUST be Utility Compatible species (ECM Appendix F \"UC\" designation, generally ≤20 feet mature height). Narrative states \"mitigation trees\" but does not confirm species. Plan must identify specific species by botanical name and verify against UC list. If trees are NOT utility-compatible species, they will grow into overhead lines.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.38: Meter locations obstructed by features**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If electric meters shown on plan  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.9.3.1  \n**Comment:** Electric meter locations not detailed on site plan. If meters proposed, verify 30-inch-wide front access, 36-inch front depth, and 6.5-foot headroom maintained without obstruction.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.39: Development maintaining clearances from streetlights**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** Buildings if streetlights present  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Streetlight pole locations not shown on site plan. If existing streetlights present, verify buildings/structures maintain clearances.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.40: Down guy wires - conflicts with paths/driveways**\n**Status:** FAIL / MISSING DATA  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern and southern boundaries where poles exist  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.17.0  \n**Comment:** Existing survey (Sheet 4) shows utility pole on northern boundary; southern boundary has overhead line. Down guy anchor locations typically omitted from plans per review guide. CRITICAL: Site plan does not show guy wire or anchor locations. If poles have down guys and driveways pass near poles, guy anchors could conflict with accessible routes. Requires verification from utility company and additional survey data.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.41: Guy easements for angled anchors (transmission)**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** No transmission structures identified. Item applies only to transmission facilities. Distribution poles use down guys (addressed in EL-1.40/1.42), not angled guy anchors.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.42: Down guy anchor easements (10-foot width)**\n**Status:** FAIL / MISSING DATA  \n**Applicable Areas:** Northern and southern poles if down guys present  \n**Code Citation:** Reviewer Convention  \n**Comment:** Easement exhibit and plat do not show down guy anchor easements. If poles have down guys (highly likely, not shown on plans), dedicated 10-foot-wide easement extending minimum 5 feet past anchor ground entry point REQUIRED per Austin Energy standards. No easement shown on exhibits.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.43: Transformers - 7.5-foot vertical clearance from overhead lines**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If pad-mounted transformers exist  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.3  \n**Comment:** Utility plan does not show transformer locations or details. If transformers present or proposed near overhead lines, verify 7.5-foot vertical clearance documented in section views.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.44: Transformers in niche - 35-foot vertical clearance**\n**Status:** N/A  \n**Applicable Areas:** N/A  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.4  \n**Comment:** No niche service configurations shown. Item applies only if transformers/switchgears are in covered/recessed installations. Not applicable to this project.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.45: Construction staging - 10-foot radial clearance from energized lines**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Entire site during construction  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.2  \n**Comment:** No construction logistics or staging plan provided. VIOLATION: Plans must include note or logistics exhibit showing construction staging areas, equipment zones, and work platforms maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance (all directions) from energized overhead lines per OSHA 1910.333 and Texas Health & Safety Code § 752. This is separate from permanent clearance requirements and is mandatory when overhead lines exist.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.46: 48-hour notification note for high-voltage work**\n**Status:** FAIL  \n**Applicable Areas:** Cover sheet  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.2  \n**Comment:** No 48-hour notification note found on cover sheet per your research. VIOLATION: Plans must include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. This note is MANDATORY when overhead lines exist on or adjacent to site.\n\n---\n\n### **EL-1.47: Service-mast roof clearance (3 feet or 18 inches)**\n**Status:** NOT-VERIFIABLE  \n**Applicable Areas:** If service masts shown on building elevations  \n**Code Citation:** UCM § 1.10.6.2  \n**Comment:** No building elevation sheets provided showing service-mast through-roof installations. Cannot verify 3-foot clearance above roof (or 18-inch if within 4 feet of roof edge) for ≤300V service. Building elevation sheets required to verify.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY OF FINDINGS\n\n**CLEAR FAILURES (Non-Compliant):**\n1. **EL-1.7** - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n2. **EL-1.8** - No section/profile exhibits showing clearance dimensions\n3. **EL-1.18** - Driveways under overhead line with no vertical clearance verification\n4. **EL-1.23** - No clearance dimensions shown on plans; cannot verify measured from conductor\n5. **EL-1.27** - Cannot confirm facilities not placed directly under/over distribution conductors\n6. **EL-1.37** - Proposed trees within 10-15 feet of overhead line; species not verified as utility-compatible\n7. **EL-1.40** - Down guy conflicts not addressed; guy locations omitted from plans\n8. **EL-1.42** - Down guy anchor easements not shown on plat/easement exhibit\n9. **EL-1.45** - No construction staging clearance plan provided\n10. **EL-1.46** - No 48-hour notification note on cover sheet\n\n**CRITICAL NOT-VERIFIABLE (Missing Essential Documentation):**\n1. **EL-1.1, 1.2, 1.3** - No building elevations or clearance dimensions to verify any clearances\n2. **EL-1.6** - Northern overhead utilities omitted from proposed plan with no explanation (demolition/relocation unknown)\n3. **EL-1.22** - Unclear if northern utility pole removed or remaining; if remaining and driveway nearby, relocation required\n4. **EL-1.31** - No surveyor mid-span clearance data when vertical clearances appear marginal\n\n**N/A ITEMS (Not Applicable):**\nEL-1.4, 1.11, 1.12, 1.15, 1.16, 1.20, 1.21, 1.34, 1.41, 1.44\n\n---\n\n**KEY ARCHITECTURAL/DOCUMENTATION GAPS:**\n- Building elevation sheets completely missing\n- Section/profile exhibits with clearance dimensions completely missing\n- Utility plan lacks conductor type labels, voltage, surveyed elevations\n- Grading plan lacks vertical clearance annotations for driveway crossings\n- Easement exhibit lacks down guy anchor easement boundaries\n- Cover sheet lacks required safety notification notes\n- Landscape plan tree species not confirmed as utility-compatible\n\nThis grouping requires substantial additional documentation and design changes to achieve compliance."}],"totalDurationMs":62301,"totalTokens":35502,"totalToolUseCount":5,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7978,"cache_read_input_tokens":21683,"output_tokens":5836,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7978},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777032493910,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MupsySqqAdrsRkrUNGq2Xk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! The agent has provided a thorough evaluation of all 47 checklist items. Now I need to compile this into the final structured output format required by the StructuredOutput tool.\n\nFrom the agent's analysis, the items that are FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE are:\n\n**FAIL items:**\n1. EL-1.7 - Building elevations with surveyed conductor elevations\n2. EL-1.8 - Section/profile exhibits with clearance dimensions\n3. EL-1.18 - Driveways vertical clearance (16 or 18 feet)\n4. EL-1.23 - Clearance dimensions measured from conductor\n5. EL-1.27 - Facilities under/over distribution lines (absolute prohibition)\n6. EL-1.37 - Trees within 10 lateral feet not utility-compatible\n7. EL-1.40 - Down guy wires conflicting with driveways\n8. EL-1.42 - Down guy anchor easements\n9. EL-1.45 - Construction staging clearances\n10. EL-1.46 - 48-hour notification note\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE items:**\n1. EL-1.1 - Buildings 7.5-foot clearance\n2. EL-1.2 - Customer facilities 15-foot radial\n3. EL-1.3 - Building projections clearances\n4. EL-1.5 - Stairs/walkways/platforms 15-foot radial\n5. EL-1.6 - Buildings in ROW clearances\n6. EL-1.9 - Fences 7.5-foot clearance\n7. EL-1.10 - Fence posts 10-foot from poles\n8. EL-1.13 - Vehicle barrier fencing clearance\n\n\n9. EL-1.14 - Retaining walls clearance\n10. EL-1.17 - Retaining wall section exhibits\n11. EL-1.19 - Vehicles parked/displayed clearance\n12. EL-1.22 - Poles in conflict with driveways (marked as fail due to discrepancy)\n13. EL-1.24 - Streetlight poles under overhead\n14. EL-1.25 - Sidewalks cleared from poles\n15. EL-1.26 - Trash enclosures under overhead\n16. EL-1.28 - Water meters clear\n17. EL-1.29 - Water lines clearance\n18. EL-1.30 - Foundations within 5 feet of property\n19. EL-1.31 - Surveyor data for marginal clearances\n20. EL-1.32 - Overhead line crossing angle\n21. EL-1.33 - Secondary over primary lines\n22. EL-1.35 - New poles spacing\n23. EL-1.36 - Decorative lighting clearance\n24. EL-1.38 - Meter locations obstructed\n25. EL-1.39 - Development clearances from streetlights\n26. EL-1.43 - Transformers vertical clearance\n27. EL-1.47 - Service-mast roof clearance\n\nNow filtering to focus only on items marked as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE rather than including the full list.\n\nFor FAIL items, I have solid evidence supporting: EL-1.7, 1.8, 1.18, 1.23, 1.27, 1.37, 1.45, 1.46, 1.42. Items like EL-1.40 and 1.22 show conflicting notes such as \"FAIL/MISSING DATA\" or \"UNCLEAR/POSSIBLE FAIL\" - these warrant inclusion as failures given the reasonable basis for non-compliance.\n\nFor NOT-VERIFIABLE, the most critical gaps are where required documentation is absent entirely (EL-1.1 through 1.3 and 1.31) or where the site plan lacks essential information (EL-1.6). I'll be selective and only report items with clear evidence of non-compliance or documentation gaps.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7063,"cache_read_input_tokens":65255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7063,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ef672522-d4e7-4b95-adea-0f34cf5c6c5b","uuid":"46079003-4acc-420f-8676-c4a3fd047742"}
