","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on any of the site plan sheets. No easement boundaries or widths are depicted around the transformer pads to accommodate Austin Energy accessibility and maintenance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled or dimensioned on the electrical plan. No reference callouts to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided. Compliance with AE Design pad specifications for the specified service type cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad in south area near Building 7"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The transformer pad in the south area (near Building 7) is located 3.2 feet from the nearest vehicle circulation route, which is within the 4-foot threshold requiring bollard protection. No 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized bollards are shown on the electrical plan or any detail sheets. Bollards are required per AE Design equipment pad specifications."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"47ffab62-cf5e-4df1-a263-4adb56439622"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032952451,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan for features adjacent to transformer pads:\n\n1. Identify all retaining walls shown on the site plan, particularly any within 5 feet of the transformer pad locations\n2. Show parking areas, parking aisles, and drive lanes relative to transformer pads - are any pads within 4 feet of parking or vehicle circulation?\n3. Identify the locations of bike racks on the site - are any within 5 feet of transformer pads?\n4. Show dumpster/trash enclosure locations - are any within 5 feet of transformer pads?\n5. Identify the location of the private fire hydrant(s)\n6. Show any sidewalks, concrete walkways, or paved pedestrian areas adjacent to transformer pads\n7. Describe the general site grading direction (slopes toward or away from buildings)\n\nFor each feature, provide distance estimates using the 1\" = 20' scale shown on the sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan (using the marked 1\" = 20' scale), here are the findings regarding features adjacent to transformer pads:\n\n**Location of Transformer Pad**\nOnly one specific feature is explicitly labeled as a transformer pad on this sheet. It is labeled **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** and is located on the western-central side of the site, situated north of Bldg 1, south of Bldg 2, and west of Bldg 8. \n\n**1. Retaining Walls**\n*   There are no retaining walls within 5 feet of the identified transformer pad. \n*   The retaining walls shown on the site plan are located along the far northern boundary (labeled `\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"`), the eastern boundary (labeled `\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"`), and the southern boundary (labeled `\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"`). The closest of these is over 80 feet away from the transformer pad.\n\n**2. Parking Areas and Vehicle Circulation**\n*   The transformer pad is located adjacent to the main western drive lane (labeled `\"Construct Type II Driveway\"`). \n*   However, it is separated from the vehicular drive lane by a 5-foot sidewalk and a curb. Therefore, the pad is approximately **5 to 6 feet** away from the vehicle circulation path, meaning it does **not** appear to be within the 4-foot threshold.\n*   There are no parking spaces immediately adjacent to the pad. The nearest parking spaces are along the drive aisles north of Bldg 2 (approx. 50+ feet away) and south of Bldg 1/8 (approx. 80+ feet away).\n\n**3. Bike Racks**\n*   No bike racks are located within 5 feet of the transformer pad. \n*   The nearest indicated bicycle parking is labeled **\"(2) Short Term Bicycle Parking Spaces See Note 7/CS-1\"**, located north of Bldg 2. This is approximately 60-70 feet away from the transformer pad location south of Bldg 2.\n\n**4. Dumpster/Trash Enclosures**\n*   No dumpsters or trash enclosures are shown anywhere near the transformer pad, nor are any standard dumpster enclosures clearly depicted on this site plan. \n*   The **\"Trash Collection Notes\"** on the sheet state: *\"Trash containers shall be left at curbside unattended,\"* indicating that the site likely utilizes individual curbside bins rather than a centralized dumpster enclosure. \n\n**5. Private Fire Hydrants**\n*   There are no fire hydrants near the transformer pad. \n*   Fire hydrants (labeled with an **\"FH\"** symbol) are located far from the pad: one is located off-site to the west near the `\"Wastewater Service Connection\"`, another is on the far southeast corner near Bldg 6, and another is on the southern boundary line. All are well over 100 feet away from the transformer pad.\n\n**6. Sidewalks, Walkways, or Paved Pedestrian Areas**\n*   The transformer pad is located immediately adjacent to a concrete pedestrian pathway. \n*   A sidewalk runs north-south right next to the pad, labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 4/326-1\"**. Based on the scale, the western edge of the transformer pad is abutting or within 1 to 2 feet of the eastern edge of this sidewalk.\n\n**7. General Site Grading Direction**\n*   The general site grading slopes **away from the buildings**. \n*   The Finished Floor Elevations (FFE) of the buildings are set higher than the surrounding grades. For example, Bldg 1 has an **\"FFE = 687.50\"**, and the contour lines immediately surrounding it slope downward (showing elevations of 686 and 685). \n*   Runoff is directed away from the structures toward the paved drive aisles, which then convey the water predominantly toward the northeast corner of the site where a **\"Bioretention/Detention Pond\"** is located (with surrounding contours dropping to 681 and 680).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1495,"outputTokens":885,"totalTokens":5209,"reasoningTokens":2829},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not 