{"level":30,"time":1777032968211,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Cx5puVRkzJysALspbWT5PH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! So the 48-hour notification requirement IS on the plans - it's in the Electric Transmission Notes section (Note 3). It specifically states: \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.\"\n\nNow let me assess the checklist items more thoroughly. Based on my research:\n\n**FINDINGS SO FAR:**\n\n1. **Existing overhead electric facilities**: Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions) clearly shows:\n   - Multiple utility poles on and adjacent to the property\n   - Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) running along the northern boundary and southern boundary\n   - Electric easements (5' easements on multiple boundaries, 15' easement on eastern side)\n\n2. **Proposed site plan**: Sheet 9 shows:\n   - 8 buildings with 25' setback from property lines\n   - Internal driveways/parking\n   - An overhead electric line (OHE) along the southern property line with utility poles\n   - NO clearance dimensions shown from overhead lines to buildings or structures\n\n3. **Electrical design**: Sheet 21 shows:\n   - All PROPOSED electrical service is UNDERGROUND (no conflicts with existing overhead lines)\n   - 3 transformer pads for the new service\n   - Meters on each building\n   - NO surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions shown from existing overhead utilities\n\n4. **Clearance issue analysis**:\n   - The checklist requires horizontal and vertical clearances from overhead conductors to buildings, structures, driveways, and parking\n   - The plans don't show measured clearances from the existing overhead conductors (on poles) to the proposed structures\n   - The plans don't show building elevation sections with conductor clearances\n   - The plans don't show profile sections through driveways with conductor clearances\n\n5. **48-hour notification**: Sheet 3 includes the required transmission line pre-construction meeting note (48 hours for Austin Energy), but the UCM § 1.10.2 requirement is for distribution lines as well, and the specific language references \"overhead lines\" which would include distribution lines.\n   \nLooking at the specific checklist requirements: EL-1.1 requires 7.5-foot horizontal clearance from building exteriors to overhead conductors, but the plans provide no surveyed conductor locations or measured setback dimensions to verify this. EL-1.2 calls for 15-foot radial clearance from certain structures, which also cannot be confirmed without conductor elevation data and clearance documentation on the plans.\n\nBuilding projections and overhangs aren't documented relative to conductor positions on the elevation sheets. The property borders Valley View Road where overhead utilities exist along the right-of-way, yet no clearance dimensions are shown. Notably, the building elevation sheets haven't been reviewed yet—these would be critical for verifying conductor locations and clearances. The site and electrical plans lack any dimensional callouts for clearances, and section views need to be examined to see if they contain this information. Vertical clearance requirements for driveways also need assessment. Looking at the elevation data, the buildings appear positioned away from the main overhead line along the southern boundary, though I can't fully confirm this without precise conductor locations and clearance measurements. The survey documentation by a registered surveyor for vertical clearances isn't present on the plans. The 48-hour notification requirement is documented on Sheet 3's Electric Transmission Notes, which satisfies that standard. I need to review the building elevation sheets to complete the full assessment.","signature":""}],