{"level":30,"time":1777032972757,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCHHKyGoHNpDucsast8T3F","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n     2→\n     3→Plan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n    11→* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n    12→* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n    13→* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n    14→* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n    15→* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n    16→* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n    17→* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n    18→* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n    19→* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n    20→* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    23→\n    24→* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n    25→* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n    26→* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n    27→* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n    28→* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n    29→* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n    30→* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n    31→* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"c060dc33-a35b-4dd0-8f81-1c91b1367639","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Wall Plan\n\nPlan view, section details, and notes for retaining walls.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet provides the structural details, plan view, and specifications for retaining walls, including a 14'-0\" maximum height retaining wall section. Its primary purpose is to guide the construction, reinforcement, and inspection of the site's retaining walls, footings, and associated slab tie-ins.\n\n**Key values**:\n* Maximum retaining wall height: 14'-0\"\n* Concrete compressive strength: 3,000 PSI (minimum 28-day)\n* Allowable soil bearing: 4,000 PSF\n* Active soil pressure (heel): 45.5 PSF\n* Passive pressure: 290 PSF\n* Soil weight: 130 PSF\n* Reinforcing steel grades: Grade 60 (for #4 rebar and larger), Grade 40 (for #3 rebar)\n* Wall vertical reinforcement: #7 @ 10\" O.C.\n* Wall horizontal reinforcement: #3 @ 12\" O.C. (each face)\n* Minimum concrete clear cover: 3\" for surfaces in contact with earth; 1 1/2\" for walls/footings adjacent to exterior/interior surfaces; 1 1/2\" above sub-grade for slabs\n* Dowel embedment: 6\" embedment for #6 rebar dowels into existing concrete\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n* **Block 2**: diagram — 14'-0\" Max Retaining Wall cross-section showing rebar spacing, gravel backfill, weep pipes, and geotextile placement. READ for exact rebar sizing and material specifications, VISION for structural layout and dimensions.\n* **Block 4**: drawing — Plan View showing the layout of the new and existing retaining walls, pond walls, and specific doweling instructions for an existing buttress. Use VISION to understand the spatial relationship, alignment, and construction phasing between new and existing walls.\n* **Block 1**: diagram — Dowel Detail showing a cross-section for tying a new slab to an existing slab with #6 rebar. READ for drill bit sizing (7/8\" for #4), epoxy installation instructions, and hand-installation notes.\n* **Block 3**: diagram — Typical Step in Footing elevation view showing standard 2'-0\" horizontal and 12\" vertical step dimensions. Use VISION for step geometry and reinforcement continuity.\n* **Block 10**: table — Design Criteria outlining IBC 2015 soil bearing and lateral pressure requirements. READ for the exact engineering design values.\n* **Block 6**: notes — General and structural notes detailing concrete specifications, clear cover minimums, and reinforcement rules. READ for material grades, cover depths, and corner bar requirements (24\"x24\").\n* **Block 9**: table — Required Inspections list. READ to confirm the three key inspection milestones (footings, walls, backfill/drainage).\n* **Blocks 5, 7, 8**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains a general schematic disclaimer (Block 5), title block data for project 3759 Valley View (Block 7), and engineer seals for MLAW Engineers (Block 8).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777032984533,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BwCKsnqWoJtWCw9MXc136r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The wall plan doesn't mention clearances from overhead electric utilities. Now let me compile my findings based on my comprehensive research:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n\n1. **Surveyed conductor elevations** - Not found on any sheet examined. The existing overhead utility poles and conductor locations are shown on Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions), but no surveyed elevations of the conductors are provided to enable vertical clearance verification.\n\n2. **Building elevation sheets** - Not included in the 39-sheet plan set. These would be required per EL-1.7 to show surveyed conductor elevations relative to buildings.\n\n3. **Horizontal clearance dimensions from conductors to buildings/structures** - Not found on Sheet 9 (Site Plan) or Sheet 21 (Electrical Design). Dimensions shown are from property lines or easement boundaries, not from the outside conductor location.\n\n4. **Vertical clearance dimensions for driveways** - Not found on Sheet 11 (Grading Plan). No dimensions showing vertical clearance from the overhead lines to the proposed driveway grades.\n\n5. **Section/profile exhibits showing conductor clearances** - Sheet 17 shows drainage conveyance sections, not electrical clearances. No other profile sheets were found showing conductor clearances.\n\n6. **Measurement from outside conductor** - Without surveyed conductor locations separate from the pole centerline, it's impossible to verify that clearances are measured from the outside conductor rather than the pole.\n\n7. **Transmission vs. Distribution distinction** - The existing facilities may include both transmission (external) and distribution (on-site), but the plans don't clearly distinguish which type of line runs where.\n\n## DEFICIENCIES IDENTIFIED:\n\nBased on the checklist items and the missing evidence, here are the key findings:\n\n**FAIL Items** (requirement not met, deficiency present):\n- **EL-1.7**: No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations\n\n\n- **EL-1.8**: Missing section and plan exhibits that dimension the distance between conductors and buildings/structures\n- **EL-1.23**: Clearance measurements not shown from the outside conductor itself, only from pole or centerline\n- **EL-1.31**: Surveyed conductor elevations absent, preventing vertical clearance verification\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE Items** (cannot confirm compliance):\n- **EL-1.1**: Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal clearance without conductor surveys and building setback dimensions from conductor\n- **EL-1.2**: Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance without conductor locations\n- **EL-1.6**: Cannot verify clearances for buildings adjacent to ROW without conductor surveys\n- **EL-1.18**: Cannot verify driveway vertical clearance (16-18 feet) without conductor elevation surveys\n- **EL-1.27**: Cannot verify facilities are not under/over distribution lines without precise conductor locations\n\n**PASS Items**:\n- **EL-1.46**: 48-hour notification note IS included on Sheet 3 (Electric Transmission Notes)\n\nMost remaining items are either not applicable to this project (no gas pumps, no transmission lines on-site with specific development within 100 feet triggering special analysis) or involve facilities not present in the plan. Need to confirm whether transmission lines exist and if the 100-foot proximity threshold applies to any requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":65590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"a1feb7a9-4c7b-4c1f-a5d9-0bb22bfab4a0"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032984696,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BwCKsnqWoJtWCw9MXc136r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review, let me now evaluate each checklist item systematically. Let me create a summary of my findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":65590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"5741f858-0306-4038-b835-7233b71a9dd6"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032985051,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ENb9MxpKNbTLw8q6U6SJwd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent measurements. The data shows a critical deficiency: the transformer pad between Buildings 4 and 5 is only 4.1 feet from the drive aisle, which means bollards are required but not shown on the plans. Let me now complete my research and evaluate all checklist items systematically.\n\nBased on my research, I have gathered the following evidence:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n### Transformer Pads Located on Site\nThe electrical plan (Sheet 21) shows **five transformer pads** at these locations:\n1. West side of Building 1 (near northwest property boundary)\n2. West side of Building 2\n3. West side of Building 8 (southwest area)\n4. Central area (between Buildings 4 and 5)\n5. Southeast area (between Buildings 6 and 7)\n\n### Key Measurements Completed\n- **Pad 1 (Bldg 1)**: 27.5 ft from building (PASS EL-13.1), 9.7 ft from drive aisle (no bollards needed)\n- **Pad 2 (Bldg 2)**: 49 ft from building (PASS EL-13.1), 8.3 ft from drive aisle (no bollards needed)\n- **Pad 3 (Bldg 8)**: 14.6 ft from building (PASS EL-13.1), 18.7 ft from drive aisle (no bollards needed)\n- **Pad 4 (Central Bldgs 4-5)**: 7.3 ft from Building 4 (PASS EL-13.1), **4.1 ft from drive aisle** (WITHIN 4-FT THRESHOLD - **REQUIRES BOLLARDS PER EL-13.38**)\n- **Pad 5 (SE Bldgs 6-7)**: 5.2 ft from Building 7 (AT minimum 5-ft threshold), 29.9 ft from drive aisle (no bollards needed)\n\n### Plan Documentation Issues\n- **NO transformer pad dimensions shown** on electrical plan (cannot verify EL-13.37)\n- **NO bollards shown or noted** on any transformer pad, especially critical for Pad 4 (EL-13.38 violation)\n- **NO transformer easements depicted** (EL-13.35)\n- **NO clearance dimensions marked** on electrical plan\n- **NO transformer pad detail sheets referenced** or attached (EL-13.37)\n- **NO specifications for service type** (single-phase vs. three-phase) visible on plans (EL-13.37)\n- **NO Austin Energy Design approval documents** provided\n- **Electrical routing shown on plans** appears to be on private property (likely PASS EL-13.36)\n\n### Applicability Assessment\nThis grouping is **APPLICABLE** to this project - five transformer pads are proposed and shown on the electrical plan (Sheet 21).\n\n### NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY\n- Transformer pad dimensions matching AE Design details (EL-13.37)\n- Transformer easements around pads (EL-13.35)\n- Bollard specifications and placement for pads within 4 feet of parking (EL-13.38) - **NOT SHOWN**\n- AE Design written approval documentation (if applicable for clearance reductions)\n- Fire rating verification for any reduced clearances (EL-13.4)\n- Transformer pad detail sheets from AE Design\n- Niche/confined space configuration documentation (not applicable - pads appear to be standard pad-mounted)\n- Oil-filled vs. dry-type equipment specifications (EL-13.32)\n- Grading/drainage direction verification around transformer pads (EL-13.32)\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:\n\n### Checklist Item Evaluation\n\n**EL-13.1** - Minimum 5-ft from buildings: **PASS** (measurements show 14.6-49 ft except Pad 5 at 5.2 ft, which is AT the minimum)\n\n**EL-13.2** - Retaining walls clearance: Not applicable (no retaining walls immediately adjacent to transformer pads, per site plan review)\n\n**EL-13.3** - Fence clearances: Not applicable (no fences immediately adjacent to transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.4** - Reduced 3-ft clearances with AE Design approval: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no AE Design approvals shown; Pad 5 is at 5.2 feet from Building 7, marginal to requirement)\n\n**EL-13.5** - Balconies/overhangs clearance: Not applicable (no balconies or overhangs directly above pads)\n\n**EL-13.6** - Windows/doors/ducts at low elevation: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no building elevations provided showing window/door locations and heights relative to transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.7** - Sidewalk clearance (minimum 2 ft): **PASS** (Pad 1 is 44.7 ft from back of sidewalk; others are adequate distance from any sidewalks)\n\n**EL-13.8** - Stairwells serving as fire exits: Not applicable (no stairwells marked as fire exits adjacent to pads on site plan)\n\n**EL-13.9** - Fire escapes (20-ft clearance for oil-filled): **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no indication whether transformers are oil-filled or dry-type; no fire escape locations shown on building plans; cannot verify drainage direction for oil-filled equipment)\n\n**EL-13.10** - Hot-stick use area clearance (min 10 ft to open area or building): **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (plans do not show access door orientation for any transformer pad, nor show the 10-foot work area boundary)\n\n**EL-13.11** - Confined space/niche clearance (35 ft vertical): Not applicable (pads appear to be standard pad-mounted, not in niches)\n\n**EL-13.12** - Fire hydrant clearance (5 ft): **PASS** (Pad 5 at 5.2 ft from fire hydrant - AT the minimum; Pad 4 at 23.2 ft - adequate distance)\n\n**EL-13.13** - Trees within 10 lateral ft must be utility-compatible: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (Sheet 31 landscape plan shows trees in the vicinity of transformer pads, but tree species identification and utility compatibility confirmation per ECM Appendix F not provided or verified)\n\n**EL-13.14** - Shrubs/vegetation clearance from transformer: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (sheet 31 shows vegetation but no dimensional clearances marked from transformer pads; access door orientation not identified)\n\n**EL-13.15** - Root barriers for trees within 20 lateral ft: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (root barrier details not shown on landscape or detail sheets; tree species near pads not verified as ECM Appendix F compliant)\n\n**EL-13.16** - Dumpster clearance (5 ft): Not applicable (dumpsters not shown on site plan near transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.17** - Bike rack clearance (5 ft): Not applicable (bike parking shown but not immediately adjacent to transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.18** - Light pole clearance (5 ft): Not applicable (light poles not shown immediately adjacent to transformer pads on electrical or site plan)\n\n**EL-13.19** - Fire lane clearance (15 ft): **PASS** (all transformer pads are set back adequately from the fire access lane; Pad 4 at 4.1 ft from drive aisle is still separate and not in the actual 24-26 ft wide fire lane)\n\n**EL-13.20** - Multiple transformer pad separation (5 ft): **PASS** (five pads are well-separated from each other)\n\n**EL-13.21-23** - Water/wastewater/storm drain clearance (5 ft): **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (utility plan sheets show water and sewer lines but no dimensioned clearances to transformer pads shown)\n\n**EL-13.24** - Gas line clearance (24-36 inches): Not applicable (no gas service shown on utility plans)\n\n**EL-13.25** - Other underground utilities (12-inch clearance): **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (utilities are shown on plans but no specific clearance dimensions marked from transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.26** - Utilities not over/under transformer pads: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (cannot confirm from available plans whether any utilities cross under or over pads)\n\n**EL-13.27** - Overhead distribution line clearance (7.5 ft sky-to-ground): **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no overhead lines shown on site plan; electrical is underground throughout site)\n\n**EL-13.28** - Overhead distribution conductors 15-ft radius: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no overhead distribution lines shown on utility plan; AT&T pad shown on plan but no overhead conductors depicted)\n\n**EL-13.29** - Niche vertical clearance (35 ft): Not applicable (no niche configurations shown)\n\n**EL-13.30** - Niche 3-hour fire walls: Not applicable (no niche service proposed)\n\n**EL-13.31** - Cross-section drawings for vertical clearances: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (no cross-sections provided showing transformer pad areas with vertical clearances to any overhead structures)\n\n**EL-13.32** - Grading/drainage from oil-filled pads: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (transformer type not specified on plans; grading plan shows general site drainage but no specific drainage flow direction marked relative to transformer pads)\n\n**EL-13.33** - Pads on private property, not in ROW: **PASS** (all pads shown on site plan within private property boundaries, not straddling property lines or in public ROW)\n\n**EL-13.34** - Pads not in prohibited easements: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** (easements shown on plans but no specific confirmation that transformer pads are outside of all prohibited easements; critical issue per facts.md regarding undepicted easements - Greenbelt Access & Use Easement and City of Austin Drainage Easement in NE corner where site features are being proposed)\n\n**EL-13.35** - Transformer easements shown, adequate width: **FAIL** (no transformer easements are depicted on any site plan, electrical plan, or easement exhibits; easement widths not specified)\n\n**EL-13.36** - Electrical routing 100% on private property: **PASS** (underground electric lines shown on Sheet 21 routing entirely through private property to buildings)\n\n**EL-13.37** - Transformer pad dimensions match AE Design details: **FAIL** (no transformer pad dimensions shown on plans; no AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets provided or referenced; pad dimensions cannot be verified against AE Design specifications)\n\n**EL-13.38** - Bollards for pads within 4 feet of parking/traffic: **FAIL** (transformer pad between Buildings 4 and 5 is 4.1 feet from central drive aisle and located adjacent to vehicle circulation route; no 4-inch diameter galvanized bollards are shown or noted on electrical plan or detail sheets)\n\n**EL-13.39** - Customer facilities not over/under overhead distribution: **PASS** (all infrastructure is underground; no customer facilities shown under or over any overhead distribution lines)\n\nNow let me compile the findings output with only the FAIL and NOT-VERIFIABLE items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72307,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":72307,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d6a22569-366b-4e39-9203-cc923425b52a","uuid":"b3c65943-697f-4d65-94d0-05e5b7b8bedc"}
{"level":30,"time":1777032986043,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BwCKsnqWoJtWCw9MXc136r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P5uac7J7Tm2Z4m53Xpkr9f","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Based on the existing conditions survey showing overhead utility poles and lines, please confirm:\n1. Are these overhead lines labeled as distribution (lower voltage, typically 12.47kV or 34.5kV) or transmission (60kV or higher)?\n2. What is the approximate distance from the closest utility pole on the property to the nearest proposed building location (refer to the property boundary and building positions on the survey)?\n3. Are there any voltage labels visible on poles or in legends identifying the line types?\n4. Are there guy wires or down guy anchors shown that would require easements?"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":11,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1264,"cache_read_input_tokens":65590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"9bcfc628-6986-47ea-9ec6-9cca29484eb4"}
