{"level":30,"time":1777033119318,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6YHiJ235JnwBjCqJYqFYg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n     2→\n     3→Provides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n    11→*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n    12→*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n    13→*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n    14→*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n    15→*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n    16→*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n    21→*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n    22→*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n    23→*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n    24→*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n    25→\n    26→**Plant List Schedules**\n    27→*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n    28→*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n    29→*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n    30→*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n    32→\n    33→**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n    34→*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n    35→*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n    36→*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n    37→*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n    38→*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n    39→\n    40→**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n    46→- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n    47→- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n    48→- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"9cc7b847-21b5-4a51-866d-f94c6e90d433","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-35/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n\nProvides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n\n**Plant List Schedules**\n*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n\n**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n\n**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
{"level":30,"time":1777033158930,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BuqN1NNEmtPXCdsVUAoTVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! Sheet 35 shows that proposed trees include:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.)\n- 2 Live Oak (100 gal.)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n\nNow I need to determine if these species are on the ECM Appendix F \"Utility Compatible\" list. Based on the grouping description, utility-compatible trees are generally species with mature height ≤20 feet that are marked \"UC\" in ECM Appendix F.\n\nHowever, I need to check if Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, or Texas Mountain Laurel are utility-compatible species. Without access to the actual ECM Appendix F list, I cannot definitively say whether these are utility-compatible or not.\n\nWhat I CAN say is:\n1. Trees are proposed on the landscape plan (Sheet 31)\n2. Some trees appear to be within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric line on the southern boundary\n3. I don't have verification of whether the proposed species are utility-compatible\n\nThis is a NOT-VERIFIABLE situation - the requirement cannot be fully assessed because I don't have the ECM Appendix F plant list to verify utility compatibility.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The vision analysis of Sheet 31 found that trees (marked \"M\" for Mitigation and \"PL\" for Parking Lot) are shown within 10-15 feet of the overhead electric line. But I haven't confirmed:\n1. The exact distance - is it within 10 feet (distribution) or 50 feet (transmission)?\n2. The species of these specific trees\n3. Whether they are utility-compatible\n\nThe landscape plan doesn't identify tree species by location, only by category (M, PL, ST, P). To properly evaluate EL-1.37, I would need either:\n- A detailed schedule mapping each landscape symbol to a species\n\n\n- Or a zoomed-in detail showing tree species near the overhead line\n- Plus confirmation of utility-compatible status\n\nSo this appears to be NOT-VERIFIABLE for EL-1.37 because while trees are proposed near the overhead line, their species and utility-compatible status cannot be confirmed from the available documents.\n\nActually, I should be more careful. Let me think about what I can actually verify:\n\nFrom Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan vision analysis):\n- Trees are shown within 10-15 feet of the OHE line on the southern boundary\n- These trees are labeled as \"M\" (Mitigation) and \"PL\" (Parking Lot) type trees\n- Tree species are not labeled on the plan itself, only categorized by function\n\nThe species list from Sheet 35 exists, but there's no way to match which specific trees near the overhead line correspond to which species. Without that connection and without access to verify utility compatibility against ECM Appendix F, I cannot confirm compliance with EL-1.37.\n\nFor the remaining items: EL-1.3 requires building elevation sheets I don't have. EL-1.14 shows retaining walls on Sheet 38 but lacks clearance dimensions from overhead conductors. EL-1.25 displays sidewalks on Sheet 9 but needs additional information to assess pole conflicts.\n\nExamining EL-1.14 more closely, the retaining walls are positioned around the site perimeter and biofiltration pond, with the overhead line along the southern edge. Without surveyed conductor locations, I can't verify the 7.5-foot clearance requirement. For EL-1.25, sidewalks run along the western frontage and internally, with utility poles shown on Sheet 4 along multiple boundaries. The site plan indicates sidewalks are spaced away from poles, though I'd need to confirm the exact distances to verify compliance. the exact spacing between poles and sidewalk isn't shown with dimensions. EL-1.25 appears not verifiable without precise measurements.\n\nLooking at what's missing, I need to identify the key deficiencies: no building elevations with surveyed conductor heights, no section or plan views showing clearance dimensions measured from the actual conductor, and no vertical clearance data. The items that fail outright are EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23, and EL-1.31. Several others—including EL-1.1, EL-1.2, and EL-1.25—cannot be confirmed without the conductor survey information and precise dimensional callouts.\n\nI should also check which items actually apply to this project. Going back through the checklist more carefully, I need to determine applicability for each standard before categorizing it as pass, fail, or not-verifiable.\n\nFor EL-1.1, buildings are proposed with overhead facilities present, so this applies. However, I can't verify the 7'6\" horizontal clearance since there are no conductor elevations or clearance dimensions shown.\n\nEL-1.2 also applies—customer facilities and distribution lines are both present—but I lack the conductor locations and radial clearance measurements needed to verify the 15-foot requirement.\n\nEL-1.3 requires building elevation sheets to assess projections, which haven't been provided, so I can't determine if this standard is even applicable or verifiable.\n\nGas pump canopies don't appear in the proposal, so EL-1.4 is not applicable. The walkways shown are ground-level surfaces rather than elevated structures, making EL-1.5 not applicable as well.\n\nBuildings 1 and 2 sit adjacent to Valley View Road's right-of-way with overhead utilities present, triggering EL-1.6, but clearance dimensions from conductors to building faces are missing. EL-1.7 fails outright—no building elevation sheets exist in the plan set to show surveyed elevations. Similarly, EL-1.8 fails because the available sheets lack dimension lines indicating clearances between conductors and building edges.\n\nFor EL-1.9 regarding fence clearances, I need to review what fencing is actually proposed.\n\nWooden privacy fences are referenced in the landscape notes on Sheet 35 with Key Note H.6, and the site plan shows fencing around the perimeter. The site plan also indicates a proposed fence line near the southern boundary where the overhead utility line runs, with tree canopies appearing to intersect or nearly intersect that utility corridor. If fences are proposed, EL-1.10 becomes applicable—fence posts must maintain 10 feet from poles—but exact measurements of post locations relative to poles aren't provided, making it not-verifiable.\n\nRetaining walls shown on Sheets 38-39 trigger EL-1.14, though clearance dimensions from overhead conductors to the walls are absent. Driveways are proposed, making EL-1.18 applicable, but vertical clearance dimensions from overhead lines to driveway grades aren't documented. EL-1.23 fails because clearance dimensions are measured from property lines rather than from the actual conductor locations.\n\nPublic sidewalk runs along the western frontage per the site plan, but EL-1.25 clearance cannot be verified without measurements. Distribution facilities and easements exist, so EL-1.27 applies, though conductor routing surveys would be needed to confirm buildings aren't beneath them. EL-1.31 fails—no surveyed conductor elevations appear on any sheet. Tree species near the overhead line cannot be determined from the landscape plan labels, so EL-1.37 cannot be verified. EL-1.46 passes; the 48-hour notification note is included on Sheet 3.\n\nThe failures are: no building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations (EL-1.7), no section/plan exhibits with clearance dimensions (EL-1.8), clearance dimensions not measured from the outside conductor (EL-1.23), and no surveyed conductor elevations for vertical clearance verification (EL-1.31). Seven items remain not-verifiable due to missing measurements or documentation. I'm identifying four items that fail the requirements: EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.23, and EL-1.31. Ten items cannot be verified without additional surveys or site-specific data—including clearance measurements, building projections, retaining walls, fence posts, and tree compatibility assessments. One item passes: EL-1.46. This accounts for 15 of the 47 checklist items, with the remaining 32 either not applicable to the project scope or requiring more detailed review.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":75802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1800,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"b47d105c-da15-40bb-82ce-a4b7a8078ea9"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033162137,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BuqN1NNEmtPXCdsVUAoTVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the Valley View Townhomes site plan, I have evaluated all applicable checklist items in the EL-MD-EXP grouping regarding overhead electric clearances. Let me now prepare my findings.\n\n## RESEARCH PHASE SUMMARY - NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY\n\n**Missing Evidence:**\n1. **Building elevation sheets** - Not included in the 39-sheet plan set; required to show surveyed conductor elevations per EL-1.7\n2. **Surveyed conductor elevations** - No registered surveyor data for existing overhead utility conductor heights on any sheet\n3. **Clearance dimensions from outside conductor** - No dimension lines from the actual conductor location (outside edge) to buildings, structures, driveways, or site features\n4. **Section/profile exhibits for clearances** - No cross-section views showing vertical clearances from overhead conductors to proposed site features\n5. **Tree species cross-reference** - Landscape plan locations cannot be matched to proposed tree species from the plant list schedule\n6. **Fence and pole documentation** - Exact measurements of fence/post locations relative to utility poles not dimensioned\n7. **Driveway/parking clearance profiles** - No vertical clearance annotations on grading plan for areas under overhead lines\n\n**Existing Evidence Found:**\n- Overhead utility lines confirmed on Existing Conditions Survey (Sheet 4) along northern and southern property boundaries\n- Electric easements marked: 5-foot electric easements on multiple boundaries\n- 48-hour pre-construction notification requirement included on General Notes (Sheet 3)\n- Proposed buildings, driveways, sidewalks, retaining walls, and landscaping all positioned and documented\n- Proposed electrical service is underground (no conflict with existing overhead lines)\n\nNow I will return my findings structured output:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":75802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1800,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"d26d56a2-87a3-4067-bfc6-084b2d803afb"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033191605,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BuqN1NNEmtPXCdsVUAoTVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TQuA5HLVMUUca5jqjVTm1S","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8","Primary site plan area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on the property (shown on Sheet 4 existing survey), and buildings are proposed (Sheets 9, 21). However, no surveyed conductor elevations or horizontal clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to any building faces are provided. Measurement from conductor location (not pole centerline) required to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be determined without surveyor data showing conductor position relative to building setbacks."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8","All customer facilities and installations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Distribution overhead conductors shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4); buildings and facilities proposed throughout site (Sheets 9, 21). Without surveyed conductor locations and radial clearance dimensions, the 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor in all directions cannot be verified. No profile drawings show radial clearance envelopes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Building projections where overhead facilities present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet plan set, preventing verification of overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, or patios relative to overhead conductors. Both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for building projections cannot be assessed."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1 and 2 adjacent to Valley View Road right-of-way"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead utility lines exist in the right-of-way along Valley View Road (western boundary per Sheet 4), and buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance (Sheet 9). No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions from outside conductor to buildings are provided, preventing verification of required 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings 1-8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are not included in the submitted site plan. The 39-sheet plan set contains no building elevation drawings. Per UCM § 1.10.3, engineered, sealed elevation drawings showing vertical relationships between overhead conductors and buildings, including all projections, with dimensioned clearances are required."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All buildings 1-8 and site structures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) show building locations and site features, but contain no dimension lines or annotations showing distances from outer electric conductors to building edges, projections, or other site features. Required section views and enlarged plan details with dimension lines originating from the outside conductor location are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed fence post locations throughout property perimeter"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fences are proposed (noted on landscape plan Sheet 31 and landscape calculations Sheet 35), including wooden privacy fences. Existing utility poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) at multiple property boundaries. Without exact measured distances between proposed fence post locations and existing pole locations, the 10-foot minimum horizontal clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls throughout site perimeter and around detention pond"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are detailed on Sheets 38-39, and overhead electric facilities exist on property boundaries (Sheet 4). However, no dimension lines or clearance annotations show distances from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of any retaining wall. Horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductors to wall faces cannot be verified without surveyor data and section exhibits."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Internal driveways, parking areas with overhead electric line proximity"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Internal driveways and parking areas are proposed (Sheets 9, 11). Overhead utility lines exist on property boundaries (Sheet 4). No vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead conductors (including any attachments) to finished driveway/parking grades are provided. Verification of 16-foot minimum (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (areas with truck traffic) clearance requires surveyed conductor elevation data and grading section exhibits not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All overhead electric clearance areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Dimension lines and clearance annotations on submitted plans show distances from property lines, easement boundaries, and pole locations, but do not originate from the outside conductor location. Per UCM § 1.10.3 and the measurement methodology in the regulatory overview, all clearances must be measured from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from utility pole centerline or easement boundaries. On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension lines must explicitly show origin at conductor position."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Public sidewalk along Valley View Road right-of-way, property end locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Existing utility poles are shown on Sheet 4 along the western property line within right-of-way. A public sidewalk is proposed along Valley View Road frontage (Sheet 9). Without dimensioned drawings showing exact clearance distances from sidewalk location to pole positions at each property end along right-of-way, the requirement cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8, all site features, electric easement areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines and electric easements (5-foot easements) are shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4). Buildings are positioned within electric easement areas on the site plan (Sheet 9). Without surveyed conductor routing and exact clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to all buildings and site features within the easement, it cannot be definitively verified that customer facilities are not installed beneath or over distribution conductors (absolute prohibition per UCM § 1.10.3) or that 7.5-foot clearance is maintained for items within easements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All structures with potential overhead conductor clearance concerns"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span conductor clearances is provided on any submitted sheet. The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows surveyed pole locations, but no conductor elevation data. When overhead facilities cross proposed site features (buildings, driveways, parking), surveyed mid-span clearance measurements are required to verify vertical clearances meet minimum requirements. These measurements are absent from the plan set."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead electric line on southern property boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed trees (marked 'M' for Mitigation and 'PL' for Parking Lot types) positioned within approximately 10-15 feet of the overhead electric line on the southern property boundary. The landscape calculations (Sheet 35) provide a plant list (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but the specific tree species cannot be cross-referenced to the landscape plan location symbols. Without confirmed species identification for the trees near the overhead line, utility-compatible status cannot be verified against ECM Appendix F. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors must be utility-compatible species (generally mature height ≤20 feet marked 'UC')."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"pass","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Pre-construction coordination for all work near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"General Notes (Sheet 3) include Electric Transmission Notes, Note 3, which requires: 'A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.' This satisfies the requirement that plans include notice requiring owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1800,"cache_read_input_tokens":75802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1800,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6f95fbc-fee7-4452-ac99-d9c79c3e8cef","uuid":"86a2ad9f-c5dc-454c-9f1f-e5e999907acd"}
