s and drainage management.\n\n### Group F: Building Proximity, Windows, and Doors\n- Part of 13:EL-13.6 (already above)\n\nI need to verify whether 13:EL-13.6 was already captured in Group A. Checking the earlier grouping, it appears the comment about building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations may have been included there.\n\nLooking more carefully at the specific requirement: building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations, heights from grade, and lateral separation distances relative to transformer pads are not provided. Cannot verify compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement when windows/doors are less than 12 feet from grade or have less than 5-foot lateral separation.\n\nThis is distinct from Group A's focus on AE Design-approved pad details and easements. This specifically requires building elevation documentation to verify the 12-foot clearance and 5-foot lateral separation standards for windows and doors.\n\n### Group A: Missing AE Design Documentation and Easements\n- 13:EL-13.37 — Transformer pad dimensions and AE Design detail sheets (3 runs)\n- 13:EL-13.35 — Transformer easements not depicted (2 runs)\n- 13:EL-13.4 — Reduced clearance requires AE Design approval docs (1 run)\n\n### Group B: Building-Related Clearances (Windows, Doors, Ducts)\n- 13:EL-13.6 — Building elevation drawings not provided; cannot verify 12-foot clearance to windows/doors (1 run)\n\n### Group C: Horizontal Clearances to Utilities\n- 13:EL\n\n-13.21 — Water line clearances (2 runs: 1 fail, 1 nv)\n- 13:EL-13.22 — Wastewater clearances (2 runs: 1 fail, 1 nv)\n- 13:EL-13.23 — Storm drain clearances (1 run: nv)\n- 13:EL-13.25 — Multiple underground utility clearances (1 run: nv)\n\n### Group D: Vertical Clearances and Utility Cross-Sections\n- 13:EL-13.31 — Vertical clearances to structures and parking (2 runs: both nv)\n- 13:EL-13.26 — Vertical relationships of utilities in profiles (1 run: nv)\n\n#