the required 20-foot horizontal clearance from fire escapes.\"}\n  ]\n\nDetail 3 (13:EL-13.32):\n- Text: \"Equipment type specification (oil-filled or dry-type) is missing from transformer data. Grading plan shows general site drainage but does not mark drainage flow direction specifically at pad locations. Surface drainage slope direction away from buildings cannot be verified for oil-filled equipment.\"\n- Citation: \"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1\"\n- SourceId: \"13:EL-13.32\"\n- Confidence: 1 (flagged in 1/3 runs)\n- RunCom\n\nments: [\n    {runNum: 2, status: \"nv\", comment: \"Transformer specifications lack identification of whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan indicates general site drainage patterns but does not specify drainage flow direction at transformer pad locations. Unable to verify that surface drainage slopes direct liquid flow away from buildings as required for oil-filled transformers per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1.\"}\n  ]\n\n---\n\n### Comment 5: Vehicle Collision Protection (Bollards)\n\n**Finding:**\n- 13:EL-13.38 (2 runs: both f)\n\n**Sheets:** [21]\n\n**Applicable Area:** \"Site Interior\"\n\n**Severity:** 3 (High) — Missing bollard protection for transformer equipment within 4-foot vehicle-proximity zone is a safety violation.\n\n**Confidence:** 3 (All runs flagged)\n\n**CrossDep:** \"\" (No cross-department issues; this is a within-scope electrical utility requirement)\n\n**Attn:** \"\" (Not flagged;\n\nclear violation)\n\n**Headline:** \"Missing bollard protection for vehicle-proximate transformer pads\"\n\n**Summary:** Two transformer pads sit within 4 feet of vehicle routes and require 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post bollards per AE Design standards, but none are shown or specified.\n\n**Details:**\n\nDetail 1 (13:EL-13.38):\nThe transformer pad between Buildings 4–5 is 4.1 feet from the central drive aisle, and the pad south of Building 7 is 3.2 feet from the nearest vehicle ci