s, installation methods, or verification that the required 4-foot deep barriers will be placed 5 feet from the equipment.\n\n---\n\n## Final Verification\n\nLet me count the findings:\n1. 13:EL-13.37 ✓\n2. 13:EL-13.35 ✓\n3. 13:EL-13.4 ✓\n4. 13:EL-13.34 ✓\n5. 13:EL-13.6 ✓\n6. 13:EL-13.21 ✓\n7. 13:EL-13.22 ✓\n8. 13:EL-13.23 ✓\n9. 13:EL-13.25 ✓\n10. 13:EL-13.31 ✓\n11. 13:EL-13.26 ✓\n12. 13:EL-13.10 ✓\n13. 13:EL-13.9 ✓\n14. 13:EL-13.32 ✓\n15. 13:EL-13.38 ✓\n16. 13:EL-13.13 ✓\n17. 13:EL-13.14 ✓\n18. 13:EL-13.15 ✓\n\nAll 18 findings accounted for. Comment distribution shows 4, 1, 6, 3, 1, and 3 findings across six comments respectively. Now I need to verify the sheet assignments and refine Comment 2 since it contains only one finding, then construct the final JSON output. For each comment's sheet list, I need to consolidate the sheets across all related findings. Comment 1 should include sheets [9, 21] covering the electrical and facts findings. Comment 2 applies only to sheet [21]. Comment 3 spans sheets [11, 19, 21] across the utility, site, and grading plan findings. Comment 4 covers sheets [11, 21] from the electrical and grading findings. Comment 5 is limited to sheet [21]. Comment 6 encompasses sheets [31, 32] for the landscape plan findings. Let me verify I'm capturing all sheets mentioned across the related findings without missing any. For each detail, I'm assigning confidence based on how many runs flagged it: 3 if all runs caught it, 2 for majority agreement, 1 if only a single run identified it.\n\nComment 1 breaks down to confidence 3 for 13:EL-13.37, confidence 2 for 13:EL-13.35, and confidence 1 for both 13:EL-13.4 and 13:EL-13.34. Averaging these gives 1.75, which rounds to a holistic confidence of 2.\n\nComment 2 has only one detail flagged by a single run, so confidence stays at 1.\n\nComment 3 starts with 13:EL-13.21 flagged by multiple runs, so that gets confidence 3, and I need to continue evaluating the remaining details in this comment.\n\n13:EL-13.