{"level":30,"time":1777033365887,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HoVEUDveZsLspeLMhdr9LE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll synthesize these 18 findings into a consolidated set of structured comments. This is clearly an **electrical utility discipline** review focused on transformer pad placement, clearances, and infrastructure coordination.\n\n## Consolidation Strategy\n\nWith 18 atomic findings, I'm targeting ~5-6 comments (roughly 1 comment per 3-4 findings). I'll merge findings that share regulatory sections and corrective actions:\n\n1. **AE Design Documentation & Easements** (4 findings: 13:EL-13.37, 35, 4, 34)\n2. **Building Elevation Documentation** (1 finding: 13:EL-13.6)\n3. **Utility Infrastructure Clearances** (6 findings: 13:EL-13.21, 22, 23, 25, 31, 26)\n4. **Transformer Pad Operations** (3 findings: 13:EL-13.10, 9, 32)\n5. **Bollard Protection** (1 finding: 13:EL-13.38)\n6. **Landscape Coordination** (3 findings: 13:EL-13.13, 14, 15)\n\n**All 18 findings preserved across 6 comments = 3:1 consolidation ratio.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21944,"cache_read_input_tokens":29600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21944,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e2934ff-0759-4870-a3d7-145fd8d18929","uuid":"f4b8a8af-cab2-4e1f-9def-76d23e5ae9c9"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033373621,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CXbo2tt5FKBtrKpv8R8s4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've successfully synthesized the 19 consolidated electrical utility findings into 5 structured review comments. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Synthesis Summary\n\n**Input:** 19 electrical utility findings across 6 checklist items (EL-1.1, EL-1.2, EL-1.3, EL-1.6, EL-1.7, EL-1.8, EL-1.10, EL-1.14, EL-1.18, EL-1.22, EL-1.23, EL-1.25, EL-1.27, EL-1.31, EL-1.37, EL-1.40, EL-1.42, EL-1.45, EL-1.46)\n\n**Output:** 5 structured comments\n\n**Consolidation ratio:** 19:5 = 3.8:1 (target was ~4:1) ✓\n\n**Coverage:** 100% — every input finding appears exactly once in a comment's details array.\n\n### Comments Produced:\n\n1. **Missing surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions** (8 details)\n   - Consolidates EL-1.1, 1.3, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8, 1.23, 1.27, 1.31\n   - Severity: 3 (High)\n   - Confidence: 3 (all aspects flagged across multiple runs)\n\n2. **Missing vertical clearance verification for driveways and transformer** (2 details)\n   - Consolidates EL-1.2, 1.18\n   - Severity: 3 (High)\n   - Confidence: 3 (both elements have consistent findings)\n\n3. **Proposed trees lack utility-compatible species designation** (1 detail)\n   - EL-1.37 (standalone)\n   - Severity: 2 (Medium)\n   - Confidence: 3 (consistently flagged across all runs)\n\n4. **Utility pole locations, guy wires, and associated clearances undocumented** (6 details)\n   - Consolidates EL-1.10, 1.14, 1.22, 1.25, 1.40, 1.42\n   - Severity: 2 (Medium)\n   - Confidence: 1 (low — each detail from single run; represents infrastructure documentation gaps)\n\n5. **Missing construction safety notifications and staging area clearances** (2 details)\n   - Consolidates EL-1.45, 1.46\n   - Severity: 2 (Medium)\n   - Confidence: 2 (EL-1.46 flagged consistently; EL-1.45 appeared in limited runs)\n\nAll findings fall within Utility discipline scope and require coordination with Austin Energy, City Arborist, and Safety/Construction Administration. Low-confidence items and areas needing clarification are marked for follow-up.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14231,"cache_read_input_tokens":31748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14231,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4bead79-d9ad-4687-a843-03346abdd75e","uuid":"6378d845-ab1b-42fa-9385-13262f23e9c3"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033376456,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CXbo2tt5FKBtrKpv8R8s4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've synthesized the 19 input findings into **5 structured review comments** with an effective consolidation ratio of **3.8:1** (19 findings → 5 comments).\n\n## Synthesis Overview\n\n**Discipline:** Electrical Utility (all findings Tier 1 — within scope)\n\n**Key consolidations:**\n1. **8 findings** merged into \"Missing surveyed conductor elevations…\" (buildings, structures, transformer, prohibition on facilities under conductors)\n2. **2 findings** merged into \"Missing vertical clearance verification…\" (driveways, transformer pad)\n3. **1 finding** standalone: Utility-compatible landscaping (distinct element, single source)\n4. **6 findings** merged into \"Utility pole locations, guy wires…\" (pole positioning, guy wires, easements, fence/wall/sidewalk clearances)\n5. **2 findings** merged into \"Missing construction safety notifications…\" (48-hour notification, staging area clearances)\n\n## Coverage & Quality\n\n- **100% coverage** — every input finding appears exactly once in a comment's `details` array\n- **All per-run data preserved** — each detail carries the original run comments (status, agent text) verbatim\n- **Discipline-consistent framing** — all comments written from electrical utility perspective\n- **Severity appropriately scaled:** High (comments 1–2: critical clearance documentation gaps blocking approval), Medium (comments 3–5: substantive deficiencies or infrastructure documentation gaps)\n- **Cross-department flags** identify coordination with Austin Energy, City Arborist, Safety/Construction Admin\n- **Low-confidence flags** mark single-run findings (Comment 4) and recommend verification actions\n\nThe output is ready for downstream section assignment and reviewer rendering."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14231,"cache_read_input_tokens":31748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14231,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4bead79-d9ad-4687-a843-03346abdd75e","uuid":"980f78f9-58bb-4ad5-b062-6ba36b603fe8"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033376840,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"1.json","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":146802,"duration_api_ms":146654,"num_turns":2,"result":"I've synthesized the 19 input findings into **5 structured review comments** with an effective consolidation ratio of **3.8:1** (19 findings → 5 comments).\n\n## Synthesis Overview\n\n**Discipline:** Electrical Utility (all findings Tier 1 — within scope)\n\n**Key consolidations:**\n1. **8 findings** merged into \"Missing surveyed conductor elevations…\" (buildings, structures, transformer, prohibition on facilities under conductors)\n2. **2 findings** merged into \"Missing vertical clearance verification…\" (driveways, transformer pad)\n3. **1 finding** standalone: Utility-compatible landscaping (distinct element, single source)\n4. **6 findings** merged into \"Utility pole locations, guy wires…\" (pole positioning, guy wires, easements, fence/wall/sidewalk clearances)\n5. **2 findings** merged into \"Missing construction safety notifications…\" (48-hour notification, staging area clearances)\n\n## Coverage & Quality\n\n- **100% coverage** — every input finding appears exactly once in a comment's `details` array\n- **All per-run data preserved** — each detail carries the original run comments (status, agent text) verbatim\n- **Discipline-consistent framing** — all comments written from electrical utility perspective\n- **Severity appropriately scaled:** High (comments 1–2: critical clearance documentation gaps blocking approval), Medium (comments 3–5: substantive deficiencies or infrastructure documentation gaps)\n- **Cross-department flags** identify coordination with Austin Energy, City Arborist, Safety/Construction Admin\n- **Low-confidence flags** mark single-run findings (Comment 4) and recommend verification actions\n\nThe output is ready for downstream section assignment and reviewer rendering.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e4bead79-d9ad-4687-a843-03346abdd75e","total_cost_usd":0.14110954999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":21,"cache_creation_input_tokens":45979,"cache_read_input_tokens":31748,"output_tokens":16088,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":45979},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":21,"outputTokens":16088,"cacheReadInputTokens":31748,"cacheCreationInputTokens":45979,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.14110954999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimensions","summary":"Overhead electric lines are present on and adjacent to the site. Buildings and site structures lack surveyed conductor elevation data and dimensioned clearances required to verify horizontal (7.5-foot sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial) and vertical clearances per UCM § 1.10.3. Building elevation sheets and section/profile exhibits with conductor measurements are absent. Additionally, code prohibits installing customer facilities directly under or over distribution conductors—this cannot be verified without surveyed conductor routing.","sheets":[4,9,21,31],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordination with Austin Energy required to provide registered surveyor mid-span clearance measurements and conductor routing; may necessitate conductor relocation or building repositioning.","attn":"Verify whether overhead electric line on northern boundary (shown on Sheet 4 existing survey) is intended to be removed, relocated, or left in place. Current site plan (Sheet 9) omits this pole location entirely, creating ambiguity about design intent.","details":[{"text":"Buildings proposed near overhead lines on property boundaries lack surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions on building elevations or plans. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.1","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Buildings are proposed on site with overhead electric lines on adjacent property boundaries. No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions are shown on building elevation sheets or plan views to verify the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained. Clearance verification exhibits are required."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric lines exist on the property (shown on Sheet 4 existing survey), and buildings are proposed (Sheets 9, 21). However, no surveyed conductor elevations or horizontal clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to any building faces are provided. Measurement from conductor location (not pole centerline) required to verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be determined without surveyor data showing conductor position relative to building setbacks."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Building locations shown on site plan with overhead electric line on southern boundary. No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed conductor elevations or roof/eave elevations. Cannot verify 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance is maintained without these essential elevation views and dimension callouts."}]},{"text":"Building projections (overhangs, eaves, balconies, roofs, patios) not shown on elevation sheets relative to overhead conductors. Required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from projections cannot be assessed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.3","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the 39-sheet plan set, preventing verification of overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, roofs, or patios relative to overhead conductors. Both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for building projections cannot be assessed."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing projections (overhangs, eaves, balconies, roofs, patios). Cannot verify required 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from building projections without elevation views."}]},{"text":"Buildings 1 and 2 positioned within clearance distance of overhead utilities on Valley View Road right-of-way and northern boundary. Existing utilities shown on Sheet 4 but omitted from proposed site plan (Sheet 9) with no notation of removal, relocation, or retention. No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.6","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead utility lines exist in the right-of-way along Valley View Road (western boundary per Sheet 4), and buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance (Sheet 9). No surveyed conductor elevations or clearance dimensions from outside conductor to buildings are provided, preventing verification of required 7.5-foot and 15-foot clearances."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) documents overhead utility line on-site along northern property boundary. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) omits northern overhead utilities with no demolition, relocation, or undergrounding notes. Cannot verify building setbacks from ROW and relocated facilities when existing utilities are not accounted for in proposed plan."}]},{"text":"No building elevation sheets included in 39-sheet plan set showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimension callouts to building faces and projections. Required engineered, sealed elevation drawings demonstrating vertical clearances are absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.7","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Building elevation sheets do not include surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors. Clearance verification requires registered surveyor data showing conductor elevations and clearance dimensions to building faces and projections. This is a required element per UCM § 1.10.3."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations and clearance dimension annotations are not included in the submitted site plan. The 39-sheet plan set contains no building elevation drawings. Per UCM § 1.10.3, engineered, sealed elevation drawings showing vertical relationships between overhead conductors and buildings, including all projections, with dimensioned clearances are required."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No building elevation sheets are included in the site plan set showing surveyed overhead conductor elevations or clearance dimensions to building faces and projections. This is a critical missing document type explicitly required by code to demonstrate vertical clearances from overhead electric conductors are met."}]},{"text":"Section and plan view exhibits lack dimensions originating from outside conductor to building edges and projections. Clearance dimension lines must extend from outer conductor (not pole centerline or multi-conductor centerline). None provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.8","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from the outer electric conductor to the outermost edge of buildings, building projections, or other site features. Clearance dimension annotations must originate from the outside conductor (not pole centerline) and extend to building edges and projections."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan (Sheet 9) and electrical design plan (Sheet 21) show building locations and site features, but contain no dimension lines or annotations showing distances from outer electric conductors to building edges, projections, or other site features. Required section views and enlarged plan details with dimension lines originating from the outside conductor location are not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No section or profile exhibits provided showing clearance dimensions from outer conductor to building edges, projections, or other site features. Plans show buildings and overhead lines in plan view only with no cross-section documentation of vertical and horizontal relationships or clearance dimensions."}]},{"text":"No clearance dimensions shown on any plan sheets. All required dimensions must originate from outside conductor location; on multi-conductor installations, outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension methodology absent.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.23","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"No clearance dimensions are shown on any plan sheets. Where clearances are required to be dimensioned, the dimension lines must extend from the outside conductor (not from utility pole centerline or pole structure). On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Dimension lines and clearance annotations on submitted plans show distances from property lines, easement boundaries, and pole locations, but do not originate from the outside conductor location. Per UCM § 1.10.3 and the measurement methodology in the regulatory overview, all clearances must be measured from the outside conductor (the actual electric wire), not from utility pole centerline or easement boundaries. On multi-conductor installations, the outermost conductor may be several feet offset from pole center. Dimension lines must explicitly show origin at conductor position."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Plans show overhead lines but provide no clearance dimension callouts measuring distances from features to overhead conductors. Code requires clearance dimensions extend from outside conductor (not pole centerline or centerline of multi-conductor lines), yet no dimensions are provided to verify this measurement methodology. Cannot verify compliance when dimensions are completely absent."}]},{"text":"Code establishes absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities (buildings, driveways, structures) under or over Austin Energy distribution conductors. Plans show buildings and driveways near/under overhead lines with no explicit documentation confirming facilities are not placed directly beneath/over conductors.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.27","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead distribution lines and electric easements (5-foot easements) are shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4). Buildings are positioned within electric easement areas on the site plan (Sheet 9). Without surveyed conductor routing and exact clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to all buildings and site features within the easement, it cannot be definitively verified that customer facilities are not installed beneath or over distribution conductors (absolute prohibition per UCM § 1.10.3) or that 7.5-foot clearance is maintained for items within easements."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Code establishes absolute prohibition against installing customer facilities (buildings, driveways, structures) under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution facilities, independent of clearance distances. Plans show driveways crossing under southern overhead line and buildings near overhead facilities. No explicit documentation confirms facilities are not placed directly beneath/over conductors. Cannot confirm compliance with absolute prohibition."}]},{"text":"Building finished floor elevations (686.25–685 ft MSL) shown; overhead conductor elevations unknown. Without surveyed conductor heights and building roof elevations, vertical clearances cannot be verified and appear marginal. Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey and site-specific analysis required but not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.31","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span conductor clearances is provided on any submitted sheet. The existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows surveyed pole locations, but no conductor elevation data. When overhead facilities cross proposed site features (buildings, driveways, parking), surveyed mid-span clearance measurements are required to verify vertical clearances meet minimum requirements. These measurements are absent from the plan set."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Building finished floor elevations range 686.25-685 ft MSL; overhead conductor elevations unknown. Without surveyed conductor heights and building roof elevations, vertical clearances cannot be verified and appear marginal. Code requires registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey and site-specific analysis when vertical clearance requirements may not be met. This critical survey and analysis are not provided despite marginal clearance conditions."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing vertical clearance verification for driveways and transformer","summary":"Driveways are proposed to cross under overhead electric lines, and a transformer pad is shown near overhead distribution lines. No vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead conductors (including attachments) to finished driveway/parking grades or to the transformer pad are provided. Mid-span surveyed clearance heights and determination of truck-traffic applicability are absent, preventing verification of minimum 15-foot (transformer radial) or 16/18-foot (driveway vertical) clearance requirements per UCM § 1.10.3 and § 1.10.6.2.","sheets":[4,9,11,21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordination with Austin Energy required for registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey; may necessitate grading adjustments, driveway rerouting, or conductor relocation.","attn":"Clarify whether any internal driveways will accommodate truck traffic (garbage collection, emergency response, delivery, etc.). This determines minimum clearance requirement (16-foot vs. 18-foot).","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad shown near overhead distribution lines on property boundaries. No clearance dimensions from outside conductor provided. Required 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor in all directions cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.2","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad is shown on the site plan with overhead electric distribution lines on property boundaries, but no clearance dimensions from the outside conductor are provided. The required 15-foot radial clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors cannot be verified from the available plans."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Distribution overhead conductors shown on existing conditions survey (Sheet 4); buildings and facilities proposed throughout site (Sheets 9, 21). Without surveyed conductor locations and radial clearance dimensions, the 15-foot radial clearance from outside conductor in all directions cannot be verified. No profile drawings show radial clearance envelopes."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Overhead electric line documented on southern boundary. Building locations shown but no clearance dimensions provided. Cannot verify 15-foot radial clearance without dimension callouts, conductor identification (primary/secondary/neutral), and voltage specifications."}]},{"text":"Internal driveways and parking areas proposed crossing under overhead electric line on southern boundary. No vertical clearance dimensions from lowest conductor (including attachments) to finished grades provided. Truck-traffic determination (16-foot vs. 18-foot minimum) not made. Registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey not provided.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.6.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.18","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Internal driveways and parking areas are proposed (Sheets 9, 11). Overhead utility lines exist on property boundaries (Sheet 4). No vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead conductors (including any attachments) to finished driveway/parking grades are provided. Verification of 16-foot minimum (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (areas with truck traffic) clearance requires surveyed conductor elevation data and grading section exhibits not provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Site plan shows proposed driveways crossing under overhead electric line on southern boundary. No vertical clearance dimensions provided on grading plan, profile sections, or utility plan. No determination whether truck traffic applies (16-foot vs. 18-foot requirement). No registered surveyor mid-span clearance survey data provided. Cannot verify driveways maintain minimum vertical clearance from lowest point of overhead facilities including any telecommunications attachments."}]}]},{"headline":"Proposed trees lack utility-compatible species designation","summary":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees planted within 10–15 feet of overhead distribution conductor on southern property boundary. Code requires trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors be Utility Compatible species (ECM Appendix F, typically mature height ≤ 20 feet, marked UC). Specific species of proposed mitigation trees are not confirmed on landscape plan, preventing verification that non-compatible species will not be planted. Non-compatible species will grow into overhead conductors, creating safety hazard.","sheets":[31,35],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":3,"crossDep":"Coordination with City Arborist and Austin Energy recommended to finalize tree species selection and confirm utility-compatible designations.","attn":"Provide a marked-up landscape plan identifying specific species for each tree location, cross-referenced to the plant schedule. Include ECM Appendix F utility-compatible verification for all trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead conductors.","details":[{"text":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows mitigation trees (M symbols) planted 10–15 feet from southern overhead line. Landscape calculations (Sheet 35) list species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but species-to-location cross-reference cannot be made. Without confirmed species identification, utility-compatible status (per ECM Appendix F) cannot be verified for trees within required 10-foot buffer.","citation":"ECM § 2.4.1.D; ECM § 2.4.2.C; UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"1:EL-1.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') planted within close proximity to overhead electric line on southern property boundary (approximately 4 trees in southeast corner area). The specific species of these mitigation trees are not identified on the landscape plan, making it impossible to verify whether they are utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors or 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors must be from the Utility Compatible list. Provide plant schedule identifying each mitigation tree species and verify compliance with utility-compatible requirements."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"The landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows proposed trees (marked M for Mitigation and PL for Parking Lot types) positioned within approximately 10-15 feet of the overhead electric line on the southern property boundary. The landscape calculations (Sheet 35) provide a plant list (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel), but the specific tree species cannot be cross-referenced to the landscape plan location symbols. Without confirmed species identification for the trees near the overhead line, utility-compatible status cannot be verified against ECM Appendix F. Trees within 10 lateral feet of distribution conductors must be utility-compatible species (generally mature height ≤20 feet marked UC)."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) depicts proposed mitigation trees approximately 10-15 feet from southern overhead electric line. Code requires trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors be Utility Compatible species per ECM Appendix F (UC designation, generally mature height ≤20 feet). Specific tree species not confirmed on landscape plan. Cannot verify proposed trees are utility-compatible; if non-compatible species are planted, they will grow into overhead conductors, creating safety hazard."}]}]},{"headline":"Utility pole locations, guy wires, and associated clearances undocumented","summary":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) documents utility poles on northern and southern property boundaries. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) omits pole locations with no notation of removal, relocation, or retention. No down guy wires, anchor locations, or associated clearances are shown. Proposed site features (fences, retaining walls, driveways, sidewalks) do not show clearance dimensions to pole locations. Down guy anchor easements required for distribution poles are not depicted on easement exhibits. Cannot verify that pole-related infrastructure conflicts are addressed or that clearances to poles and guy anchors are maintained.","sheets":[2,4,9,31,38,39],"applicableArea":"Site-wide","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Coordination with Austin Energy required to confirm pole retention, relocation, or removal; verify down guy locations, anchor easement requirements, and clearance zones for all proposed site features.","attn":"Contact Austin Energy directly to obtain registered surveyor documentation of pole locations, guy wire routing, anchor locations, and any required easements. Confirm whether northern boundary pole (Sheet 4) is on-site or off-site, and design intent (retain or relocate). Re-verify all clearances after pole status is confirmed.","details":[{"text":"Fences proposed throughout property perimeter near existing utility poles (Sheet 4). Exact measured distances between proposed fence post locations and pole locations not provided. Cannot verify 10-foot minimum horizontal clearance to poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.10","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Fences are proposed (noted on landscape plan Sheet 31 and landscape calculations Sheet 35), including wooden privacy fences. Existing utility poles are shown on the existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) at multiple property boundaries. Without exact measured distances between proposed fence post locations and existing pole locations, the 10-foot minimum horizontal clearance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Retaining walls detailed on Sheets 38–39 throughout site perimeter. Overhead electric facilities on property boundaries. No dimension lines or clearance annotations show distances from outside conductor to wall faces. Horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified without surveyor data and section exhibits.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"1:EL-1.14","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Retaining walls are detailed on Sheets 38-39, and overhead electric facilities exist on property boundaries (Sheet 4). However, no dimension lines or clearance annotations show distances from the outside conductor to the outermost edge of any retaining wall. Horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from conductors to wall faces cannot be verified without surveyor data and section exhibits."}]},{"text":"Existing survey shows utility pole on northern property boundary. Proposed plan omits pole location with no notation regarding relocation, removal, or retention. If pole remains and site improvements (driveway, building, etc.) within 30 feet, pole relocation to minimum 30 feet from driveway edge required. Current plan does not address pole conflicts.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.22","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) documents overhead utility pole on-site along northern property boundary. Proposed site plan (Sheet 9) omits this pole location with no notation regarding relocation, removal, or disposition. If pole remains and any site improvements (driveway, building, etc.) are within 30 feet of pole, relocation to minimum 30 feet from driveway edge is required. Current plan does not address pole conflicts."}]},{"text":"Public sidewalk proposed along Valley View Road frontage (Sheet 9) near existing utility poles shown on Sheet 4 (western property line, right-of-way). Exact clearance distances from sidewalk to pole locations at each property end not dimensioned. Cannot verify sidewalk setback from poles.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.25","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Existing utility poles are shown on Sheet 4 along the western property line within right-of-way. A public sidewalk is proposed along Valley View Road frontage (Sheet 9). Without dimensioned drawings showing exact clearance distances from sidewalk location to pole positions at each property end along right-of-way, the requirement cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Existing survey shows utility poles on northern and southern boundaries. Down guy wires and anchor locations typically omitted from plans but are critical infrastructure. Site plan shows no down guys, anchors, or clearances. If poles have down guys (common for distribution poles) and site improvements (driveways, accessible paths, buildings) near pole bases, guy anchors and cables could conflict. Verification from Austin Energy and survey documentation required.","citation":"UCM § 1.17.0","sourceId":"1:EL-1.40","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Existing conditions survey (Sheet 4) shows utility poles on northern and southern property boundaries. Down guy wires and anchor locations are typically omitted from plans but are critical infrastructure. Site plan does not show any down guy wires, anchors, or associated clearances. If poles have down guys (common for distribution poles) and site improvements (driveways, accessible paths, buildings) are located near pole bases, guy anchors and cables could conflict with these features. Requires verification from Austin Energy and survey documentation."}]},{"text":"Easement exhibit (Sheet 2) and site plan do not show down guy anchor easements. Per Austin Energy standards, down guy anchors require dedicated 10-foot-wide easement extending minimum 5 feet past anchor ground entry point. If poles have down guys (typical), required easements must be depicted on plat and easement exhibits. Missing easement documentation.","citation":"Reviewer Convention","sourceId":"1:EL-1.42","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Easement exhibit (Sheet 2) and site plan do not show down guy anchor easements. Per Austin Energy transmission engineering standards, down guy anchors from distribution poles require dedicated 10-foot-wide easement extending minimum 5 feet past anchor ground entry point. If poles have down guys (typical for poles on property), required easements must be depicted on plat and easement exhibits. Missing easement documentation represents deficiency."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing construction safety notifications and staging area clearances","summary":"Plans do not include required notice that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before any work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. No construction logistics or staging plan is provided documenting equipment laydown zones, work platforms, or crane operation areas maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2. These construction-phase requirements are separate from permanent clearances and must be addressed in plan notes and construction administration protocols.","sheets":[1,3,9],"applicableArea":"Plan Documentation","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Coordination with Safety/Construction Administration to finalize construction notification language and staging area logistics. Austin Energy and electrical contractor sign-off may be required.","attn":"Add explicit note to cover sheet or Sheet 3 (General Notes) stating: 'Owner/Contractor must notify Austin Energy at minimum 48 hours before any work begins near high-voltage overhead electric lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003.' Additionally, require construction staging plan or logistics exhibit showing equipment laydown zones and work platforms maintain 10-foot radial clearance from all energized overhead lines.","details":[{"text":"No construction logistics, staging plan, or equipment operation zones provided on site plans. Construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms must maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2. Mandatory separate requirement from permanent clearances. Plans must include logistics plan or note addressing construction phase clearances.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.45","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"No construction logistics, staging plan, or equipment operation zones provided on site plans. Code requires construction staging areas, equipment laydown zones, and work platforms maintain minimum 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead electric lines per OSHA 1910.333 and UCM § 1.10.2. This is mandatory separate requirement from permanent clearances. Plans must include logistics plan or note addressing construction phase clearances from overhead lines."}]},{"text":"Cover sheet (Sheet 1) and general notes (Sheet 3) do not include required notification that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before any work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. Sheet 3 includes pre-construction safety meeting requirement for transmission facilities but no general contractor notification note for all overhead electric facilities (distribution and transmission).","citation":"UCM § 1.10.2","sourceId":"1:EL-1.46","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Sheet 3 includes a pre-construction safety meeting requirement (48 hours before construction) for transmission facilities, but does not include a general contractor note requiring notification to Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. A comprehensive 48-hour notification note applicable to all overhead electric facilities (both distribution and transmission) is required on the cover sheet or general notes."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Cover sheet and general notes do not include required notification regarding high-voltage work. Code requires plans to include note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before any work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. This safety notification is mandatory when overhead electric facilities exist on or adjacent to site and construction is proposed."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"46f08130-b53a-43a1-9321-cde21a22ea0e"}
