{"level":30,"time":1777033401591,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"2.json","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TJZMnpesVcjZ7XyWntqi8G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! I've successfully synthesized the 12 input findings into 4 well-structured review comments using the StructuredOutput tool. Let me verify my work:\n\n1. **Consolidation**: 12 findings → 4 comments = 3:1 ratio ✓\n2. **Coverage**: Every sourceId accounted for:\n   - Comment 1: 2:EL-2.1, 2:EL-2.3, 2:EL-2.15 (3 findings)\n   - Comment 2: 2:EL-2.6, 2:EL-2.7 (2 findings)\n   - Comment 3: 2:EL-2.8, 2:EL-2.9 (2 findings)\n   - Comment 4: 2:EL-2.10, 2:EL-2.11, 2:EL-2.14, 2:EL-2.12, 2:EL-2.13 (5 findings)\n   Total: 12 ✓\n\n3. **No Tier 3 exclusions**: All findings are within electrical utility scope ✓\n\n4. **Detail preservation**:\n   - All specific measurements preserved (0-6 feet, 1.7 feet, 8.5 feet, 90 ft, 60 ft, etc.)\n   - All species names preserved (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel)\n   - All sheet references included\n   - All code citations present\n   - All per-run comments copied verbatim ✓\n\n5. **No repetition across levels**:\n   - Headlines are standalone (3-12 words)\n   - Summaries frame the issue without restating details\n   - Details add specific findings not restated in summary ✓\n\n6. **Appropriate severity**:\n   - Comments 1 and 2 assigned severity 3 (High) since they represent actual violations on major and utility infrastructure\n   - Comments 3 and 4 assigned severity 2 (Medium) for verification gaps and documentation issues ✓\n\n7. **Appropriate confidence**:\n   - Comment 1 confidence set to 3 (caught across 2-3 runs)\n   - Comment 2 confidence set to 2 (identified in 2 runs)\n   - Comment 3 confidence set to 1 (single-run finding)\n   - Comment 4 confidence reflects mixed run detection patterns ✓\n\n8. **Cross-department notes**: Included references to Austin Energy for Comments 2 and 3 ✓\n\n9. **Attention flags**: Flagged Comments 3 and 4 due to low confidence and unverifiable elements ✓\n\nAll findings have been organized, deduplicated, and mapped to the required schema structure.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19929,"cache_read_input_tokens":28977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19929,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6873508e-e3d9-457d-859a-f8828951895f","uuid":"5e6122b1-4b52-4fa7-a810-d5d7b9381d02"}
{"level":30,"time":1777033403174,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"2.json","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01TJZMnpesVcjZ7XyWntqi8G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Synthesis complete.** I've consolidated your 12 electrical utility findings into **4 actionable review comments** using the simplified schema.\n\n## Summary of Consolidation\n\n| Comment | Findings | Focus | Severity |\n|---------|----------|-------|----------|\n| Overhead distribution trees violate clearance distances | EL-2.1, 2.3, 2.15 | Large trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) 0–6 feet from overhead conductors; missing Austin Energy approval | **High (3)** |\n| Trees violate clearance from utility poles and transformer pads | EL-2.6, 2.7 | Measured violations: 8.5 feet from poles, 1.7 feet from transformer; infrastructure not labeled | **High (3)** |\n| Underground electrical equipment clearances not verified | EL-2.8, 2.9 | Underground equipment not shown on landscape plan; 5-foot and 20-foot clearances + root barriers unverified | **Medium (2)** |\n| Landscape plan lacks species labels and clearance dimensions | EL-2.10, 2.11, 2.12, 2.13, 2.14 | Missing species IDs, mature height notations, dimension lines, cross-references, and measurement methodology notes | **Medium (2)** |\n\n**All 12 input findings preserved** with exact measurements, species names, sheet references, and per-run comments carried through to `runComments` arrays for traceability. No information dropped or lost."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19929,"cache_read_input_tokens":28977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19929,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id