{"level":30,"time":1777033414480,"pid":122,"hostname":"7e1d7a35-fad","step":"synthesize-comments","item":"13.json","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HoVEUDveZsLspeLMhdr9LE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018NQykSFqW5nuFpKdrv6zVA","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"comments":[{"headline":"Missing AE Design approvals and easement documentation","summary":"Required Austin Energy Design approvals, transformer easements, and recorded easement depictions are not provided. Compliance with AE Design standards and verification that pads avoid conflict with existing utility easements cannot be confirmed.","sheets":[9,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Austin Energy Design and Legal/Real Estate — new transformer easements require AE coordination and legal review; recorded easement compliance requires property records verification.","attn":"Verify recorded easement locations per facts.md. Two critical unrecorded easements affect NE portion of site: Greenbelt Access & Use (0.31 acres) and City of Austin Drainage (0.130 acres).","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled on electrical plan and no AE Design-approved detail sheets are provided. Pad dimensions must match AE Design-approved specifications for specified service type (single/three-phase) and equipment load.","citation":"UCM § 1.5.2.6; UCM § 1.18.0","sourceId":"13:EL-13.37","confidence":3,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not shown on the submitted electrical plan. No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets (which specify pad dimensions based on service type and equipment specifications) are included in the site plan submission. Provide AE Design approval letter and transformer pad detail sheets confirming pad dimensions match the specifications for the proposed service type (single-phase or three-phase)."},{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not shown on the electrical plan, and no Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets have been provided or referenced. Pad dimensions must match AE Design-approved details for the specified service type (single-phase or three-phase) and equipment load."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad dimensions are not labeled or dimensioned on the electrical plan. No reference callouts to Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided. Compliance with AE Design pad specifications for the specified service type cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Transformer easements for all five proposed pads are not depicted on any plan sheet. Easement boundaries and widths required to accommodate Austin Energy accessibility and maintenance operations are not specified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.35","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"No transformer easements are depicted on the electrical plan, site plan, or easement exhibits. Transformer easements are required around all five proposed transformer pads to provide adequate access for Austin Energy Design operations and maintenance, and the required easement widths have not been specified."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer easements are not shown on any of the site plan sheets. No easement boundaries or widths are depicted around the transformer pads to accommodate Austin Energy accessibility and maintenance requirements."}]},{"text":"Transformer pad southeast of Buildings 6–7 is 5.2 feet from Building 7 wall, at the minimum threshold. If reduced clearance below 5 feet is proposed, AE Design written approval and verification of required conditions (not in confined space, adequate window/door/duct clearance, 3-hour fire rating) must be documented.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.4","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad between Buildings 6 and 7 is located at 5.2 feet from Building 7 wall (at the 5-foot minimum threshold). If this clearance is claimed as reduced clearance (less than 5 feet to brick/masonry), documentation of Austin Energy Design written approval and verification of required conditions (not in confined space, adequate window/door/duct clearance, 3-hour fire rating) must be provided. Cannot verify clearance compliance status from available documents."}]},{"text":"Two critical recorded easements not depicted on site plan: Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731, 0.31 acres NE interior) and City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137, 0.130 acres NE corner). Transformer pad locations relative to these and all recorded utility easements cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.34","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"According to facts.md, two critical easements are recorded but NOT depicted on the submitted site plan: (1) Greenbelt Access & Use Easement (Instrument 2010070731) covering 0.31 acres in NE interior, and (2) City of Austin Drainage Easement (Instrument 2011021137) covering 0.130 acres in NE corner. Specific confirmation that all five transformer pads are located outside drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, and electrical easements under overhead lines cannot be verified without proper easement depiction on plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing building elevation documentation for clearance verification","summary":"Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations, heights from grade, and lateral distances to transformer pads are not provided. Cannot verify 12-foot horizontal clearance and 5-foot lateral separation requirements.","sheets":[21],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Architect — Building elevations must show window, door, and duct locations with heights and lateral distances from transformer pads.","attn":"Architect must provide elevation drawings with dimensioned window/door/duct locations and heights. Verify compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance (when openings are within 12 feet of grade) and 5-foot lateral separation requirements.","details":[{"text":"Adjacent multi-story residential buildings (1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8) lack elevation documentation showing window, door, and duct heights and lateral separations from transformer pads. Compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance and 5-foot lateral separation cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.6","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are adjacent to multi-story residential buildings (Buildings 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, and 8). Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations, heights from grade, and lateral separation distances relative to transformer pads are not provided. Cannot verify compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement when windows/doors are less than 12 feet from grade or have less than 5-foot lateral separation."}]}]},{"headline":"Inadequate clearances from transformer pads to utility infrastructure","summary":"Transformer pads lack documented minimum clearances to water, wastewater, storm drain, and other underground utilities. Some pads violate the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance requirement. Cross-sections showing vertical utility relationships are not provided.","sheets":[11,19,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Utility Departments (Water, Wastewater, Stormwater) — Clearance conflicts may require utility line relocation or pad relocation, requiring coordination with utility providers.","attn":"Run 1 findings indicate confirmed clearance violations (Pads 2 and 3 to water line; Pads 1 and 2 to wastewater line). Verify current utility routing and pad coordinates; confirm corrective action in revised plans.","details":[{"text":"Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 0.9 feet from nearest water line; Pad 3 (southwest area near Building 8) has zero clearance/overlaps water line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required. Dimensioned clearances must be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.21","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is located only 0.9 feet from the nearest water line; Transformer Pad 3 (southwest area near Building 8) has zero clearance/overlaps with the water line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required. Relocate pads or reroute water lines to achieve required clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water utility lines are shown on utility and electrical plans but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between water lines and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to water infrastructure."}]},{"text":"Transformer Pad 1 (northwest entrance near Building 1) is 4.6 feet from wastewater line; Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 2.5 feet from wastewater line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from all sides. Dimensioned clearances must be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer Pad 1 (northwest entrance area near Building 1) is located 4.6 feet from the nearest wastewater line; Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 2.5 feet from wastewater line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from all sides. Relocate pads or reroute wastewater lines to achieve required clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wastewater utility lines are shown on utility and electrical plans but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between wastewater lines and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater infrastructure."}]},{"text":"Storm drain infrastructure routing relative to transformer pads lacks dimensioned clearance markings. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.23","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on site plan but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between storm drain infrastructure and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines."}]},{"text":"Specific dimensioned clearances between transformer pads and multiple underground utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) are not marked on any plan. Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from pads to other utilities cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.25","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown on site (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) but specific dimensioned clearances between transformer pads and other underground utilities are not marked on any plan. Cannot verify minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities."}]},{"text":"Cross-section or profile drawings showing vertical clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead structures, parking garages, and enclosed areas are not provided. Vertical clearance compliance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.31","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are located within site development area with buildings and structures in close