d or dry-type. If oil-filled, grading plan must show surface drainage flow direction at pad locations with slope percentages and 20-foot clearance from fire escapes.","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad access door orientation is not indicated on electrical plan. Required 10-foot minimum clearance to open area for hot-stick use cannot be verified. South pad is 5.9 feet from Building 7; if access door faces this building, 10-foot requirement would not be met.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.10","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan does not identify transformer access door orientation or show the hot-stick use area boundary (minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure required). Cannot verify whether the access door sides of all five transformer pads have adequate clearance to open area or confirm hot-stick use area compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad access door orientation is not indicated on the electrical plan. Without door orientation, the required 10-foot minimum clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure cannot be verified. The south pad is 5.9 feet from Building 7; if the access door faces this building, the 10-foot requirement would not be met."}]},{"text":"Transformer specifications do not indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan does not show surface drainage flow direction around pads. For oil-filled transformers, verification that drainage slopes direct liquid flow away from buildings cannot be confirmed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.9","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer specifications do not indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan does not show surface drainage flow direction around transformer pads. If oil-filled transformers are proposed, verification that surface drainage and grading 