electrical easements under overhead lines cannot be verified without proper easement depiction on plans."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing building elevation documentation for clearance verification","summary":"Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations, heights from grade, and lateral distances to transformer pads are not provided. Cannot verify 12-foot horizontal clearance and 5-foot lateral separation requirements.","sheets":[21],"applicableArea":"Building Envelope","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Architect — Building elevations must show window, door, and duct locations with heights and lateral distances from transformer pads.","attn":"Architect must provide elevation drawings with dimensioned window/door/duct locations and heights. Verify compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance (when openings are within 12 feet of grade) and 5-foot lateral separation requirements.","details":[{"text":"Adjacent multi-story residential buildings (1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 8) lack elevation documentation showing window, door, and duct heights and lateral separations from transformer pads. Compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance and 5-foot lateral separation cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.6","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are adjacent to multi-story residential buildings (Buildings 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, and 8). Building elevation drawings showing window, door, and ventilating duct locations, heights from grade, and lateral separation distances relative to transformer pads are not provided. Cannot verify compliance with 12-foot horizontal clearance requirement when windows/doors are less than 12 feet from grade or have less than 5-foot lateral separation."}]}]},{"headline":"Inadequate clearances from transformer pads to utility infrastructure","summary":"Transformer pads lack documented minimum clearances to water, wastewater, storm drain, and other underground utilities. Some pads violate the 5-foot minimum horizontal clearance requirement. Cross-sections showing vertical utility relationships are not provided.","sheets":[11,19,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Utility Departments (Water, Wastewater, Stormwater) — Clearance conflicts may require utility line relocation or pad relocation, requiring coordination with utility providers.","attn":"Run 1 findings indicate confirmed clearance violations (Pads 2 and 3 to water line; Pads 1 and 2 to wastewater line). Verify current utility routing and pad coordinates; confirm corrective action in revised plans.","details":[{"text":"Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 0.9 feet from nearest water line; Pad 3 (southwest area near Building 8) has zero clearance/overlaps water line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required. Dimensioned clearances must be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.21","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is located only 0.9 feet from the nearest water line; Transformer Pad 3 (southwest area near Building 8) has zero clearance/overlaps with the water line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required. Relocate pads or reroute water lines to achieve required clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Water utility lines are shown on utility and electrical plans but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between water lines and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to water infrastructure."}]},{"text":"Transformer Pad 1 (northwest entrance near Building 1) is 4.6 feet from wastewater line; Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 2.5 feet from wastewater line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from all sides. Dimensioned clearances must be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.22","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":1,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer Pad 1 (northwest entrance area near Building 1) is located 4.6 feet from the nearest wastewater line; Transformer Pad 2 (mid-western side yard near Building 2) is 2.5 feet from wastewater line. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from all sides. Relocate pads or reroute wastewater lines to achieve required clearance."},{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Wastewater utility lines are shown on utility and electrical plans but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between wastewater lines and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to wastewater infrastructure."}]},{"text":"Storm drain infrastructure routing relative to transformer pads lacks dimensioned clearance markings. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 2.9.1.B.2","sourceId":"13:EL-13.23","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Storm drain lines are shown on site plan but no specific dimensioned clearances are marked between storm drain infrastructure and transformer pad locations. Cannot verify minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance from transformer pads to storm drain lines."}]},{"text":"Specific dimensioned clearances between transformer pads and multiple underground utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) are not marked on any plan. Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from pads to other utilities cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.A","sourceId":"13:EL-13.25","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown on site (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric) but specific dimensioned clearances between transformer pads and other underground utilities are not marked on any plan. Cannot verify minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance from transformer pads to other underground utilities."}]},{"text":"Cross-section or profile drawings showing vertical clearances from transformer pad locations to overhead structures, parking garages, and enclosed areas are not provided. Vertical clearance compliance cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.3","sourceId":"13:EL-13.31","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pads are located within site development area with buildings and structures in close proximity. No cross-section or profile drawings are provided showing vertical clearances from transformer pad locations to any overhead structures, parking structures, or enclosed areas. Cannot verify vertical clearance compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths or demonstrating clearances to any overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas associated with transformer locations. Vertical clearance compliance cannot be verified."}]},{"text":"Profile or cross-section drawings showing vertical relationships between transformer pads and utility lines are not provided. Confirmation that pads and Austin Energy underground facilities are not located over/under other utility lines cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.5.B","sourceId":"13:EL-13.26","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Plans show multiple utility lines crossing throughout the site. Profile or cross-section drawings showing vertical relationships between transformer pads and utility lines are not provided. Cannot confirm that transformer pads or Austin Energy underground facilities are not located over or under other utility lines, and that customer buildings/foundations/structures are not installed over Austin Energy underground facilities."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing transformer equipment specifications and pad drainage documentation","summary":"Transformer specifications do not identify equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type). Grading plan does not show surface drainage flow direction at transformer pad locations. Operational compliance cannot be verified.","sheets":[11,21],"applicableArea":"Utilities & Infrastructure","severity":2,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"Electrical Engineer and Civil Engineer (Grading) — Equipment type specification and drainage slope direction require coordination.","attn":"Transformer equipment specifications must clearly identify whether oil-filled or dry-type. If oil-filled, grading plan must show surface drainage flow direction at pad locations with slope percentages and 20-foot clearance from fire escapes.","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad access door orientation is not indicated on electrical plan. Required 10-foot minimum clearance to open area for hot-stick use cannot be verified. South pad is 5.9 feet from Building 7; if access door faces this building, 10-foot requirement would not be met.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.10","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Electrical plan does not identify transformer access door orientation or show the hot-stick use area boundary (minimum 10-foot clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure required). Cannot verify whether the access door sides of all five transformer pads have adequate clearance to open area or confirm hot-stick use area compliance."},{"runNum":3,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer pad access door orientation is not indicated on the electrical plan. Without door orientation, the required 10-foot minimum clearance to open area or adjacent building/structure cannot be verified. The south pad is 5.9 feet from Building 7; if the access door faces this building, the 10-foot requirement would not be met."}]},{"text":"Transformer specifications do not indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan does not show surface drainage flow direction around pads. For oil-filled transformers, verification that drainage slopes direct liquid flow away from buildings cannot be confirmed.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.9","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer specifications do not indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan does not show surface drainage flow direction around transformer pads. If oil-filled transformers are proposed, verification that surface drainage and grading slopes direct liquid flow away from buildings (minimum 20-foot horizontal clearance from fire escapes also required) cannot be confirmed from available plans."}]},{"text":"Equipment type specification (oil-filled or dry-type) is missing from transformer data. Grading plan shows general site drainage but does not mark drainage flow direction specifically at pad locations. Surface drainage slope away from buildings cannot be verified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1","sourceId":"13:EL-13.32","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Transformer specifications do not identify whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading plan shows general site drainage but does not mark drainage flow direction specifically at transformer pad locations. Cannot verify that surface drainage slopes direct liquid flow away from buildings (required for oil-filled transformers per UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1)."}]}]},{"headline":"Missing bollard protection for vehicle-proximate transformer pads","summary":"Two transformer pads are located within 4 feet of vehicle circulation routes. Equipment within 4 feet of parking areas requires 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized bollards per AE Design standards. No bollards are shown or specified.","sheets":[21],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":3,"confidence":2,"crossDep":"","attn":"","details":[{"text":"Transformer pad between Buildings 4–5 is 4.1 feet from central drive aisle. Transformer pad south of Building 7 is 3.2 feet from nearest vehicle circulation route. Both within 4-foot threshold requiring 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post bollards. No bollards shown or specified.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.38","confidence":2,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"fail","comment":"Transformer pad located between Buildings 4 and 5 is positioned 4.1 feet from the central drive aisle (vehicle route). Equipment installed within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle circulation routes requires 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal post bollards per AE Design pad details. No bollards are shown or noted on the electrical plan or detail sheets, and no bollard specifications or locations are provided."},{"runNum":3,"status":"fail","comment":"The transformer pad in the south area (near Building 7) is located 3.2 feet from the nearest vehicle circulation route, which is within the 4-foot threshold requiring bollard protection. No 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized bollards are shown on the electrical plan or any detail sheets. Bollards are required per AE Design equipment pad specifications."}]}]},{"headline":"Incomplete landscape documentation for transformer pad protection","summary":"Landscape plan does not identify tree species or confirm utility-compatibility per ECM Appendix F. Clearances from shrubs and low-lying vegetation are not dimensioned. Root barrier details are not shown for trees within 20 feet of transformer pads.","sheets":[31,32],"applicableArea":"Site Interior","severity":2,"confidence":1,"crossDep":"Landscape Architect — Landscape plan must specify tree species, clearances from pad edges, and root barrier installation details.","attn":"Landscape plan must identify all tree species and confirm utility-compatibility per ECM Appendix F. Verify 10-foot clearance from access door side, 5-foot from other sides. Provide 4-foot deep root barrier details 5 feet from pads for trees within 20 feet.","details":[{"text":"Trees shown in landscape plan near transformer pad locations lack species identification. Utility-compatible category confirmation per ECM Appendix F not provided. Cannot verify that trees within 10–15 lateral feet of equipment meet compatibility requirements.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4; ECM Appendix F","sourceId":"13:EL-13.13","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows trees in the vicinity of transformer pad locations. Tree species identification and cross-reference with ECM Appendix F utility-compatible category confirmation not provided. Cannot verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of any overhead distribution conductors are utility-compatible species."}]},{"text":"Landscape plan shows vegetation and planting areas but lacks dimensioned clearances from transformer pad edges. Transformer access door orientation not identified on electrical plan. Cannot verify 10-foot clearance from access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.14","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Landscape plan shows vegetation and planting areas but does not show dimensioned clearances from transformer pad edges. Transformer access door orientation is not identified on electrical plan. Cannot verify 10-foot clearance from access door side and 5-foot clearance from other sides of shrubs and low-lying vegetation."}]},{"text":"Root barrier details are not shown on landscape plan or detail sheets. Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads require 4-foot deep root barriers installed 5 feet from equipment. Landscape plan provides no root barrier specifications or installation confirmation.","citation":"UCM § 1.10.10.4","sourceId":"13:EL-13.15","confidence":1,"runComments":[{"runNum":2,"status":"nv","comment":"Root barrier details are not shown on landscape plan or detail sheets. Trees within 20 lateral feet of transformer pads (part of underground electric infrastructure) require root barriers 4 feet deep installed 5 feet from equipment. Landscape plan does not provide root barrier specifications, installation details, or confirmation that root barriers will be installed around trees near transformer pad locations."}]}]}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"90c9c0e3-8737-4bbc-9980-066c33876984"}
